    "description": "Appointment to the post of Director General of the Department of Census and Statistics",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13393",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mrs. D.D.G.A. Seneviratne, who is presently serving as Director General of the Department of Census and Statistics is due to retire from the Public Service with effect from 2025-09-05 upon completion of the age of 60 years. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, to appoint Mrs. K.M.D.S.D. Karunaratne, the most senior Additional Director General of the Department of Census and Statistics to the post of Director General of that Department falling vacant, with effect from the said date, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Amendment of the fines relating to offences under the Employment of Women, Young Persons and Children Act, No.47 of 1956",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13392",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Employment of Women, Young Persons and Children Act, No.47 of 1956, completely prohibits the employment of children below the age of 16 years and in accordance with the provisions of the said Act, regulations have been imposed to be followed by employers regarding the employment of young persons above the age of 16 but below the age of 18. According to the relevant Act and the regulations issued in accordance with the provisions of the said Act, it is a punishable offence to employ children and young persons of the relevant age group in hazardous occupation that may be detrimental to health, safety and morals. The Amendment made to the said Act in the year 2003 has introduced provisions to impose a fine not exceeding Rs.10,000/- or imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or both such fine and imprisonment and also to order compensation to the prejudicated child at the discretion of the Court, on a person found guilty under the provision of the said Act. However, it has been observed that the amount of the relevant fine is inadequate. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour to update and revise the minimum fines mentioned in sections 7(3), 13(2) and 20(a)(3) of the Employment of Women, Young Persons and Children Act, No.47, 1956, complying with the Convention No. 138 and 182 of the International Labour Organization which have been ratified by Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Amendment of Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing (Incorporation) Act, No.41 of 1980",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13391",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing has been incorporated by the Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing (Incorporation) Act, No.41 of 1980 and promotes marketing education by maintaining strong partnerships with the country's leading higher education institutions/universities including the Wayamba University of Sri Lanka, the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka and the Rajarata University of Sri Lanka. The Institute annually provides education to nearly 8,000 students with marketing and entrepreneurship professional qualifications and leading companies in the country obtain the services of the Institute to provide marketing training to their employees. It has been identified that the provisions of the Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing (Incorporation) Act, No.41 of 1980 should be amended to further expand the services provided by the Institute and enable it to perform more efficiently. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development to amend the said Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Rehabilitation and Modernization of the Sri Lanka Planetarium",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13390",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Planetarium has been designed by Dr. A.N.S. Kulasinghe and constructed as a major component of the Industrial Exhibition held in the year 1965. As the deterioration of the structure of the building and the obsolescence of its physical facilities and technical infrastructure are currently being observed, the need to modernize it while preserving its unique architectural features has been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Science and Technology to assign the relevant task to the National Engineering Research and Development Centre (NERD), a premier state institution with expertise in prestressed concrete technology, based on the concurrence given by the National Procurement Commission, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Expeditiously completing the Project for renovation and conservation of the National Art Gallery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13389",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Activities of the Project for renovation and conservation of the National Art Gallery are being carried out by the Sri Lanka Navy and approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201102\u201119 to complete all the activities of the project within the year 2024 itself. Nevertheless, it has not been possible to fully complete the work in the last year and a financial provision of Rs.120 million has been allocated for the same under the budget estimates for the year 2025. However, it has now been identified that the said provisions are not sufficient to fully complete the work of the project and that an additional financial provision of Rs.32 million is required. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs for securing additional budgetary provisions to complete the renovation work of the National Art Gallery expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Conducting inquiries into complaints made with regard to missing persons",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13388",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Office on Missing Persons has been established under the provisions of the Office on Missing Persons (Establishment, Administration and Discharge of Functions) Act, No.14 of 2016. The Office is responsible for conducting investigations into missing and disappeared persons and issuing reports to their relatives. Out of the 16,966 complaints received by the said Office so far, 10,517 complaints are still pending for investigation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice and National Integration to implement a special project to complete the investigations and related duties by the end of 2027 in order to provide justice to the aggrieved parties and to appoint 25 panels comprising of 75 experts including retired Judges, Senior Administrative Officers, Lawyers and other qualified persons for the relevant task, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Removal of the concessions granted in purchasing houses from the 'Viyathpura' Housing Project by the Members of Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13387",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022\u201107\u201104 to provide 101 Housing Units from the Viyathpura Housing Complex constructed by the Urban Development Authority, for a period of one year on rent basis to the then Members of Parliament who lost their homes due to the unrest that arose in the country on 2022\u201105\u201109. Subsequently, those Members of Parliament have submitted requests to provide them with the opportunity to purchase those houses under a concessionary scheme. Accordingly, the Cabinet has granted its approval on 2024\u201107\u201115 to provide a single housing unit which is sold to general people for a minimum value of Rs.15.5 million and maximum value of Rs.22 million at a reduced minimum value of a housing unit to Rs.13.34 million and maximum value to Rs.18.21 million, to Members of Parliament under a concessional scheme, and initially charge 25% from the sale price and recover the remaining amount from them over a period of 15 years at an interest rate of 10% per annum. Twenty Nine (29) former Members of Parliament have deposited 25% of the sale price as of 2024\u201112\u201131 to purchase houses under the said scheme. However, due to this concessional scheme, the Urban Development Authority had to incur a loss of about Rs.92.126 million and has not been able to cover the costs incurred. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development, Construction and Housing to abolish the concessional scheme approved as referred to above with immediate effect and provide the opportunity for the 29 relevant Members of Parliament to purchase the said houses with the same method and prices applicable to the general public if they so agree, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Installation of Barricade Nets in selected perennial reservoirs to protect freshwater fish harvest",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13386",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Inland fisheries and aquaculture play a major role in providing nutritious food to the communities in rural areas. However, the washing away of fish during overflows of inland reservoirs and release of water through sluice gates has severely reduced the yield of freshwater fish. It has been identified that between 20,000 to 40,000 kilograms of fish are lost from a single freshwater reservoir per year prior to human consumption. It has been shown that washing away of mature fish leads to a decrease in fish population and the rapid depletion of future fish stocks due to the escape of sexually mature fish with breeding capacity. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources to implement a programme to install barricade nets in 250 selected perennial freshwater reservoirs within 02 years by the Sri Lanka National Aquaculture Development Authority in order to prevent the loss of freshwater fish harvest and to increase freshwater fish production, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Local assembly of a Light Train Set with three coaches",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13385",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Most of the trains currently in use are used for passenger transport in suburban areas and only a few rail buses are currently in operation to meet the transport needs of the rural community. However, practical problems have arisen in operating rail buses according to the existing train schedule. It has also been identified that it is not economically viable to deploy train sets used for operation in suburban areas to rural areas due to the lack of sufficient number of passengers. Therefore, it has been planned to introduce light train sets with three coaches for railway lines in areas such as Puttalam, Batticaloa and Mihintale which can be operated at the rural level, equipped with an electronic control system powered by a diesel engine mounted on the coaches and with other modern facilities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport, Highways, Ports and Civil Aviation to take necessary steps to locally assemble a light train set with three coaches with a capacity of about 200 - 240 passengers and sufficient cargo space to meet the transportation needs of the rural community, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Reconstruction Project of the Sluice Tower, Sluice Barrel and remaining parts of the Senanayake Samudraya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13384",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Senanayake Samudraya, which was vested in the public on 1953-08-28, provides irrigated water to about 120,000 acres of paddy fields and contributes to adding 20 Megawatts of electricity to the national grid. In 1992, cracks were first observed in the sluice tower and the sluice barrel connected to the main dam and in the structure of outer spill constructed outside the main dam. Over time, these cracks have been widening and spreading. Although, it has been identified that the relevant structures should be rebuilt in order to provide a permanent solution to this, it has not been possible to construct a new sluice structure so far due to reasons such as the high cost of construction, possibility of creating a major rice shortage in the country due to the inability of providing irrigated water to a large area of \u200b\u200bcultivation, consequent to the depletion of water in the reservoir for about 02 years, and the absence of adequate technical capacity. In order to mitigate the existing risk and the damage that may occur in the event of a disaster, it has been planned to maintain the total capacity of the reservoir at approximately 40% after releasing water for the Yala season 2025 and carry out the proposed construction. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation to select a suitable contractor for the relevant constructions by inviting International Competitive Bids, enabling to obtain the latest technological knowledge available in the world, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Establishment of the Customs Verification Centre at Kerawalapitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13383",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2025\u201103\u201117 to transfer a portion of land belonging to the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation to the Sri Lanka Customs for the establishment of the Customs Verification Centre in Kerawalapitiya, and a Committee has been appointed to determine the modality for the establishment of the said Customs Verification Centre. The said Committee has submitted its recommendations with appropriate criteria for selecting a more viable business modality. Accordingly, based on the recommendation of the said Committee, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development to follow the procedure for calling Expressions of Interest and Requests for Proposal to select a suitable Private Partner to implement the proposed Kerawalapitiya Customs Verification Centre project under a Hybrid Public-Private Partnership Model."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Establishment of Diplomatic relations with Antigua and Barbuda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13382",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to establish formal diplomatic relations with 13 countries in the Latin American and Caribbean region. Accordingly, required measures have already been taken by the Government of Sri Lanka as of now to establish diplomatic relations with the countries of the region, other than Antigua and Barbuda. The proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism to sign the Agreement on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Antigua and Barbuda, aiming to accrue mutual benefits by both countries and enhance existing friendly relations and cooperation in the political, socio-economic and cultural fields, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Closure of Non-Functioning State-Owned Enterprises",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13381",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Some State\u2011Owned Enterprises established long ago to achieve the objectives such as providing public services and promoting strategic economic activities have become inactive due to reasons such as continuation of those enterprises is not practical owing to the incompatibility of the objectives of their establishment with the present mandate and market requirements and financial underperformance. It has been identified as appropriate to liquidate and close down State-Owned Enterprises belonging to various categories such as Statutory Bodies, State Corporations and State-Owned Companies that do not make a meaningful contribution to the national economy or the public service delivery, instead of continuing to operate them as a burden to the Government. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, the approval of the Cabinet was granted to formally liquidate and close down 33 State-Owned Enterprises that are not-functioning at present, in 02 stages under the supervision of a special liquidation unit to be established under the said Ministry."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-03-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Admission of Students from Grade 2 to 11 except Grade 5 and 6 in Schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13380",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Maintenance of the number of students in a classroom, only within the approved limits is essential to implement the new proposed education reforms. Therefore, it has been identified that it would be appropriate to introduce a proper mechanism to provide the opportunity to admit students to intermediate grades other than Grades 5 and 6 in schools, while ensuring the right of all children in the country for education. Taking into account the said matters, it has been planned to issue new circular instructions to provide the opportunity to apply for the intermediate grades in other schools, so that priority is given to students genuinely need to be admitted to another school from the school they are currently studying, for various reasons. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in her capacity as the Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education to cancel the circular instructions\u00a0 issued so far pertaining to the admission of students from Grade 2 to Grade 11 other than Grade 5 and 6 in schools and issue new circular instructions for the same, taking into considerations the recommendations made by the Parliamentary Sub\u2011Committee appointed by the Advisory Committee of the\u00a0 Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
