    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-21 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government anticipates to achieve an economic growth rate over 5% of the real Gross Domestic Production (GDP) over the medium term. The Government has focused its attention on investment-friendly policy formulation, infrastructure development and export diversification to achieve sustainable economic growth and economic stability. However, since private investment has been at a low level over the past few decades and the Government investment is about 4%-5% of the GDP, it has been identified that promoting private sector investment is essential to achieve the targeted economic growth. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to establish the Cabinet Appointed Special Committee on Economic Management to oversee and facilitate policy discussions on economic development, ensuring efficiency and alignment with national economic objectives, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-21-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2025-04-21",
    "description": "Appointment to the Post of Commissioner General of the Department of Motor Traffic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13136",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-21 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mr. Nishantha Anuruddha Weerasinghe, Special Grade Officer of the Sri Lanka Administrative Service who is currently serving as the Commissioner General of Motor Traffic, has requested to be released from the duties of the post of Commissioner General of Motor Traffic, enabling him to serve in a post in another field in the Public Service. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport, Highways, Ports and Civil Aviation to attach                                   Mr. Nishantha Anuruddha Weerasinghe to the Ministry of Public Administration, Provincial Council and Local Government with immediate effect, enabling to be appointed to another suitable post and to appoint                            Mr. Kamal Amarasinghe, Special Grade Officer of the Sri Lanka Administrative Service who is presently serving as the Secretary, Ministry of Road, Transport, Housing and Construction, Industrial and Rural Development, North Western Province, to the Post of Commissioner General of Motor Traffic thus falling vacant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-21-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2025-04-21",
    "description": "Regulations under the provisions of the Anti-Corruption Act, No.9 of 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13135",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-21 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Anti-Corruption Act, No.9 of 2023, has been enacted to give effect to certain provisions of the United Nations Convention against Corruption and other internationally recognized norms, standards and best practices and to provide for the establishment of an independent Commission to detect and investigate allegations of bribery, corruption and offenses related to the declaration of assets and liabilities and associated offenses. The Minister shall make Regulations in consultation with the Commission, in respect of matters required by the Act to be prescribed or in respect of which Regulations are authorized to be made. Approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2025\u201103\u201117 to publish the Regulations so made in consultation with the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption, in the Government Gazette. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice and National Integration to submit the Anti-Corruption (Declaration of Assets and Liabilities) Regulations 2025 published through the Extraordinary Gazette Notification No.2428/43 dated 2025\u201103\u201120, for approval of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-21-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2025-04-21",
    "description": "Making provisions for the registration of electric motor tricycles (three-wheelers)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13134",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-21 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the use of rechargeable batteries in manufacturing motor tricycles (three\u2011 wheelers) powered by electricity and converting motor tricycles powered by petrol or diesel (three - wheelers) into electric powered motor tricycles, the tare weight of such motor tricycles (three - wheelers) increases. Therefore, approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022\u201108\u201108 to amend the definition in the Motor Traffic Act as the maximum tare weight of a motor tricycles (three - wheelers) as 600 kg, in order to resolve the interpretation issues arising during the registration of such motor tricycles (three-wheelers). However, taking into account the need to introduce a battery system that is capable of covering longer distances on a single charge, the need for a battery system with a higher capacity for air-conditioned luxury motor tricycles (three\u2011wheelers), and the added weight when using electric resistance - operated brakes, local manufacturers engaged in the production and conversion of electric motor tricycles (three-wheelers) have requested the Department of Motor Traffic to revise the definition in such a manner that the tare weight of an electric powered motor tricycle (three-wheeler), including the weight of the battery system shall not exceed 650 kg. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Transport, Highways, Ports and Civil Aviation, it was decided to grant policy approval of the Cabinet to amend the Motor Traffic Act incorporating the proposed amendment."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-21-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2025-04-21",
    "description": "Establishment of the Gambling Regulatory Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13133",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-21 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish the Gambling Regulatory Authority to function as the sole independent regulator with a broad and overarching scope on operations in the gambling industry in Sri Lanka including online and off\u2011shore gambling activities on ships and in the Colombo Port City. Clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared as per the approval granted by the Cabinet on 2025\u201102\u201124 to prepare a Bill for the same. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development to publish the Gambling Regulatory Authority Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
