    "doc_id": "2025-03-10-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2025-03-10",
    "description": "Payment of annual contributions to the International Solar Alliance (ISA) and signing of the Country Partnership Framework (CPF) between Sri Lanka and ISA",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13072",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-03-10 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Solar Alliance has been established with the aim of supporting the member nations pathway to promote the use of solar energy. At present, 75 countries, including Sri Lanka, have become its members and 54 countries have ratified the Partnership Framework Agreement. Sri Lanka is required to pay a voluntary contribution of US$ 25,000 annually based on the category to which it belongs. As a member State, Sri Lanka has the opportunity to accrue benefits such as capacity building relating to solar energy sector through Solar Technology Application Resource Centres (STAR-C), Policy Development, Access to Funding, Global Networking, Knowledge Exchange, from the International Solar Alliance. Accordingly, the following proposals made by the Minister of Energy, were approved by the Cabinet:\n\n*\tto continue the payment of an annual contribution of US$ 25,000 from the financial year 2024/25 onwards.\n\n*\tto establish a Solar Technology Application Resource Centre (STAR-C) in Sri Lanka.\n\n*\tto sign the 'Country Partnership Framework' between Sri Lanka and the International Solar Alliance."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-03-10-002-en",
