    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-12-30",
    "description": "Implementation of the Pledge Loan Scheme carried out previously for the purchase of paddy, as an Annual Programme from the Maha Season - 2024/25",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12961",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-30 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2023\u201108\u201114, has decided to implement a Pledge Loan Scheme for Small and Medium Scale (SME) Paddy Millers through State Banks at a concessionary interest rate with the objective of ensuring a reasonable price for paddy harvest and strengthening SME Paddy Millers. Since it has been observed that this programme has achieved high progress in the previous seasons, it has been identified that it is desirable to implement the said programme in every season from the Maha Season \u2011 2024/25. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development to implement a Pledge Loan Scheme up to a maximum of Rs. 50 million for the SME Paddy Millers (including Co-operative Societies operating paddy mills) with a maximum daily milling capacity of 25 MT, through the State and Private Banks under a concessionary interest rate, subject to a few specific criteria, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-12-30-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-12-30",
    "description": "Submission of the First Biennial Transparency Report of Sri Lanka to the \tUnited Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12960",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-30 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has been a party to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change since 1993 and the Paris Agreement since 2016. Accordingly, Sri Lanka is committed to implementing the decisions taken by the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change and the Paris Agreement. Under Article 13 of the Paris Agreement, each party should submit its First Biennial Transparency Report in relation to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change before 2024\u201112\u201131. The First Biennial Transparency Report of Sri Lanka has been prepared in keeping with guidelines of the the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change, Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change and the Paris Agreement. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to submit the said Report to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-12-30-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-12-30",
    "description": "Appointment of an Officials' Committee for expeditious strategic decision?making on the implementation of public investment projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12959",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-30 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with section 44(3) of the Public Finance Management Act, No.44 of 2024, there shall be a Committee appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers comprising of not more than eleven (11) members from the Heads of entities responsible for planning, resource mobilizing, budgeting, financing and monitoring relating to taking expeditious strategic decisions on the implementation of public investment projects, based on the information provided by the Chief Accounting Officers and the Accounting Officers. It is observed that it has not been possible to move towards the targeted development due to the failure to achieve the anticipated results and the benefits commensurate with the cost incurred from public capital investment in the past decade. Therefore, the Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to the proposal made by the Hon. President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, to establish a ''Public Investment Monitoring and Evaluation Committee'' consisting of 11 members, including two Secretaries to the Ministries and a Senior Additional Secretary to the President, to be appointed by the Secretary to the President, enabling to overcome various problems affecting the implementation of the development projects/programmes and to suggest measures to be taken in relation to project management and monitoring."
  },
