    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sugathadasa National Sports Complex is an internationally recognized first class sports complex, and is the only sports complex in Sri Lanka, which is equipped with 400, 200 and 80 meter synthetic running tracks with all the facilities of International Standards. The resurfacing of these synthetic running tracks had been carried out in year 2018, and Athletics Association of Sri Lanka has reported that the condition of the tracks is not suitable even for the national level sports competitions due to the numerous damages that exist on those tracks at present. with the aim of providing the necessary facilities to guide athletes to the national and international level, it has been identified that the renovation of these synthetic running tracks in conformity with the international standards should be a task of high national priority. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Youth Affairs and Sports to resurface the synthetic running tracks of the Sugathadasa National Sports Complex, prepare the football ground located in the middle, install the necessary electronic time machines and to renovate the light towers by following the prescribed procurement process, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-12-18-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-12-18",
    "description": "Administration of Temporary Shelters for providing Protection to Female Victims of Violence",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12937",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to providing temporary care and protection to female victims of gender based violence and children, the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs maintains ten (10) shelters viz. one each in Gampaha, Ratnapura, Monaragala, Colombo, Matara, Batticaloa, Mullaitivu and Jaffna Districts and two (02) shelters in Anuradhapura District, and it has been planned to start a temporary shelter in Nuwara\u2011Eliya District from January 2025. The administration and maintenance cost of some shelters is directly borne by the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs, while the relevant cost of some shelters is borne by women-welfare based Organizations. Protection to 2,852 female victims has been provided from 2020 up to the second quarter of the year 2024 and a cost of Rs.60.35 million has been borne for the same. However, the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs has received only an allocation of Rs.37.69 million for the purpose during the said period and bills amounting to Rs.22 million remain to be settled. Accordingly, taking into consideration to the proposal made by the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, Cabinet approval was granted to allocate Rs.25 million for the year 2025 and for the allocation of the necessary provisions for the ensuing years through the Annual Budgetary Estimates."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-12-18-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-12-18",
    "description": "Programme for providing morning meal to children in Early Childhood Development Centres/Pre-schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12936",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Secretariat for Early Childhood Development implements a programme from the year 2017 under the technical guidance of the Ministry of Health, to provide morning meal for children in Early Childhood Development Centres/Pre-schools where there is a high percentage of underweight children. As at present, each child is granted Rs.60/- per day and it is expected to extend the benefits for about 155,000 children in the year 2025. As the current daily allocation of Rs.60/- in insufficient due to the increase of prices of food items, the proposal made by the Minister of Women and Child Affairs to increase the sum of Rs.60/- allocated for each child per day up to Rs.100/- and to implement the said programme in future in Early Childhood Development Centres/Pre-schools to be selected based on the criteria of \"Pre\u2011schools with high percentage of underweight children\", was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-12-18-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-12-18",
    "description": "Securing additional provisions for the completion of the balance works of the Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12935",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The \u201cWater Supply and Sanitation Improvement Project\u201d has been initiated to increase the access to pipe-borne water services and improve sanitation facilities, focusing 540 Grama Niladhari Divisions in 07 Districts viz. Mullativu, Kilinochchi, Badulla, Monaragala, Rathnapura, Kegalle and NuwaraEliya. For this purpose, a credit amount of USD 165 million has been granted by the International Development Association under the Investment Project Financing Instrument of the World Bank. An additional financing component (second phase) has been approved to expand the scope of the Project, under which the Projects on extension of existing pipelines have been identified and implemented in Matara, Kurunegala, Matale and Gampaha Districts as well. Despite the planning of the Projects to be completed by 2025-06-30, the total cost estimate of the Project has to be increased by Rs. 1,180 million due to the reasons such as price increase in construction materials and the revision of Value Added Tax (VAT). Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development, Construction and Housing to revise the total cost estimate of the Project and allocate necessary additional provisions through the Budget Estimates in year the 2025, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
