    "date_str": "2024-12-02",
    "description": "Granting permission to import rice without obtaining Import Control Licenses",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12912",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-02 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet considered the suitability of temporarily removing the restrictions currently existing for the importation of rice, taking into consideration the scarcity of Nadu rice and other varieties of rice in the local market and the loss that has  occurred to the paddy cultivation due to the heavy rain persisted in the last few days. Accordingly, it was decided to grant permission with immediate effect to import rice to the country without obtaining import control licenses  until 2024-12-20."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-12-02-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2024-12-02",
    "description": "Provision of an allowance for School- Age Children to purchase stationery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12911",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-12-02 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- A survey conducted by the Department of Census and Statistics has revealed that the adverse effects of the economic crisis have caused a significant negative impact on the education of 55% of school children. This percentage is higher in rural and estate areas, and it has been revealed that 53.2% of the affected children have either reduced or completely stopped purchasing school stationery, where as 26.1% have resorted to reusing previously used school stationery. Therefore, with the aim of minimizing the adverse impact on the education of school children, the proposal made by the Hon. President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, to provide an allowance for school children to purchase school stationery before the commencement of academic activities in the year 2025, as follows, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\t* Provision of an allowance of Rs.6000/- per child for the children of Aswesuma Beneficiary families to purchase stationery through the Welfare Benefits Board.\n\n\t* Provision of an allowance of Rs.6000/- through the Ministry of Education, \tHigher Education and Vocational \tEducation for each child who fall into the categories of parentless children not included in the Aswesuma programme, children from families where mother or father is disabled, all \tschool age children in orphanages and children who have left \tdestitute, due to special circumstances."
  },
