    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-11-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Post of Director General of the Department of External Resources has fallen vacant due to the appointment of Mr. D. A. P. Abeysekara, Special Grade Office of the Sri Lanka Planning Service who served in the said Post, to a Post of Deputy Secretary to the Treasury with effect from 2024\u201111\u201106. The Post of Director General, Department of Project Management and Monitoring is also due to fall vacant, since Mr. N.S.M.P. Ranjith, Special Grade Officer of the Sri Lanka Planning Service is due to retire from the Public Service on reaching 60 years of age on 2024\u201111\u201110. A suitable officer has to be appointed to the Post of Director General of the Public Debt Management Office as well, scheduled to be established in the General Treasury. Accordingly, on a proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Development, Policy Formulation, Planning and Tourism, the Cabinet decided to make the following appointments:\n\n*\tAppointment of Mr. R.M.S.P.S. Bandara, Special Grade Officer of the Sri Lanka Planning Service, presently serving as an Additional Director General of the Department of External Resources, to the Post of Director General of the Department of External Resources with effect from 2024\u201111\u201106.\n\n*\tAppointment of Mr. S.S. Mudalige, Special Grade Officer of the Sri Lanka Planning Service, presently serving as the Director General of the Highways Division of the Ministry of Transport, Highways, Ports and Civil Aviation, to the Post of Director General of the Department of Project Management and Monitoring and for the continuation of the appointment to act in the Post of General Manager of Railways.\n\n*\tAppointment of Mrs. Udeni Udugahapatthuwa, Grade 1 Officer of the Sri Lanka Planning Service, presently serving as a Director of the Department of External Resources, to act in the Post of Director General of the Public Debt Management Office with effect from 2024\u201112\u201101, scheduled to be established in the General Treasury."
