    "doc_id": "2024-09-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-09-30",
    "description": "Revisiting the Entitlements, Allowances and Privileges of the Members of Parliament, Ministers and Former Presidents",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12830",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-30 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Members of Parliament elected by the people, the Ministers and the former Presidents have been provided with different entitlements, allowances and privileges such as salaries, allowances, pensions, official quarters, vehicles, staff, office equipment, security personnel etc. The Government has to incur a considerable cost from the public taxes for the provision of said entitlements, allowances and privileges and it has been found the need to reduce this huge expenses within the existing fiscal space. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in her capacity as the Minister of Justice, Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils, Local Government and Labour to appoint a Committee with the following composition, to examine the matters in that regard and submit a Report with appropriate recommendations within two (02) months to limit the irrational entitlements, allowances and privileges which are causing an unnecessary burden to the General Treasury on a rational basis or to introduce other suitable alternative methodologies:\n\n*\tJustice K.T. Chitrasiri - (Chairman),\n\u00a0\u00a0\tRetired Judge of the Supreme Court;\n\n*\tMr. D. Dissanayake,\n\u00a0\u00a0\tRetired Ministry Secretary;\n\n*\tMrs. Jayantha C.T. Bulumulla,\n\u00a0\u00a0\tRetired District Secretary/Government Agent;"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-09-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-09-30",
    "description": "Making Provisions for the General Election 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12829",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-30 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- By the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2403/13 dated 2024\u201109\u201124, the 09th Parliament was dissolved and 2024\u201111\u201114 has been fixed as the date for the Parliamentary General Election. However, provisions required to conduct a Parliamentary General Election have not been allocated within the budget estimates 2024. In such case, it was decided to grant the concurrence of the Cabinet for the action taken by the Hon. President to issue Rs.05 billion from the Consolidated Fund for the year 2024, in terms of the powers vested with the President by paragraph (4) of Article 150 of the Constitution for the issuance of funds from the Consolidated Fund to conduct a Parliamentary General Election. Further, approval of the Cabinet was also granted to allocate Rs.06 billion for the expenses to be settled in the year 2025 for conducting the General Election, from the Vote on Account to be submitted to Parliament for the year 2025."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-09-13-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2024-09-13",
    "description": "Granting Pardon to Mr. Diyunuge Edward Henry Pedris who was executed 109 years ago by an unjustifiable judgment of the Colonial Court Martial",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12828",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mr. Diyunuge Edward Henry Pedris who was then 27 years old, had been sentenced to death on 1915\u201107\u201107 without considering any appeal by the Colonial Administration of Sri Lanka, being convicted for the offence of treason, having court\u2011martialed him, allegedly accusing him of inciting riots and treason against the Government. The remains of Mr. Diyunuge Edward Henry Pedris had been cremated in an undisclosed location by adopting the procedure prescribed for cremating a criminal convicted under the martial law. It had been revealed later that his assassination had been executed as a plan of the senior officials who ruled the country then. Accordingly, upon the submission of the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2401/23 dated 2024\u201109\u201112 issued by the Hon. President, on the posthumous Presidential Pardon granted to the Late Mr. Diyunuge Edward Henry Pedris who had been unlawfully executed on 1915\u201107\u201107 after an unjust trial, it was decided to grant the concurrence of the Cabinet for the action taken by the Hon. President."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-09-13-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2024-09-13",
    "description": "Amending the Proposed Personal Income Tax Structure",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12827",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a measure to increase the Government tax revenue, a method of taxation on personal income was introduced from 2023\u201101\u201101 with the annual income tax exemption limit of Rs.1.2 million and the marginal tax rate from 6% to 36%. As a result, although the tax revenue of the Government was increased, the Government initiated discussions with the International Monetary Fund regarding the requests received to the fact that the middle-income earning group, who were more affected by the personal income tax, should receive some relief. The facts that the revenue targets of the Government are being met by the mid 2024 and certain fiscal targets have been over performed, were brought to the attention at those discussions. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to take necessary action to amend the Inland Revenue Act, No.24 of 2017, enabling to pursue action as follows from 2025\u201104\u201101 and impose legal provisions required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tMaintaining the Tax free threshold as the same value of Rs. 1.2 million.\n\n*\tIncreasing the first tax bracket of which the taxable income is determined from \tRs. 500,000 to Rs. 720,000.\n\n*\tThereafter, increasing each tax bracket up to the fifth tax bracket by Rs.220,000 each.\n\n*\tMaintaining the existing tax tares ranging from 6% to 36% unchanged.\n\n*\tAccordingly, the impact of the proposed amendments would be as follows:\n\n\n\n\nMonthly Income (Rs.)\nPercentage deducted from the current tax charged\n\n\n\n\n150,000/-\n14%\n\n\n200,000/-\n20%\n\n\n300,000/-\n25%\n\n\n400,000/-\n23%\n\n\n500,000/-\n15%\n\n\n750,000/-\n8%\n\n\n1,000,000/-\n6%"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-09-13-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2024-09-13",
    "description": "Penal Code (Amendment) Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12826",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2024\u201104\u201129 to amend the Penal Code to prohibit corporal punishment in any sphere and to make appropriate legislation for the same. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-09-13-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2024-09-13",
    "description": "Removal of the temporary suspension on the importation of Motor Vehicles",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12825",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a measure to reduce the increasing pressure on the country's foreign exchange market and to ensure the distribution of available foreign exchange for the importation of essential goods including medicine, fuel and food, the importation of non-essential goods has been temporarily suspended from March 2020. In view of the recovery of the economy with the reform measures agreed under the Extended Fund Facility Programme of the International Monetary Fund, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to lift the temporary import suspension related to the importation of motor vehicles and non-motorized goods classified under 304 HS Codes, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tGranting permission to import vehicles used for public passenger transportation, vehicles used for special purposes and other non\u2011motorized goods to be effective from 2024\u201110\u201101.\n\n*\tGranting permission to import vehicles used for commercial or goods transportation to be effective from 2024\u201112\u201101.\n\n*\tGranting permission to import motor vehicles used for personal purpose (Cars, Vans, Sport Utility Vehicles, Pickups etc.) to be effective from 2025\u201102\u201101."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-09-13-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-09-13",
    "description": "Implementation of Floating Solar Projects on Reservoirs belonging to the Mahaweli Authority of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12824",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has given priority to the development of floating solar projects on the existing water bodies in order to increase the generation of renewable energy. Accordingly, the Sri Lanka Mahaweli Authority of Sri Lanka has identified 03 main reservoirs namely Randenigala, Moragahakanda and Kalawewa for the development of floating solar projects. Feasibility studies have been conducted regarding the aforesaid places. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to authorize the Ceylon Electricity Board to select investors under the competitive procurement procedure for the development of floating solar projects in the Randenigala, Moragahakanda and Kalawewa reservoirs, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
