    "date_str": "2024-08-26",
    "description": "Implementation of the proposed Skills Development Programme from the year 2025 onwards",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12782",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-26 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet Appointed Oversight Committee on the implementation of the National Education Policy Framework has submitted the following proposals to implement on priority basis:\n\n(i)\tTo provide 50,000 job focused training scholarships annually, aiming high-demand industry specific jobs through the network of public or private Vocational Training Centres to be effective from 2025 under a Student Based Funding Scheme.\n\n(ii)\tTo award 60,000 Opportunities of Vocational Training Courses annually targeting students engaged in secondary education.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Chairman of the Cabinet Appointed Oversight Committee on the implementation of the National Education Policy Framework to implement the said proposals and to allocate provisions by the General Treasury for the ensuing period of 05 years from the year 2025 so as to securing the provisions required for the same through the financial investment of Rs. 100 million already agreed and proposed to be implemented by the Asian Development Bank and the Government and to implement the National Education Policy Framework together with the Cabinet Appointed Oversight Committee appointed to implement the said Framework and the Ministry of Education, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
