    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Child Protection Authority has introduced the National Guidelines for Child Day Care Centers in the year 2017 with a view to ensuring that all Child Day Care Centers located throughout the Island follow the same operating procedure and introducing a formal registration and supervision mechanism. Accordingly, the National Policy on Child Day Care Facilities has been prepared to implement the child day care service in a uniform manner in every Province and to ensure the introduction of a formal regulatory and monitoring mechanism. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment to implement the said National Policy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-08-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-08-05",
    "description": "Increasing the efficiency and quality of the Public Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12721",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that it would be appropriate to integrate the information technology systems in the Public institutions with a view to enhancing the efficiency and quality in the public institutions as well as discharging duties effectively and optimum manner by minimizing the duplication errors and the verification of information. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to take action as follows when entering data to the information technology systems regulated/ developed by all Public Sector Institutions including State Corporations and Statutory Boards, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tmaking it compulsory to use the National Identity Card number to recognize a Sri Lankan citizen who is older than 15 years.\n\n*\tmaking it mandatory to use the Passport number to recognize a foreign national.\n\n*\tmaking it compulsory to use the Business Registration Number to recognize the identity of institutions and the National Identity Card Number of Sri Lankan members of Owners/Board of Directors of such institutions and the passport of number of foreign members.\n\n*\tensuring data standardization enabling to share the relevant data formally with the other Public Sector Institutions."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-08-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-08-05",
    "description": "Establishment of a Regional Centre for Maritime Studies in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12720",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into account the maritime security and the various initiatives taken by Sri Lanka in that regard as a member of the Indian Ocean Rim Association (IORA), the Government of France has identified Sri lanka as the most appropriate location to establish a \"Regional Centre for Maritime Studies\" in order to circulate the knowledge and procedures obtained through the common studies throughout the Region. It has been proposed to establish the proposed Centre at the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and to obtain the necessary assistance and infrastructure facilities for the same from the Naval and Maritime Academy at Trincomalee. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to enter into a Bilateral Agreement between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of France pertaining to the establishment of the proposed \"Regional Centre for Maritime Studies\", was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
