    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "Public Assets Management Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12699",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201110\u201117 has granted approval to identify and compile a National Asset Register of Non-financial immovable or movable assets fully owned, assigned, possessed, vested in, held or utilized by a public institution and to introduce a Law on state asset management, incorporating the provisions for updating the said Register from time to time and ensuring the receipt of proper returns of these Assets to the Government institutions. Accordingly, the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman has received the clearance of the Attorney General. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-22-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "National Agenda for Anti-Corruption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12698",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- When the present Government took over in July 2022, their priority was to restore the fiscal and debt sustainability and transform the economy by improving governance and eliminating corruption. Accordingly, the foundation for the Anti-Corruption Agenda was laid through the enactment of the Anti-Corruption Act, No.9 of 2023 repealing the Bribery Act (Chapter 26), the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption Act, No.19 of 1994 and the Declaration of Assets and Liabilities Law No.1 of 1975, in order to enforce the provisions of the United Nations Convention against Corruption and other relevant international norms and practices such as the Financial Action Task Force Standards. Also, currently, the preparation of the Proceeds of Crime Bill is at the final stage. Accordingly, the following measures have been identified as key action items in the Anti-Corruption Agenda in line with the Legal, Organizational and Strategic Frameworks for Anti-Corruption as stated in the International Monetary Fund Governance Diagnostic Technical Assistance Report.\n\n* Enactment of the Anti-Corruption Act, No.9 of 2023\n\n* Developing a National Anti-Corruption Plan for the period 2025-2029\n\n* Amendment of the National Audit Act, No.19 of 2018.\n\n* Establishment of an effective and transparent Asset Declaration and Conflict of Interest Systems.\n\n* Introducing new methodologies to execute the Proceeds of Crime and Money Laundering.\n\n* Strengthening Investigation and Prosecution of Corruption Cases.\n\n* Introducing amendments to the Companies Act, No.07 of 2007 enabling to strengthen the Beneficial Ownership Framework and taking other relevant measures.\n\n* Enactment of a Public Procurement Law to ensure the transparency of the Public Procurement.\n\n* Publishing all the firms receiving tax exemptions under the Strategic Development Projects Act, No.14 of 2008 and through the Board of Investment.\n\n* Temporary suspending the application of the Strategic Development Projects Act, No.14 of 2008, until the promulgation of an explicit and transparent process for the evaluation of proposals and costing of investment promotion conditions.\n\n* Implementing a State-Owned Enterprises Reform Policy.\n\n* Initiation of short-term Anti-corruption measures within each revenue department.\n\n* Establishment of a new management arrangement for the Employee Provident Fund.\n\n* Revision of legislation, regulations and processes relating to financial sector oversight in the banking sector.\n\n* Empowering the Judicial Services Commission.\n\n* Strengthening the Right to Information.\n\r\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to confirm the Anti-Corruption Agenda as the National Agenda of the Government for Anti-Corruption in principle and direct all the relevant authorities to comply with the said Agenda, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-22-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "Amendments to the Online Safety Act No.9 of 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12697",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Subsequent to the passage of the Online Safety Act in Parliament adhering to the decision given by the Supreme Court pertaining to the said Bill, the Online Safety Act No.9 of 2024 is in force at present. Even though, experts in the field had proposed amendments with regard to certain clauses in the said Bill prior to the passage of the said Bill in Parliament, it was not possible to incorporate such amendments to the Bill at the Committee Stage. Accordingly, approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201102\u201112 to prepare a Bill to amend the Online Safety Act No.9 of 2024 by incorporating the said amendments. As such, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. The Proposal made by the Minister of Public Security to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and to submit the same thereafter to Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-22-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "Establishment of a Regulatory Institution in the Name of \"Films Sri Lanka\" \tinstead of the proposed \"National Films Development Commission\"",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12696",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal submitted to establish the \"National Films Development Commission\" to establish a new institutional framework enabling the National Film Corporation to move away from the current business activities and carry out regulatory-based activities, provide opportunities and facilities to enter the digital platform thereby moving the local cinema to the international arena, was taken up for discussion at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201104\u201129. In this instance, it has been decided that all stakeholders in the film industry should be consulted and views be obtained regarding the proposal. Accordingly, it has been decided to replace the name of the \"National Films Development Commission\" with \"Films Sri Lanka\" based on the matters furnished at the discussion held with the relevant parties and to take into account the proposals presented at the said meeting in the preparation of the proposed Bill.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill for the establishment of \"Films Sri Lanka\" based on the above matters, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-22-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "Amendments to the Inland Revenue Act, No.24 of 2017 to expedite the Tax Appeals Process",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12695",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the provisions of the Inland Revenue Act, any taxpayer aggrieved by a decision of the Department of Inland Revenue can submit an appeal to the Commissioner General of Inland Revenue on such decision. The Commissioner General of Inland Revenue should give his decision in that regard not later than 02 years. Any taxpayer aggrieved by the said decision too can submit an appeal to the Tax Appeals Commission to review the said decision, and the decision of the Tax Appeals Commission must be given within 270 days from the date of receipt of such review request. Accordingly, the said appeal process may take almost three years whereby approximately 73 billion rupees of tax could not be charged to the government revenue during the past. Taking into account the said matters, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to introduce appropriate amendments to the Inland Revenue Act, No. 24 of 2017 to expedite and regulate the tax appeal process, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-22-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "Conserving the 'Gedige' tradition Statue Chamber in the Gadaladeniya Sadhdarmathilaka Rajamaha Viharaya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12694",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Gadaladeniya Sadhdarmathilaka Rajamaha Viharaya was built during the Gampola Era according to the Pallawa architecture under the patronage of a thero known as Dharmakeerthi. It has been proposed to build a covering roof for the purpose of conserving the chamber of Gedige tradition of the said temple. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to assign the above task to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau which is an institution possessing the capacity and resources for that purpose, since the Department of Archaeology does not possess required human resources and technical equipment, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
