    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- A land in extent of about 0.1765 hectares belonging to the Department of Irrigation and along with the buildings located therein have been vested with the then Ministry of Higher Education, with the approval of the Cabinet, on 50 years lease basis for the hostel requirement of female students studying in the Institute of Indigenous Medicine. By the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2023\u201102\u201113, the Institute of Indigenous Medicine has been transformed into a Faculty of the University of Colombo and the said Faculty has decided to utilize the aforementioned land to be utilized for the hostel requirement of  female students. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to vest the plot of land located at No.330, Dr. N.M. Perera Mawatha, Colombo 08 with the University of Colombo, enabling to utilize the said land for the hostel requirement of the female students of the said Faculty, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-22-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "Preparation of Reports to be submitted to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12683",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change and the Paris Agreement, Sri Lanka is obliged to prepare National Communication Reports on Climate Change and submit the same to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change. Accordingly, the First Biennial Transparency Report is scheduled to be submitted by 2024\u201112\u201131 and the Second Biennial Transparency Report by 2026\u201112\u201131. Also, Sri Lanka should submit its Fourth National Communication Report in 2027. The Ministry of Environment has submitted a Project Report to the Global Environment Facility in order to secure funds required to prepare such Reports and submit the same during the period of 2024\u20112028. The Global Environment Facility has agreed to provide a Grant of US$1.23 million for the preparation of related reports based on the said Project Report. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Environment to enter into relevant Agreements to obtain the said Grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-22-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "National Social Protection Policy of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12682",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Disjointed programmes, schemes, institutions and products which are integral in the current Social Protection System are proven to have limited effectiveness in the said Social Protection System and less contribution to the National development. Accordingly, the Ministry of Finance,Economic Stabilization and National Policies has identified the necessity of having a Social Protection System for Sri Lanka. The National Social Protection Policy has been formulated to provide a strategic guidance for the development of a well-coordinated and harmonized Social Protection System with the contribution of all relevant parties. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, to implement the said Policy was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
