    "decision_details_body": "- Approval  of  the  Cabinet  has  been  granted  on  2024\u201103\u201118  to  amend  the  Primary  Court's  Procedure  Act  in  order  to  overcome  the  issues  faced  by  the  applicants  who  make  applications  under  section  66  of  the  said  Act.  Accordingly,  the  Certificate  of  Constitutionality  of  the  Attorney  General  has  been  received  for  the  Bill  prepared  by  the  Legal  Draftsman.  The  proposal  made  by  the  Minister  of  Justice,  Prison  Affairs  and  Constitutional  Reforms,  to  publish  the  said  Bill  in  the  Government  Gazette  and  thereafter,  present  the  same  in  Parliament  for  approval,  was  approved  by  the  Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-15-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2024-07-15",
    "description": "Obtaining  approval  for  the  amendments  proposed  to  the  Animal  Welfare  Bill  by  the  Sectoral  Oversight  Committee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12671",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-15 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval  of  the  Cabinet  has  been  granted  on  2022\u201101\u201110  to  submit  the  Animal  Welfare  Bill,  to  Parliament  and  accordingly,  the  said  Bill  has  been  submitted  to  Parliament.  The  said  Bill  has  been  submitted  to  the  Sectoral  Oversight  Committee  on  Food  Security  and  Agriculture  for  its  recommendations  and  the  said  Committee  has  proposed  several  amendments  to  the  said  Bill.  The  Legal  Draftsman  has  prepared  the  said  amendments  so  that  it  could  be  presented  at  the  Committee  Stage  of  the  said  Bill  in  Parliament  and  the  clearance  of  the  Attorney  general  has  been  received  for  the  same.  Accordingly,  the  proposal  made  by  the  Minister  of  Agriculture  and  Plantation  Industries  to  present  the  relevant  amendments  at  the  Committee  Stage  of  the  Animal  Welfare  Bill  in  Parliament,  was  approved  by  the  Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-15-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2024-07-15",
    "description": "Procuring  medicinal  Ginger  required  for  manufacturing  purposes  in  the  Sri  Lanka  Ayurvedic  Drugs  Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12670",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-15 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Medicinal  ginger  is  used  as  an  ingredient  for  87  types  of  medicines  manufactured  by  the  Sri  Lanka  Ayurvedic  Drugs  Corporation,  and  currently  there  is  a  severe  shortage  of  medicinal  ginger  in  the  market.  There  is  a  stock  of  50  tons  of  medicinal  ginger  that  has  been  confiscated  by  the  Sri  Lanka  Customs,  and  the  the  proposal  made  by  the  Minister  of  Health  to  get  the  said  stock  of  medicinal  ginger  at  concessional  prices  to  the  Sri  Lanka  Ayurveda  Drugs  Corporation,  was  approved  by  the  Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-15-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2024-07-15",
    "description": "Launching  the  SMART  Youth  Exhibitions  &  Nights-2024  Programme  implemented  by  the  National  Youth  Services  Council,  islandwide",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12669",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-15 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The  young  community  had  to  face  an  extremely  stressful  situation  due  to  the  restrictions  of  travel,  mutual  relationships,  personal  meetings  and  gatherings  in  groups  amidst  the  severe  impact  of  the  Covid-19  pandemic,  which  prevailed  globally  for  two  years  from  the  year  2019.  It  has  been  found  that  it  is  advisable  to  hold  recreational  programmes  islandwide  aimed  at  preventing  the  youth  from  being  subjected  to  such  pressures,  developing  their  entertainment,  enjoyment  and  mental  wellness,  providing  opportunities  for  the  young  community  to  maintain  social  relationships  physically,  and  giving  them  the  opportunity  to  work  together  as  well.  Accordingly,  the  proposal  made  by  the  Minister  of  Sports  and  Youth  Affairs  to  implement  the  SMART  Youth  Exhibitions  &  Nights  -  2024  programme  covering  the  entire  island,  was  approved  by  the  Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-15-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-07-15",
    "description": "Completion  of  the  work  of  the  Nanu  Oya  Railway  Station  Modernization  Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12668",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-15 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval  of  the  Cabinet  has  been  granted  at  the  Cabinet  meeting  held  on  2023\u201104\u201103  to  implement  the  Nanu  Oya  Railway  Station  Modernization  Project  utilizing  the  funds  of  the  Sri  Lanka  Tourism  Development  Authority  and  the  Sri  Lanka  Tourism  Promotion  Bureau.  Due  to  revision  in  the  prices  of  construction  materials,  the  contract  value  of  Rs.74.63  million  for  the  modernization  of  Nanu  Oya  railway  station  has  increased  to  Rs.101.81  million.  Accordingly,  Cabinet  approved  the  proposal  made  by  the  Minister  of  Tourism  and  Lands  to  complete  the  relevant  modernization  works  under  the  Central  Engineering  Consultancy  Bureau,  on  the  recommendation  of  the  Department  of  Sri  Lanka  Railways  and  to  secure  additional  provisions  required  for  the  purpose  from  the  Sri  Lanka  Tourism  Development  Authority  and  the  Sri  Lanka  Tourism  Promotion  Bureau."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-15-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-07-15",
    "description": "Allocation  of  Funds  from  the  Saudi  Fund  for  Development  to  complete  \tthe  \tsection  I  of  the  half  completed  work  of  the  Godagama-Homagama  \tRoad",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12667",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-15 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Funds  of  the  Saudi  Fund  for  Development  have  been  utilized  to  implement  the  Kurinchakerny  Bridge  Project  in  Trincomalee  District.  After  completion  of  the  procurement  process  of  the  said  project,  there  is  still  a  loan  balance  of  US$  10.5  and  it  has  been  decided  to  utilize  the  said  balance  amount  for  the  completion  of  Section  I  of  the  Godagama-Homagama  road,  which  is  half  completed.  In  order  to  complete  the  rest  of  the  said  road,  an  amount  of  US$  12  million  is  needed  and  the  Saudi  Fund  for  Development  has  agreed  to  provide  the  remaining  US$1.5  million  from  the  loan  amount  of  the  Road  Network  Development  Project  funded  by  the  Saudi  Fund  for  Development.  Accordingly,  the  proposal  made  by  the  Minister  of  Transport  and  Highways,  to  secure  funds  and  complete  section  I  of  the  Godagama-Homagama  road,  which  is  half  completed,  was  approved  by  the  Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
