    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Initial discussions have been held between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Asian Development Bank for the implementation of the Power Sector\t Reforms and Financial Sustainability Programme. The proposed programme consists of 03 sub\u2011programmes and it is expected to receive a loan amount of\tUSD 300 million by USD 100 million for each sub-programme. The\tproposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to obtain a USD 100 million loan from the Asian Development Bank to finance the proposed sub\u2011programme\u201101 for the implementation of institutional structural reforms in the Ceylon Electricity Board and the Lanka Electricity Company (Pvt) Ltd., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Comprehensive Strategies to uplift the Small and Medium Scale Enterprise Sector in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12632",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Micro, Small and Medium Scale Enterprises make a direct contribution for generating employment, fostering innovation and for economic growth in Sri Lanka. Due to the economic difficulties faced by Sri Lanka in the past period, the Micro, Small and Medium Scale entrepreneurs were severely affected. Therefore, taking into account the need to province investment and working capital assistance to revitalize those entrepreneurs, the Government has taken steps to implement a number of strategies. Accordingly, the project for re\u2011empowerment of the Micro, Small and Medium Scale Enterprises sector has been implemented under Asian Development Bank funds, in order to implement the loan projects in the Small and Medium Scale Enterprise sector and about 40 billion rupees have been allocated for the year 2024 for the same. In addition, approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201102\u201124 for the implementation of an Incentive Loan Scheme worth 20 billion rupees with the aim of re-energizing the Micro, Small and Medium Scale entrepreneurs as well. It is planned to allocate 02 billion rupees from the said provisions and implement a special loan scheme for women entrepreneurs as well by creating a Revolving Fund and the said loan scheme is scheduled to be implemented from 2024\u201107\u201101. The information presented by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies was considered by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Amendment of the Employees' Provident Fund Act, No.15 of 1958",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12631",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Employees' Provident Fund has been established by the Employees' Provident Fund Act, No. 15 of 1958 for the social security of the private and semi\u2011government sector employees who are not entitled to a pension. It has been identified the necessity of amending the said Act to increase the number of members covered by the Act in accordance with the current socio-economic changes and to provide quality and efficient service to the members to suit the present. The proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill based on the initial Draft prepared accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Criminal Procedure (Special Provisions) Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12630",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Criminal Procedure Amendment Act, No.25 of 2024 has been passed in Parliament on 2024\u201105\u201131 in order to provide for Judges to take into account the time spent by an accused in custody prior to his conviction as a part of his sentence for the offense for which he is convicted. However, since the above Bill does not apply to persons convicted prior to the passage of the said amendment Act, it has been identified that a mechanism to take into account the time spent in custody prior to their conviction or pending determination of the appeal is needed. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minster of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to introduce a special provisions law to execute the powers vested with the President under Article 34 of the Constitution so as to take necessary action with regard to the said convicted persons as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
