    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Construction of 934 Rainwater Harvesting Tanks in Jaffna District by the Government of India",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12627",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted on 2016\u201110\u201125 to sign a Memorandum of Understanding with the Government of India to construct 3,000 rainwater harvesting tanks in the District of Jaffna using the funds offered by the Government of India to supply clean potable water in the said District. Even though the project was scheduled to be completed within a period of 03 years, due to the financial and technical problems which have arisen, the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201110\u201110 has decided to extend the project period up to June 2024 and to install 1,831 PVC rainwater tanks instead of ferro-cement tanks. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to establish 934 water harvesting tanks using the remaining funds under the Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Establishment of the National Quality Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12626",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The necessity of establishing a National Quality Council has been pointed out through the National Quality Policy submitted in the year 2016, the National Quality Infrastructure Strategy 2018-2022 and the National Export Strategy of Sri Lanka 2018-2022. At present, National Quality Institutions and other National Quality Regulatory Agencies are functioning as independent institutions under the scopes of various Line Ministries. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security to appoint a Working Committee with the representations of the relevant Line Ministries and National Quality Institutions to implement the proposal for the establishment of the National Quality Council, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Revision of the Renewable Energy Purchase Tariff under the Standardized Power Purchase Agreement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12625",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Standardized Power Purchase Agreement should be entered into under a technology-based, Cost-reflective Feed in Tariff System pertaining to the Renewable Energy Projects with a capacity of 10MW or less as per the Sri Lanka Electricity Act, No. 20 of 2009 and its subsequent amendments. Accordingly, although approval of the Cabinet has been granted on 2023\u201103\u201113 to implement a variable renewable energy purchasing tariff, only a few developers have signed the Agreement for that purpose. Therefore, a Committee comprising of representatives from the Ministry of Power and Energy, the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, the Ceylon Electricity Board, the Sustainable Energy Authority of Sri lanka and the Central Bank of Sri Lanka has been appointed in order to obtain recommendations on the renewable energy tariff calculation. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to accept the price calculation formula submitted by the said Committee and to implement the proposed tariff revisions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Vesting a portion of Land in Kalmunai with the Urban Development Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12624",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Kalmunai town is one of the main service centres in the Ampara district and it is considered as an administrative, trade and commercial centre of the province. According to the Development Plan for the Kalmunai Municipal Council area, the coastal area of Kalmunai has been designated as a suitable area for tourism and recreational activities, but it has been recognized that the facilities available in the town are not adequate for tourism and recreational activities. Accordingly, in order to meet such requirements, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to take over a plot of land in extent of 01 rood 29.44 perches located in Rest House road in the coastal area of Kalmunai to the Urban Development Authority for a project to construct a Tourism Facility Centre, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Handing over the Henry Pedris Ground to the Isipathana College for Sports Activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12623",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Non\u2011availability of a permanent playground to the Isipathana College, Colombo where there are many talented players, has become a severe impediment to improve the skills of such players. Therefore, an Agreement was reached between the two parties in the year 2016 to use the Henry Pedris Ground owned by the Colombo Municipal Council to the sports activities of the Isipathana College, and the period of the said Agreement has ended in the year 2017. By handing over the Henry Pedris Ground to the Isipathana College, it can be properly improved and maintained and it will pave the way to productively utilize the said ground for the sports activities of the students of the College and also surrounding schools as well as the people of the area. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Sports and Youth Affairs to hand over the Henry Pedris Ground to the Isipathana College, keeping the name of the ground unchanged, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Project on sustainable and efficient Electric Mobility System in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12622",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The United Nations Environment Programme, an organization accredited by the Green Environment Fund, has granted US$ 1.09 million for the implementation of the project on Sustainable and Efficient Electric Mobility System in Sri Lanka. According to the project implementation plan, the Ministry of Environment has been identified as the National Designated Entity. However, since the scope of the project falls under the Ministry of Transport and Highways, the Ministry of Transport and Highways has the ability to take necessary measures to implement the project more efficiently together with all the relevant parties. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways, for the Ministry of Transport and Highways to become the executing agency of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Project Agreement between the Sri Lanka Export Development Board and the Swiss State Secretariat for Economic Affairs on Global Textile and Clothing Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12621",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to enter into a Project Agreement between the Swiss State Secretariat for Economic Affairs and the Sri Lanka Export Development Board to implement the second phase of the Global Textiles and Clothing Programme for Sri Lankan Textile and Clothing Sector. By entering into the said Agreement, Sri Lanka will be able to obtain the support of the Global Textiles and Clothing Programme for a transformation of Textile and Apparel Industry based on the shift towards quality green products by promoting digitization. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to sign the said agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Allocating a plot of land for the establishment of the Mahabage Police Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12620",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Mahabage Police Station which serves nearly 50,000 people living in 08 Grama Niladhari Divisions, is currently maintained in a small plot of land in extent of 21.5 perches bordering the Colombo - Negombo main road. Under this backdrop, due to the facts that there is no suitable place for vehicle parking and to keep court productions in safe custody, inadequate barracks and non availability of quarters for the officers, both the general public and the serving police officers encounter severe difficulties. Therefore, the proposal made by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government to allocate a plot of land in extent of 40 perches from the land where the Wattala divisional Secretariat Division has been previously established for the development of required facilities for the said police station, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-07-01-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Economic Empowerment of Women in the Micro, Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (MSME) Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12619",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that, in Sri Lanka, participation of women in economic activities is lower than other regional and Asian countries due to various reasons. According to the Sri Lanka Labour Force Survey conducted in the year 2022, out of the economically active population, 35% is women and it shows a significant disparity in the gender contribution rates of economic participation. Limited financial literacy and the factors such as that women do not have property or other collateral required for obtaining loans and lack of opportunities to access financial resources have been identified as the main obstacles encountered by women entrepreneurs in Sri Lanka. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. President to implement a special loan scheme in order to remove barriers preventing women from entering economic activities, utilizing Rs. 02 billion, out of Rs.20 billion which has been allocated to re-energize Micro, Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (MSME) Sector by the Cabinet decision dated 2024\u201102\u201126, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-06-24-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2024-06-24",
    "description": "Amending the Mediation Boards Act, No.72 of 1988",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12617",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-06-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2023\u201109\u201125 to amend the section 7 of the Mediation Boards Act, No.72 of 1988, in order to overcome administrative issues such as unavailability of constituted or functioning mediation boards or delay in issuing the Certificate of Non\u2011settlement by the Mediation Board and to fulfill the requirement of not preventing the parties from resorting to the Court of Law, in the event both parties accept that there is no settlement. Accordingly, the Legal Draftsman has prepared the amending Bill and the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the same. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
