    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2023-01-09 to call for Expressions of Interest from the interested parties for the use of facilities of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport. Expressions of interest have been called accordingly and 05 institutions have submitted their Expressions of interest. The proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to transfer the management of Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport to M/s Shaurya Aeronautics (Pvt) Ltd and Airports of Regions Management Company of Russia or its joint venture for a period of 30 years as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Amendment of the Civil Aviation Authority of Sri Lanka Act, No.34 of 2002 and the Civil Aviation Act, No.14 of 2010",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12511",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found essential to amend the Civil Aviation Authority of Sri Lanka Act, No.34 of 2002 and the Civil Aviation Act, No.14 of 2010 so as to suit to the Civil Aviation Policy of the country, industry requirements and the emerging global trends in the Civil Aviation, since the applications, boundaries and limitations of the Aviation Industry are rapidly growing day by day. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft Bills to amend the said Acts, based on the recommendations of the Committee appointed to obtain recommendations in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Duties to be performed by Sri Lanka within the year 2024 after accepting the Chairmanship of the Indian Ocean Rim Association (IORA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12510",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka is required to organize several official meetings during the year 2024, after receiving the Chairmanship of the Indian Ocean Rim Association (IORA) which consists of 23 member countries bordering the Indian Ocean, for a period of 02 years. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to hold the following official meetings in Sri Lanka and to host the same, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\ni.\tHolding the 26th Meeting of the IORA Committee of the Senior Officials (CSO) on 30th and 31st May 2024.\n\nii.\tHolding the 27th Annual Committee of the Senior Officials (CSO) in November 2024.\n\niii.\tHolding the 24th meeting of the Council of Ministers (COM) in November 2024."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Introduction of a New Regulator for the Petroleum Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12509",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the importation, refining, distribution and sale of petroleum products including Gasoline, Gas oil, Kerosene, Aviation Fuel Oil, Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) and Lubricants operate within the existing legal framework, this sector lacks a comprehensive regulatory mechanism. As many private entities are also involved in the importation and distribution of petroleum products, the need for an independent, dynamic, effective and efficient regulatory mechanism has been recognized to address the challenges in the said sector, enhance product quality and protect the interests of consumers, investors and other stakeholders. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to appoint a Committee headed by the Secretary, Ministry of Power and Energy to study in that regard and make recommendations and prepare a legal framework for the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Providing Two (02) Land Lots located in Pitipana, Homagama to National School of Business Management Limited (NSBM)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12508",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The land in extent of 237 Acres which is known as Mahenawatta located at Pitipana in Homagama has been acquired by the Urban Development Authority with the intention of reserving lands for the development of science and technology sectors as per the concept of \u201cKnowledge Based Town\u201d which comes under the Homagama Town Development Plan. The proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to grant a portion of 14 Acres 03 Roods and 12.8 Perches and another portion of 20 Acres out of the above land for the construction of Phase II and phase III of National School of Business Management Limited respectively, to the said Institute, on long term lease basis, subject to charging the assessed value of the Chief Government Valuer, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Holding the First Conference of the Wetland Link International - Asia Oceania at Diyasaru Park, Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12507",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Wetland Link International (WLI) is an international support network for Wetland Education Centres which is led by the Wildfowl and Wetlands Trust (WWT) of the United Kingdom. WLI consists of 350 Wetland Education Centres across 06 continents. The Wetland Link International Asia has been established as a subsidiary to the WLI for the improvement of Wetlands in Asia and it comprises 100 member wetlands. In addition, WLI-Asia together with the Wetland Centers of Australia and New Zealand have formed the WLI-Asia Oceania. It has been proposed to hold the First Conference of the WLI - Asia Oceania in Colombo hosted by Diyasaru Park which is managed by the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation, together with Meetings, Incentives, Conferences and Exhibitions as a MICE Tourism Promotion Programme from 16 to 22 June 2024. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to hold and host the said Conference in Colombo with participation of 100 foreign delegations and 75 local groups, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Vesting the Land where the Negombo Eththukala Beach Park is located with the Urban Development Authority for the development of the said Park",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12506",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Eththukala Beach Park (Browns Beach) with an extent of 06 Acres 01 Rood 9.1 Perches is the only beach park in the Negombo Municipal Council area and it is located in the High-Density Promotional Tourism Zone of the Negombo Development Plan 2021\u20112030. The Negombo Municipal Council has decided to vest the management of the said Park with the Urban Development Authority with a view to converting the same as an attractive park for the local and foreign travelers. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to vest the said land with the  Urban Development Authority as a Free Grant as per the provisions of the State Land Ordinance in order to develop the same as a tourist zone in conformity with the relevant development plans, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Expansion of the Mindfulness Training Programme being implemented \tfor school children islandwide",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12505",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted on 2022\u201112\u201112 to implement the \"Programme for the Introduction of Mindfulness for School Children\" with a  view to creating calmness by avoiding the frequent complexity and stress developing in the minds of school children. Accordingly, this programme is being implemented  successfully in each school in the country over a period of one year. The proposal made by the Minister of Education to commemorate the day following the Vesak Day as the National Mindfulness Day annually, to implement the programme called \"Towards a Mindfulness Country from the Vesak Week' annually in future coinciding with the Vesak Week and to hold the 'International Mindfulness Conference' at the beginning of the Month of May in each year from the year 2024, as a step forward of the said Programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-25-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-04-25",
    "description": "Entering into Memoranda of Understanding/Agreements in view of Educational Collaboration",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12504",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Education to enter into the following  Memoranda of Understanding/Agreements between Sri Lankan Universities and Foreign Universities/Agencies with the objective of developing the higher educational collaboration, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tThe Memorandum of Understanding between the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka and the University of Salford, United Kingdom pertaining to fostering multidisciplinary research for disaster resilience and integrated natural resource management.\n\n*\tThe Tripartite Agreement among the University of Jaffna and the National University of Singapore and Singapore Health Services Pte. Ltd. to establish a Regional Collaborating Centre with the aim of coordinating global health efforts.\n\n*\tThe Memorandum of Understanding between the University of Ruhuna and the Southern Health NHS Trust of the United Kingdom and Northern Ireland pertaining to the MARIE Project on the mental health effects of menopause on women globally.\n\n*\tThe Memorandum of Understanding between the Open University of Sri Lanka and the Tomorrow Technology Education Service Center, China pertaining to the designation and empowerment of Tomorrow Technology Education Service Center as the duly authorized representative for the purpose of endorsing and marketing the academic programmes offered by the Open University of Sri Lanka to the students from China.\n\n*\tThe Memorandum of Understanding between the University of Sri Jayewardenepura and the Tomas Bata University in the Czech Republic to develop cooperation between the two parties.\n\n*\tThe Agreement between the Rajarata University of Sri Lanka and the University of Naples Federico II, Italy on capacity building, research collaborations, innovations and use of aquaculture biosystems technology."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
