    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Samastha Lanka\tSasanarakshaka Mandalaya and Vietnam Buddhist Sangha",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12503",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the Samastha Lanka Sasanarakshaka Mandalaya and Vietname Buddhist Sangha for further strengthening the existing cultural and religious relationship between Vietnam and Sri Lanka. The Draft Memorandum of Understanding for that purpose, has received the approval of the Minister of Foreign Affairs and the clearance of the Attorney General's Department. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to sign the said Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Introduction of Indicative Price for selected Essential Food Commodities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12502",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that even though the Sri Lankan Rupee is becoming appreciated against the US Dollar and some other foreign currencies, no reduction is observed in the retail price of the imported essential food commodities in the market. Also, there is a significant difference between the landed price and the retail price of the essential\timported food commodities. Under this situation, the Consumer Affairs Authority has taken steps to implement a programme to study the estimated market prices of selected essential food commodities and publish those prices as Indicative Prices weekly, on the guidance of the Ministry of Trade, Commerce and Food Security. Through this, the consumers will be able to buy the said food items by being\tvigilant of the market prices of those essential food commodities. The information submitted by the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security regarding the Indicative Prices of so selected 09 essential food commodities, was considered by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Sri Lanka Electricity Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12501",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2023-11-20 to publish the Sri Lanka Electricity Bill in the Government Gazette and submit it to Parliament for approval. After the promulgation of the said bill accordingly, views and suggestions have been received from the various stakeholders including the general public and it has been identified further amendments to be made to include appropriate provisions in the said Bill after evaluation of the said views and suggestions and to enable better reflection of the Government policy on reforms of the Electricity sector. The Attorney General's clearance has been received for the Electricity Bill which has been re-prepared by the Legal Draftsman incorporating also the amendments identified as such. Accordingly, The proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter submit it to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "\u201cNakathata Pelayak\u201d - National Tree Planting Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12500",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the 2024 Avurudu Nakath Seettuwa, the National Tree Planting Auspicious Time has been set as at 6.16 a.m. on April 18. The information presented by the Minister of Agriculture and Plantation Industries, mentioning that the steps are being taken to apprise the public to plant a perennial crop with an export potential or a perennial crop with a food value at that auspicious time and implement a programme for that purpose, was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Modernization of Automobile Workshops in Colleges of Technology and\tTechnical Colleges under the Grant Aid by Korea International Cooperation\tAgency of the Republic of Korea (KOICA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12499",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Korea International Cooperation Agency has provided financial assistance during the period 2013-2015 for the upgrading of 05 Automobile Technology courses in Maradana, Kandy, Bandarawela, Kegalle and Samanthurai Technical Colleges that are operated under the purview of the Department of Technical Education and Training. As the workshops have been in use for about 10 years now, their equipment needs to be repaired, updated and newly supplied. The Korea International Cooperation Agency has agreed to provide a grant assistance of US$ 75,500 for those tasks. The proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign the proposed Record of Discussion to be signed between the two parties for that purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Implementation of the proposed reforms of State-Owned Banks",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12498",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the weaknesses in the fields of governance, risk management and supervision of the state-owned banks, these banks had to face severe difficulties during the recent economic crisis. Therefore, with the aim of preventing the recurrence of such difficulties, a number of reforms to be carried out in those banks have been identified by an expert committee consisting of the members of the International Monetary Fund, World Bank and Central Bank of Sri Lanka. As a Structural Benchmark of the Extended Fund Facility Programme provided by the International Monetary Fund, as well as the basic activities under the Development Policy Operations implemented by the World Bank, the said reforms have to be implemented promptly. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to implement those reform proposals, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Revision of Security Deposits at Elections",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12497",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that it would be appropriate to update the existing limits of security deposits in a timely manner as per the present social, economic and political background, in terms of the provisions of the Presidential Elections Act, the Parliamentary Elections Act and the Provincial Councils Elections Act. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Hon. President and the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to revise the relevant security deposits as follows, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n    \u2022 Increasing the security deposit of a candidate from a recognized political party up to Rs. 2.6 million and the security deposit of an independent candidate up to Rs. 3.1 million, as per the the Presidential Elections Act No. 15 of 1981.\n      \n    \u2022 Increasing the security deposit of a candidate from a recognized political party up to Rs. 11,000/- and the security deposit of a candidate of an independent group up to Rs. 16,000/-, as per the Parliamentary Election Act, No. 1 of 1981.\n\n    \u2022 Increasing the security deposit of a candidate representing a recognized \tpolitical party up to Rs. 6,000/- and the security deposit of a candidate of an independent group up to Rs. 11,000/-, as per the Provincial Councils Elections Act, No. 2 of 1988."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Recruitment of 2,500 English Medium Teachers under the Programme on \t\"English for All\"",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12496",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified at an assessment conducted with regard to 765 schools the fact that although the existing approved cadre of teachers to teach GCE Ordinary Level subjects in English medium is 4,441, there is a requirement of 6,500 teachers for the purpose and many schools have expanded English medium teaching by making necessary arrangements in addition to the number of teachers currently employed. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Hon. President and the Minister of Education to increase the number of 765 schools where subjects are taught in English medium, up to 1,000 in the year 2024 and to increase the approved cadre of English medium subject teachers up to 6500 and recruit 2500 English medium teachers to fulfill the teacher requirement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Designating as Secondary Businesses of Strategic Importance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12495",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposals made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to designate the following Companies as Secondary Businesses of Strategic Importance and grant exemptions or incentives to such Companies from the Acts indicated under Schedule II of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, and to publish the Orders for the same through the Gazette Notifications, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n    \u2022 PORT CITY BPO (PRIVATE) LIMITED - to maintain a business for providing shared Business Process Outsourcing (BPO) services for the overseas entertainment industry.\n      \n    \u2022 IVIVA PTE LTD - to maintain a business for providing Information Technology services that develops Smart City IT - enabled products and solutions to support their diverse portfolio of global clients to transition to low-carbon economy.\n\n    \u2022 ECHELON TRADE (PVT) LTD - to maintain a business engaged with global trade of textiles, garments, luxury watches, gold and gems, electronics and cosmetics.\n\n    \u2022 99X TECHNOLOGY AS - to maintain a business in product engineering and innovations and providing services to global independent software vendors to formulate digital solutions to real user problems through web development, mobile development as well."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Submission of an Order under the Sri Lanka Export Development Act No. 40 of 1979 to Parliament for approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12494",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201105\u201129 has granted approval to resume the Sri Lanka's Tariff Liberalization Programme under the Sri Lanka - Singapore Free Trade Agreement. Taking into account the implementation of CESS Levy as at 2018\u201105\u201101, the said programme has been categorized into three categories as 'Category 0', 'Category 10' and 'Category X'. Accordingly, an Order under the provisions of the Sri Lanka Export Development Act No. 40 of 1979 has been published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2024\u201101\u201104 to give effect to remove the first annual installment of 1/5th of CESS Levy applicable on 1,087 HS Codes categorized under the 'Category 10' and for the single point removal of the CESS Levy applicable on 300 HS Codes categorized under the Category of \"0\". As such, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to submit the said Order to Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Establishment of Diplomatic Relations between the Sri Lanka and the Republic of Chad",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12493",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, Sri Lanka has established diplomatic relations with 46 countries in the African continent, and the Republic of Chad also has expressed its consent to establish diplomatic relations with Sri Lanka. The Republic of Chad, as a multilateral partner, has extended its support to Sri Lanka in the United Nations and other multilateral forums. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to establish diplomatic relations with the Republic of Chad, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Project for the establishment of Youth Agri-Entrepreneurship Villages to advance the Agriculture Modernization Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12492",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-04-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In view of attracting youth community to the agriculture and developing their economic status, it has been planned to implement the Project for establishing the Youth Agri-Entrepreneurship Villages to create a community of youth Agri-Entrepreneurs and to introduce the agriculture modernization to agricultural areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture and Plantation Industries to implement the Project for establishing the Agri-Entrepreneurship Villages by selecting one village each in the selected Divisional Secretariat Divisions in the year 2024 and to facilitate the young farming community to use new technology and smart technology, as its first phase, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-04-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-04-08",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka Institute of Biotechnology Private Limited (SLIBTEC) and the Monash University, Australia",
