    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Economic Transformation Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12471",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2024-03-04 to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare the Economic Transformation Bill. The Initial Draft for the Economic Transformation Act has been prepared including the main objectives of the National Policy on Economic Transformation and incorporating necessary provisions enabling the establishment of the key Institutions namely Economic Commission, Investment Zone Sri Lanka, Office for International Trade, Sri Lanka Institute of Economics and International Trade and National Productivity Commission, to support the Government to achieve those objectives.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare the Bill and submit expeditiously, incorporating the amendments submitted by the Attorney General, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "National Digital Economy Strategy for Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12470",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The necessity of National Digital Economy Strategies and implementation plan for the same has been identified in order to achieve the country's vision of becoming a high income economy by 2048 and reach anticipated results. Accordingly, the  \u201cNational Digital Economy Strategy for Sri Lanka - 2030\u201d has been prepared with the participation of experts in the field and consultation of the professional bodies and chambers. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Technology to implement the said strategy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Amendment of the National Minimum Wage of Workers Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12469",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the provisions of the National Minimum Wage of Workers Act, No.3 of 2016, the National Minimum Wage has been set as Rs.12,500/-. A triparte subcommittee consisting of trade unions and employees representing Small and Medium Entrepreneurs appointed on the recommendations of the National Labour Advisory Council, has recommended to increase the National Minimum Wage up to Rs.17,500/-. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment to amend the National Minimum Wage of Workers Act, No.3 of 2016, enabling to increase the National Minimum Wage by Rs.5000/- from Rs.12,500/- to Rs.17,500/- and National Minimum Daily Wage by Rs.200/- from Rs.500/- to Rs.700/-, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Repeal of the Prevention of Domestic Violence Act, No.34 of 2005",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12468",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2023-06-12 to publish the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman to amend the Prevention of Domestic Violence Act, No.34 of 2005 catering to the current needs in the Government Gazette and submit the same in Parliament for approval. However, since the amendments have to be made to a large number of sections in the Act, it deemed appropriate to repeal the current Act in effect and to formulate a new Act under the same title including all the relevant amendments, for the easy understanding of the public. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a new Act enabling to pursue action in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Repealing the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12467",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Special Commodity Levy has been imposed under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007 to charge a single composite levy to facilitate the importation of 64 goods classified under 210 HS Codes. Due to various issues arised during the implementation of the Levy, the necessity of repealing the said Levy Act has been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to repeal the said Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Submission of an Order to Parliament for approval as per the provisions of the Revenue Protection Act No.19 of 1962",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12466",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201105\u201129 has granted approval to resume the Sri Lanka's Tariff Liberalization Programme under the Sri Lanka - Singapore Free Trade Agreement. Accordingly, an Order has been published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2023\u201106\u201130 as per the provisions of the Revenue Protection Act No.19 of 1962 in order to eliminate the first annual installment of the Customs Import Duty imposed on 1,116 HS Codes classified with regard to Category 6 of the Tariff Liberalization Programme of the Sri Lanka - Singapore Free Trade Agreement, with effect from 2023\u201107\u201101. Approval of Parliament has also been received for the said Order on 2023\u201110\u201104. An Order has been published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2024\u201101\u201104 as per the provisions of the Revenue Protection Act No.19 of 1962 in order to remove the Customs Import Duty applicable for 1,222 HS Codes classified under the Category 6 of the Tariff Liberalization Programme for the implementation of the second phase of the said Programme. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the said Order to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Project for the establishment 70 MW, AC ground mounted solar PV power \tplants in 1 to 5 MW, AC capacity",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12465",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201110\u201102 has granted approval to award \tthe relevant contracts for the supply of 51MW to establish Solar PV Power \tPlants at 5 Grid Substations on Build, Own and Operate basis with 20 years \toperational period under the Project for establishment of 70MW, AC ground \tmounted Solar PV Power Plants in 1-5 MW AC capacity at 11 Grid \tSubstations. Proposals have been re-invited for the supply of 19 MW for the \tremaining 06 Grid Substations. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister \tof Power and Energy to award the contracts for the establishment of  Solar PV \tPower Plants at Ampara, Habarana, Kosgama, Kurunegala, Pannala and \tWeyangoda Grid Substations, to the relevant investors, as recommended by the \tCabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee taking into consideration the \tproposals submitted, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Hosting the International Conference conducted annually by the\tInternational Pepper Community, in Sri Lanka in the year 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12464",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Organization called the International Pepper Community has been established in the year 1972 jointly by the major pepper producing  countries in the world under the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia. Sri Lanka, India, Indonesia, Malaysia and Vietnam function as the major and permanent members of this Organization. Sri Lanka has obtained the permanent membership of the  International Pepper Community in the year 2002 and its annual International Conferences have been held in Sri Lanka in the years 1999, 2006, 2012 and 2017. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture and Plantation Industries to host the 52nd International Conference of the International Pepper Community in Sri Lanka in this year, with a view to reaching agreements pertaining to the fields of sharing the results of technological and economic research relating to the pepper production among the member countries, formulating and promoting programmes for traditional and new markets and building up collaboration for relaxing tariff and non tariff barriers in the international market, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Conferring the Expressways being in operation under the Road Development Authority to Sahasya Investments Ltd. (SIL)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12463",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2024\u201102\u201105 to separate the expressway network, expressway lands, expressway loans(local) and the staff from the Road Development Authority and assign them with Sahasya Investments Ltd., in order to be able to manage them in a more commercial manner and approval has been given for the Action Plan related thereto at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201102\u201105. Accordingly, Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways to transfer the day-to-day operations and management of the existing expressways to Sahasya Investments Ltd., under a formalized Management Agreement, to be effective from 2024\u201104\u201101 and to transfer all relevant assets to Sahasya Investments Ltd., within a period of 06 months after conducting a legal and a financial feasibility study which will be jointly carried out by the Road Development Authority and Sahasya Investments Ltd."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Improvement of training courses and other facilities of the Korea National Vocational Training Institute (K-TEC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12462",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka - Korean National Vocational Training Institute, Orugudawatta  was established under a financial assistance of Rs.2,900 million provided by the Export Import Bank of Korea. The Export Import Bank of Korea has agreed to grant a financial support of USD 1.5 million to further improve the courses conducted by the Institute and the existing facilities in the Institute. This project, which is proposed to be implemented within a period of 16 months, will facilitate the common requirements of all courses including Automobile Technology, CNC Manufacturing Technology, Welding Technology, Electrical Technology, Electronic Technology, Automation and Robotic Technology, Fluid Power Technology and Mechatronics Technology. The clearance of the Attorney General and the concurrence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Department of External Resources have been received for the draft Memorandum of Understanding to be signed between the two parties in order to implement the proposed project. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign the relevant  Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Promotion of registration of vessels under the Flag of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12461",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Registration of vessels is a major source of a large amount of foreign exchange inflow to the local economy and there is a potential to generate many direct and indirect employment opportunities. The proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to call for Expressions of Interest from eligible local and foreign institutions for promotion of the registration of vessels under the Flag of Sri Lanka, and to evaluate such proposals by a Technical Evaluation Committee and select the most suitable institution based on the recommendations of a Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-25-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-03-25",
    "description": "Designate CODEGEN INNOVATIONS (PRIVATE) LIMITED as a Secondary Business of Strategic Importance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12460",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-25 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- CODEGEN INNOVATIONS (PRIVATE) LIMITED is a company registered in Sri Lanka as a division of the CodeGen Group which specialises in technology solutions encompassing software, data science, design and hardware. The  Company has been approved as an authorized person by the Colombo Port City Economic Commission and the said Company has made a request to designate it as a Secondary Business of Strategic Importance. The Company has planned to make an initial investment of USD 500,000 and generate approximately USD 15 million within a period of 05 years and create approximately 400 job opportunities during that period. Therefore, as per the provisions of the Colombo Port City (Guidelines on the Grant of Exemptions or Incentives to Businesses of Strategic Importance) Regulations, No.02 of 2023, the said Company is eligible to be granted exemptions or incentives. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion for granting exemptions or incentives to CODEGEN INNOVATIONS (PRIVATE) LIMITED as per the provisions of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act and  publish an Order for the same, in the Government Gazette, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Importing eggs required for providing eggs to the consumers at a reasonable\tprice",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12459",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2023-12-18 to import eggs upto 2024-04-30 in order to maintain a stable price for eggs in the local market. Accordingly, approximately 18 million eggs have been imported so far and it has been calculated that another 42 million eggs should be imported for the needs during the festive season. Bids have been invited from the Indian companies recommended by the Department of Animal Production and Health to import the required quantity of eggs and the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to award the relevant procurements as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Approved Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Providing relief to Low-income families",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12458",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- At the beginning of the year 2023, arrangements were made by the Government to provide Nadu rice 10 kg for each family per month for a period of two months covering approximately 2.74 million families in 25 districts including Samurdhi beneficiaries. It has been observed that it is appropriate to implement the said programme in this year as well as\ta support to maintain the nutrition level of identified low-income families. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to implement the programme of providing 10 kgs of rice for one family per month for a period of two months covering approximately 2.74 million low-income families identified through District Secretaries/Government Agents with the involvement of Small and Medium Scale paddy millers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Awarding the Procurement for the implementation of Rooftop Solar Power\tprojects implemented in Religious places under Indian Government Funds",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12457",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2024-01-08 to install Rooftop Solar Power systems in religious places, under a loan facility of US$ 1,000 million granted by the State Bank of India, subject to a credit limit of US$ 17 million. Accordingly, bids have been invited to select a suitable institution to implement this project and 06 bids have been received. Taking into consideration the recommendation made by the Procurement Appeal Board on the recommendation submitted by the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Standing Cabinet Approved Procurement Committee, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to award the procurement of Implementation of  Rooftop Solar Power systems for a contract price of US$ 17 million to M/s Premier Energies Ltd, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Acceleration of Rural Development Programmes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12456",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Many development projects which were initiated at rural level had to be halted, due to the economic issues prevailed in the past few years. However, since the Government has already made a considerable investment for these projects, the said projects should be completed expeditiously and provide the anticipated benefits of the same to the rural community. It has been observed that the amount of provisions allocated under the Decentralized Budget Programme are not sufficient to carry forward the Rural Development Programmes which have already been halted midway in the relevant areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to provide allocation of another Rs. 2000 million under the Decentralized Budget Programme to re-implement the Development Projects that had to be halted in the midway at rural level and increase the provisions allocated for Special Development Initiatives of implemented under the supervision of the Presidential Secretariat by another Rs.1000 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Providing Fertilizer Subsidy to the farmers for Yala Season 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12455",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Fertilizer Secretariat has estimated that 110,298.1 MT, 27,711.1 MT and 33,412.4 MT of Urea, TSP and MOP chemical fertilizers respectively are required for paddy cultivation in Yala season 2024. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposals submitted by the Minister of Agriculture and Plantation Industries, the Cabinet decided the following:\n\n    \u2022 Importation of fertilizer for Yala season 2024 by the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Ltd. and Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Company Ltd. and sell them to the farmers at a concessionary price competitively with the Private sector. \n      \n    \u2022 Provision of an amount of Rs.15,000/- as a Financial subsidy per hectare for maximum of 2 hectares cultivated per farmer for paddy cultivation in Yala season 2024, by the Department of Agrarian Development.\n\n    \u2022 Direct remittance of the relevant financial subsidy to the bank accounts of the farmers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Establishment of an Inter-Ministerial Tourism Committee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12454",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since it has been identified that the present resurgence of Sri Lanka's Tourism industry plays a vital role towards the country's economic recovery and growth, it has been proposed through the Budget 2024, a number of steps including the implementation of a long term programme for the promotion of tourism sector and targeting at least 05 million tourists to the country per year. Owing to the multi\u2011faceted nature of the tourism industry and the distribution of various assets, laws and responsibilities among several Government institutions, It is essential to maintain an efficient coordination and collaboration among the relevant institutions to reap the expected benefits. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to establish an Inter-Ministerial Tourism Committee headed by the Secretary to the President with  the representations of the relevant Government institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Civil Procedure Code (Amendment) Bill (Issue and Service of summons)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12453",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted at the Cabinet meetings held on 2021\u201110\u201111 and 2023\u201107\u201131 to amend the Civil Procedure Code incorporating necessary provisions to improve the procedure for issuance and service of summons in relation to a civil proceeding by including the mode of service of summons via courier service and electronic mail as ordinary services and also another several amendments to suit with the present day needs. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received to the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman accordingly. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Amendment to the Primary Courts Procedure Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12452",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Primary Court, in respect of a dispute affecting land, take only preventive or provisional action pending the final adjudication on title or right to possession which is the function of a civil court. Since a Primary Court order prevails until a final decision is made by a District Court in determining rights and District Court action is subject to two appeals, inevitable delays occur and in this context, even a trespasser or a squatter would be able to remain in possession of the relevant land for an inequitable period of time. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to amend the  Primary Courts Procedure Act enabling to fulfill the objectives expected through section 66 of the Primary Courts Procedure Act, No. 44 of 1979  as amended by the Act No. 49 of 1980 more effectively, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Preparing a Bill to amend the Constitution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12451",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found necessary to change the existing electoral system to achieve the objectives of the Regulations of Election Expenditure Act No. 3 of 2023 and to ensure full realization of a democratic election. A Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee has been appointed to submit a Report with recommendations to the Cabinet after obtaining the views of all Party leaders representing Parliament and other relevant Parties for that purpose. They have expressed their views to the Committee to elect 160 out of the 225 Members of Parliament by the voters directly in the respective constituency and to elect the rest of 65 Members of Parliament at national or provincial level as per the proportional representation and the majority of participants have expressed their concurrence for that. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft necessary legislation to amend the Electoral system, taking also into consideration the recommendations submitted by the Committee appointed under the Chairmanship of Prime Minister, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-18-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-03-18",
    "description": "Amendment of the Sri Lanka Foundation Act, No.31 of 1973",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12450",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Foundation established under the Sri Lanka Foundation Act, No.31 of 1973 functions as a centre for training and awareness services related to sustainable development, social integrity, socio-economic development, good governance, entrepreneurship and democracy. As of now, the Sri Lanka Foundation conducts different courses from certificate level to higher national diploma level and the need has arisen to revise the aims and objectives as well as the powers and functions of the said Foundation so as to suit to the present day requirements. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to amend the  Sri Lanka Foundation Act, so as to be able to take action accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
