    "description": "Initiation of two floating solar power generation pilot projects with a \tcapacity of 1 MW each on the surface of Chandrika Wewa Reservoir and \tKiriibban Wewa Reservoir",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12426",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-04 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been decided to implement two (02) floating solar power pilot projects with a capacity of 1 MW each on the surface of the Chandrika Wewa Reservoir and the Kiriibban Wewa Reservoir as per the Record of Discussion signed between the Korea Institute for Advancement of Technology and the Ministry of Power and Energy in Sri Lanka. A request has been submitted seeking each of plots in extent of 0.99 hectares on the water surface of the Chandrika Wewa reservoir located at Embilipitiya Divisional Secretariat and Kiriibban Wewa Reservoir located at Sevanagala Divisional Secretariat and blocks of land in extent of 0.1 hectares each from land reserves of those reservoirs for the activities such as construction of power plants, transmission stations, training of maintenance workers and maintenance of solar panels in relation to those two (02) pilot Projects. The implementation of the proposed Project will enable  a feeding of about 03GWh annual electricity generation into the National Grid. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation to grant the aforesaid plots on the water surfaces and block of lands to the Sustainable Energy Authority of Sri Lanka on annual lease permits in order to maintain the relevant solar power generation pilot projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-03-04",
    "description": "International Counter Ransomware Initiative Summit",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12425",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-04 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tSri Lanka has also been invited to join the International Counter Ransomware Initiative, which the United States started in 2021 with a group of other countries as a forum to discuss international coordination to combat ransomware. As of now, 48 countries around the world, the European Union as well as the Interpol have joined the said initiative. Since Sri Lanka too has recently faced with negative experiences with  ransomware, it has been recognized that joining the international initiative against ransomware could accrue benefits. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Technology; and the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to join with the international Counter Ransomware Initiative and take further steps in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-04-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-03-04",
    "description": "Approval for Policy Framework for appointing  Public Customs Bonded Warehouses -  (Chapter 235)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12424",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-04 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Customs Bonded Warehouse is a storage facility used to ensure the safety and quality of goods prior to payment of applicable duties on imported goods and transportation of goods. Under the provisions of section 69 of the Customs Ordinance (Chapter 235), the Minister in charge of the subject of Finance on the recommendation of the Director General of Customs can appoint Customs Bonded Warehouses. Taking into account the development of warehousing technologies and the need to create competitive advantage in the supply chain process, it has been recognized that the mandatory minimum floor area of a public customs bonded warehouse should be revised. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies for the implementation of the \"Revised and Updated Policy Framework for appointing Public Customs Bonded Warehouses\" prepared under section 69 of the Customs Ordinance, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-04-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-03-04",
    "description": "Development of the Telecommunications Industry through Advancement of Information and Communication Technology (ICT) Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12423",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-04 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In line with Sri Lanka's Digital Economy Strategy, the need to develop the Telecommunications Industry through the improvement of Information and Communication Technology (ICT) education has been identified to foster economic growth and innovation, thereby enabling to create skilled professionals required for the sustainable development of the Telecommunications Industry. The Telecommunication Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka is empowered to utilize or disburse 50% of the Telecommunication Development Charge collected from the licensees for the development of the telecommunications industry. Accordingly, Cabinet approved the joint proposal made by Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Technology; and the Minister of Education to implement the \u201cSmart School Project\u201d enabling to provide required equipment for 1000 schools where Information Communication Technology is taught as a subject for the GCE (Advanced Level), from the provisions of the Telecommunication Development Charge Fund; and to initiate a scholarship programme to provide financial assistance to 5,000 students from low-income earning families studying ICT as a subject."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-03-04-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-03-04",
    "description": "Establishment of the Land Management Trust for regulation of the disposition of lands owned by the State and Government Statutory Institutions for investment purposes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12422",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-04 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The State owns around 82% of the total land extent of the country and safeguarding and controlling those lands is entrusted with a number of government institutions. It has been observed that various issues have arisen in  releasing State lands for investment purposes due to these institutions are not following an integrated approach. Therefore, in order to encourage opening up of new industries and services and investment opportunities that can create new employment opportunities, it is essential to establish a duly empowered mechanism from the point of identification of lands with suitable potentials to that of properly releasing lands to investors following a transparent procedure. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to establish the Land Management Trust comprising of the representatives of all relevant Ministries and Institutions under the Chairmanship of the Secretary to the President to submit appropriate recommendations pertaining to the release of lands owned by the State and Government Statutory Institutions, to investors, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-02-26-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-02-26",
    "description": "Amendment to the Recovery of Loans by Banks (Special Provisions) Act, No.4 of 1990",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12421",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-02-26 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the economic downturn prevailing over last 3 years, large scale, medium scale and small scale local businessmen have to encounter severe difficulties in running their businesses. Currently, the economy is getting stronger again to some extent and the necessary initial steps for that are being taken by the General Treasury. Nevertheless, various parties have pointed out that there are issues with regard to paying off the loans obtained by the small and medium scale businessmen from the banks in the past for their business activities. In this backdrop, banks are taking action to take over and auction the properties of a significant number of businessmen following the existing legal provisions, due to the default of loans by them. It has been observed that it would be appropriate to provide some grace period for the payment of the relevant loans alleviating the crisis situation that may arise in the business sector so as not to prejudice the banking system. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to temporarily suspend the methodology adopted by banks to take over the properties of debtors due to the default of loans up to 2024\u201112\u201115 and to amend section 4 of the Recovery of Loans by Banks (Special Provisions) Act, No.4 of 1990 to impose necessary legal provisions in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-02-26-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-02-26",
    "description": "Drafting the Public Financial Management Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12420",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-02-26 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201105\u201108 has granted approval to draft a new Fiscal Rules Framework and to incorporate the same to the proposed Public Financial Management Act. Accordingly, a preliminary draft has been prepared under the consultancy and the policy guidance of a Supervisory Committee appointed by the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies under the Co-Chairmanship of two Deputy Secretaries to the Treasury and including other Treasury Departments. As such the proposal made by the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare the Public Financial Management Bill based on the said preliminary draft and to authorize the Secretary to the Treasury to appoint a Committee of Experts to initiate the formulation of Financial Regulations until the proposed Bill is prepared by the Legal Draftsman, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
