    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-02-05",
    "description": "Accession to the 1988 Protocol of the International Convention for the Safety of Life at Sea, 1974 (SOLAS) and the 1988 Protocol of the International Convention on Load Lines, 1966 as amended in 2003",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12385",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-02-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka has contributed tremendously to the development of Sri Lanka as a Maritime Nation by ratifying 19 Maritime Conventions and Protocols over the past 40 years. Member States are required to comply with the Conventions of the International Maritime Organization  and in order to meet that requirement and to be able to include provisions for the 1988 Protocol of the International Convention for the Safety of Life at Sea, 1974 and the 1988 Protocol of the International Convention on Load Lines, 1966 as amended in 2003, measures have been taken to amend the Merchant Shipping Act, No.52 of 1971. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation Services to access to the aforesaid Protocols by depositing the instruments of accession documents through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs along with the depositories related to the Protocols, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-02-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-02-05",
    "description": "The United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) grant funded \tpromoting Autonomy, Literacy and Attentiveness through Market \tAlliances (PALAMA) Project in Sri Lanka - Phase II",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12384",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-02-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In 2018, the Government of the United States of America has provided a grant of US$ 26 million to Sri Lanka through the United States Department of Agriculture and the 'Save the Children' institute to implement the Promoting Autonomy, Literacy and Attentiveness through Market Alliances Project. The said project is due to be completed by the second quarter of 2024, and the Government of America has taken action to provide a grant of US$ 32.5 million through the 'Save the Children' institute to implement its second phase. It has been planned to implement the second phase of the said project aiming to  bridge the short-term resource gaps within the Government-run \u201cSchool Meals Programme\u201d, improve the reading outcomes and literacy of school age children, promote good health and hygiene across schools and communities, strengthening of support systems and capacity building for sustainability. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, to implement the said project after entering into a Memorandum of Understanding between the relevant parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-02-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-02-05",
    "description": "Strategy to promote Inclusive and Sustainable Businesses to achieve the\tSustainable Development Goals in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12383",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-02-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Purpose-driven enterprises that use commercially viable models to generate positive social and environmental impact ranging from green businesses and social enterprises to models empowering vulnerable communities are called Inclusive and Sustainable Businesses (ISBs). The inadequate access to information, skills training, partnerships, financial facilities and formal recognition for the existing Inclusive and Sustainable Businesses in Sri Lanka has constrained the growth and the positive impact of those businesses. As such, in supporting and facilitating the development of Inclusive and Sustainable Businesses, the need for specific strategies has arisen to integrate the provisions related to the promotion of Inclusive and Sustainable Businesses with the government policies related to national business, industry, finance and investment. Accordingly, the Sri Lanka Sustainable Development Council, with the support of the Trade, Investment and Innovation Division of the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UNESCAP) has obtained the views of all relevant parties and formulated \u201cStrategy to promote Inclusive and Sustainable Businesses to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals in Sri Lanka\". The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to implement the said strategy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
