  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "Amendments to the Penal Code",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12364",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meetings held on 2021\u201101\u00ad\u201118 and 2021\u201106\u201128 to introduce amendments to the Penal Code in order to amend the law on statutory rape in the Penal Code and fill the gaps in the law of rape and make the rape of boys a heinous crime. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "Amendments to the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No.15 of 1979",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12363",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Upon the recognition that it is not fair for the accused or appellants to languish in custody for a long period of time in addition to their period of sentence owing to the law's delays, approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the Meeting held on 2023\u201102\u201120 to amend the sections 323(5) and 333(5) of the Code of Criminal Procedure, enabling to be considered the time spent in custody by the accused/appellant be remitted from the period of imprisonment required under his jail sentence. Accordingly, a Bill has been drafted by the Legal Draftsman and the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the same. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "Amendments to the Bills of Exchange Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12362",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Some of the provisions of the Bills of Exchange Ordinance No. 25 of 1927, which is currently in force, have raised some contentious issues, while some other provisions have become obsolete. Therefore, a Committee has been appointed under the chairmanship of President's Counsel Mr. Nihal Jayawardene to obtain recommendations on the amendments to be made to the Bills of Exchange Ordinance in order to clarify and improve the law of negotiable instruments. The joint proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies and the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, based on the recommendations containing in the Report submitted by the said Committee, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to amend the  Bills of Exchange Ordinance No. 25 of 1927, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "Obtaining the support of the Fleming Fund of the United Kingdom to implement the National Strategic Plan on Combating Antimicrobial Resistance for Sri Lanka (2023-2028)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12361",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Antimicrobial Resistance has been identified as one of the top 10 public health threats faced by humans. In 2019, the World Health Organization has estimated that annually 1.27 million deaths are directly caused by drug-resistant bacteria due to the effect of antimicrobial resistance and 4.95 million deaths are associated with drug-resistant bacteria. In addition, the World Health Organization has recognized that antimicrobial resistance causes significant economic costs to the countries. Under this backdrop, the Fleming Fund aid programme managed by the Department of Health and Social Care of the United Kingdom supports about 25 countries in Africa and Asia to deal with antimicrobial resistance. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to take necessary action to implement the National Strategic Plan on Combating Antimicrobial Resistance 2023-2028 with the support of the Fleming Fund under that grant programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "The Cooperation Agreement between the Ministry of Health of Sri Lanka and the Latter-day Saint Charities (LDSC), United States of America",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12360",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the provisions of the Agreement reached between the Ministry of Health and the Latter-day Saint Charities of the United States of America in order to obtain special wheelchairs for persons with spinal cord injuries, Sri Lanka has received a consignment of wheelchairs and other mobility aids as  donations. Upon a request made by the Ministry of Health considering the severe shortage of oncology pharmaceuticals existed during the recent past, the Latter-day Saint Charities has agreed to supply a stock of 13 types of such drugs to Sri Lanka as a donation through the registered suppliers of the National Medicines Regulatory Authority. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence to pursue action, based on the facts presented by the Minister of Health regarding the acceptance of the relevant donation, following the accepted procedure."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "Vesting the National Cinnamon Research and Training Center at Palolpitiya, Thihagoda, with the Department of Cinnamon Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12359",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201108\u201114 has granted approval to establish a new Department in the name of he Department of Cinnamon Development with effect from 2023\u201109\u201101. It has been identified that it would be appropriate to vest the National Cinnamon Research and Training Centre  falling under the purview of the Department of Export Agriculture at present with the newly established  Department of Cinnamon Development for its research activities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture and Plantation Industries to vest the National Cinnamon Research and Training Centre and its all assets as well as all functions and duties carried out by  National Cinnamon Research and Training Centre, with the Department of Cinnamon Development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "Obtaining technical assistance under the \"Sustainable Consumption and \tProduction Outreach\" implemented by the German Development \tCooperation (GIZ)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12358",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'Promoting public procurement practices that are sustainable in accordance with national policies and priorities' has been included as 7th sustainable development target under 'Ensuring Responsible Consumption and Production' identified as the 12th sustainable development goal by the United Nations. The Cabinet has previously granted approval for the National Policy on Green Procurement prepared to formally and adequately incorporate the green elements to the Government procurement process and to the National Framework on Eco\u2011Labeling prepared to implement for facilitating the identification of trustworthy green goods and services and for minimizing the practice of 'green washing' in the market. The German Development Cooperation has agreed to provide technical assistance under the 'Sustainable Consumption and Production Outreach' implemented in several Asian countries, for programmes scheduled to be implemented under the said policies. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to enter into an Implementation Agreement between the Ministry of Environment and the German Development Cooperation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-24-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-01-24",
    "description": "Signing of the Sri Lanka Thailand Free Trade Agreement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12357",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Improving the supply capacity, attracting export oriented Foreign Direct Investments and broadening market access for Sri Lankan goods and services have been identified as strategies to be essentially adopted for the growth of Sri Lankan economy. Accordingly, the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2018.01.16 has granted approval to initiate negotiations to enter into a Free Trade Agreement  with Thailand which is a largest economy and a largest outward investor in the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN). During the process of negotiations, the National Trade Negotiation Committee has consulted all relevant local stakeholders as well. Clearance of the Attorney General and the concurrence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have been received for the complete draft Free Trade Agreement containing Preamble and 14 Chapters with Annexes which include enhancing trade and investments, conformity for domestic laws and regulations and facilitating the knowledge transfer, prepared after nine rounds of negotiations held between Sri Lanka and Thailand. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to sign the proposed Sri Lanka - Thailand Free Trade Agreement between both parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Increase of the Cost of Living Allowance of the Government Employees",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12356",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government had planned, through the Budget Proposals of the year 2024, to increase the Cost of Living Allowance of the government employees by Rs. 10,000/- from the month of January 2024 and to grant the said allowance from April 2024. Owing to the current difficult economic situation, various parties have requested to grant at least a part of that allowance within the first couple of months of the year. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to grant 50% of the increased Cost of Living Allowance viz. Rs. 5000/- to all government employees from the month of January 2024 and to increase some allowances paid to the Medical Officers and University Lectures, taking into account the pressure created by the economic situation prevailing in the country, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Project for the Development of the Torrington Hockey Ground",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12355",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Construction activities of the synthetic hockey playground located in Torrington have been carried out in the year 2009 and the turf of the said playground has become unfit for sports due to the expiration of time and the excessive use. The Asian Hockey Federation is in agreement to provide a synthetic hockey turf for the said playground free of charge. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Sports and Youth Affairs  to obtain the synthetic turf required for the Torrington Hockey Ground from the Asian Hockey Federation and to develop the said playground in accordance with  the international standards, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Poison, Opium and Dangerous Drugs (Disposal of court productions) Regulations of 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12354",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under subsection (6) of section 77A of the Poison, Opium and Dangerous Drugs Ordinance, the Minister in charge of the subject of Justice has been vested with powers to prescribe by Regulations, the mechanism of disposal of court productions including a drug, substance, article or a preparation, with the concurrence of the Judicial Service Commission. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to submit  the Poison, Opium and Dangerous Drugs (Disposal of court productions) Regulations of 2023 published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No. 2360/21 dated 2023\u201111\u201127, prescribing the mechanism of disposal of court productions including drug, substance, article or preparation as per the parameters of the law, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Rehabilitation of 100,000 km of Alternative Roads, Bypasses and Rural Roads",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12353",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to improve 1,500 km of roads out of roads where the constructions have been initiated under the 100,000 km programme and  suspended at present, in the year 2024, to maintain the safety and transport compatibility. Rs. 20 billion has been estimated as the total cost for that purpose and it is scheduled to be completed the works within six (06) months in the year 2024. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways to implement the programme to make the selected roads suitable for transportation, within the period of first six months in the year, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Awarding of contract for Ground Handling Services of SriLankan Airlines Limited at Tokyo-Narita Airport (NRT), Japan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12352",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited following the limited international bidding procedure for the selection of a suitable service provider to provide ground handling services for the aircrafts of SriLankan Airlines Limited at Tokyo-Narita Airport, Japan and accordingly, 02 bids have been received. The proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the contract for the supply of  ground handling services at Tokyo-Narita Airport, Japan from 2024\u201108\u201101 to 2027\u201107\u201131, to  International Air Cargo Terminal Co. Ltd, the lowest evaluated substantially responsive bidder, as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Cooperation programme for 2023-2025 between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Turkmenistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12351",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Turkmenistan have agreed to sign a Cooperation Programme for the period from 2023 to 2025. The objectives of this Cooperation Program are to promote, strengthen and expand bilateral relations including political, economic and cultural cooperation between the two countries, as well as focusing on issues of  mutual interest. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to implement the proposed Cooperation Programme between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Turkmenistan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Re-opening of Sri Lanka Missions/Posts abroad",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12350",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified the need of re-opening the following Sri Lankan Missions which were temporarily closed during the period of 2021/2022 :\n\n\t(i)\tSri Lanka Consulate General in Cyprus, Nicosia,\n\t(ii)\tSri Lanka Embassy in Baghdad, Iraq,\n\t(iii) \tSri Lanka Consulate General in Frankfurt, Germany.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to re-open the above-mentioned Sri Lankan Missions/Posts abroad, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Establishment of a Sri Lankan Embassy in Astana, Kazakhstan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12349",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to further develop the existing diplomatic relations between Kazakhstan and Sri Lanka, it has been recognized that it is appropriate to establish a Sri Lankan Embassy in Astana, Kazakhstan. The establishment of the  Secretariat of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia (CICA) in Kazakhstan and Sri Lanka being a member of that Conference provide Sri Lanka a great opportunity to engage with the Central Asian Region. Also, since there it indicates a significant increase in tourist arrivals from Kazakhstan to Sri Lanka, the establishment of an embassy of Sri Lanka in Astana will help to further promote tourism and cultural cooperation between the two countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to establish the proposed Sri Lankan Embassy in Astana, Kazakhstan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Establishment of new Investment Zones",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12348",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the Budget Speech 2022, it was emphasized the need to create an integrated mechanism between the public and private sectors to build up an export-oriented economy. Accordingly, it has been identified the appropriateness of developing the new Investment Zones as follows.\n\n    \u2022 Establishment of new Investment Zones in the Northern, Eastern, North-Western and Southern Provinces.\n    \u2022 Establishment of new Investment Zones in Mankulam, Paranthan Chemicals Company premises and Kankesanthurai Cement Corporation premises. \n    \u2022 Establishment of new Investment Zones in Iranawila and Trincomalee areas.\n    \u2022 Expansion of the existing Investment Zones in Bingiriya and Hambantota.\n\nThe Asian Development Bank has agreed to provide technical assistance for the establishment of the proposed economic zones. Accordingly,  the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to develop the said Investment Zones based on a suitable Public-Private Partnership model, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Establishment of a University of Science and Teachnology in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12347",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the objective of preparing the foundation to create a cadre of skilled\tprofessionals to take the leadership in critical sectors of new scientific \tdiscoveries, technological  innovation and sustainable development, it has been \tidentified the appropriateness of establishing a University of Science and \tTechnology in collaboration with a renowned university in United States of \tAmerica. Such a university will cater to utilize cutting-edge methodologies, \tfoster global \tacademic connections and create an environment for research and \tdevelopment. The  proposal made by the Hon. President to select one partner \tuniversity from among several identified universities including UC Berkeley, \tUC Riverside, UC Davis, University of Michigan and establish the proposed \tUniversity of Science and Technology as a Public-Private Partnership in \tcollaboration with the said university, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "The Anuradhapura Maha Vihara Development Plan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12346",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since the Maha Viharaya in Anuradhapura is a place with significant religious and historical importance in Sri Lanka, it has been identified the need to implement the exploration and conservation activities of the Maha Viharaya in a formal manner within a specific time frame. Accordingly, upon the notification of Hon. President,  Prof. Robbin Coningham, a senior foreign expert with international experience in the field of archaeology has submitted a project report on implementation of  the exploration, excavation and conservation project of the Maha Vihara. Through the said project report, it has been proposed to implement this project within a time period of 6 years from 2024 to 2029. The proposal made by the Hon. President to implement the exploration, excavation and conservation activities of the Maha Viharaya as per the project report of Prof. Robbin Coningham, jointly by the Presidential Secretariat and the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural affairs under the direct supervision of the Department of Archaeology and the Central Cultural Fund, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
