    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Overcrowding in prisons in Sri Lanka has been identified as a long-standing problem. As a remedy to that problem, a Committee headed by a Judge of the Supreme Court has been appointed to make suitable recommendations to introduce legal provisions to detain in appropriate cases suspects and convicts under House Arrest as an alternative to remand/imprisonment. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to introduce appropriate laws, based on the Report submitted by the said Official's Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Amendments to the Partition Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12302",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201109\u201125 has granted approval to introduce appropriate amendments to the Partition Act in order to conclude the partition cases expeditiously. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman accordingly. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Amending the Schedule VIII of the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance No.2 of 1937",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12301",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- More than 680 plant species belonging to 121 genera have been declared as protected plants in accordance with the plant classification systems coming under the Schedule VIII of the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance No.2 of 1937 as was last amended by the Fauna and Flora Protection (Amendment) Act No.7 of 2022. However, the necessity to amend the said Schedule to suit the current day needs has been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Resources Conservation to appoint a Committee consisting of experts in the fields of plant taxonomy and nomenclature, ecology, wildlife conservation and ethanobotany and to amend the Schedule VIII of the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance as per the recommendations of the said Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Conducting an investigation over the assassination of Mr. Edward Henry\tPedris 108 years ago by a judgment of the Colonial Military Court",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12300",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mr. Edward Henry Pedris who was 27 years at the time, has been brought before a Court Martial on charges of inciting riots and treason against the Government by the colonial administration of Sri Lanka and convicted of treason and executed on 1915\u201107\u201107 without considering any appeal. The body of the late Mr. Henry Pedris has been cremated in an undisclosed premise following the procedure prescribed for the cremation of a convicted criminal under the Martial Law. His assassination has been later identified as a result of a plan carried out by the senior officers who administered the country at that time. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. President to appoint a committee comprising of three members which is chaired by retired Supreme Court Judge Mr. Anil Goonaratne, to disclose actual information related to the said execution, study relevant information and submit a Report with recommendations to the Cabinet in order to bring justice to him."
  },
  {
