    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the Constitution, the Government of Sri Lanka is obliged to 'assure all persons' right to universal and equal access to education at all levels to eradicate the illiteracy'. Since providing all the facilities by the Government for the said task is practically difficult, the support of the other parties is also obtained for that. Accordingly, since the year 2005, the Ministry of Education has been implementing the Reading Development Programme and Girls' Education Programme together with the Room to Read organization. As of now, it has been planned to further expand the said programme and implement within a period of five (05) years to be effective from 2023\u201112\u201101, and for that purpose, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to enter into a new Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Education and the Room to Read organization, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-10-30",
    "description": "Entering into Agreements by the Open University of Sri Lanka on highe education cooperation and on the establishment of the Chinese Language Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12237",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been agreed to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Shanghai Open University of China and the Open University of Sri Lanka for higher education cooperation aiming to promote international cooperation, scholarly collaboration and cultural interaction and friendship and to sign a tripartite agreement among the Open University of Sri Lanka, Shanghai Open University and the Bank of China Ltd., pertaining to the establishment of a Chinese Language Centre under the fields of collaboration under the said MoU. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to enter into relevant agreements to be valid for a period of five (05) years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-10-30",
    "description": "Drafting a new Employment Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12236",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Concept Paper prepared by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment having discussed with the Trade unions, Employers and relevant stakeholders in order to draft a new Employment Act so as to suit to the current requirements, was taken up for discussion at the Cabinet Meeting held on 2023\u201108\u201107. At the said Cabinet Meeting, it was decided to refer the said Concept Paper to the Trilateral Committee which is functioning under the Prime Minister's Office representing Employers, Employees and the Government, to further discuss in that regard with all relevant stakeholders and submit recommendations. Accordingly, the said Committee chaired by the Hon. Prime Minister submitted a Report with recommendations regarding the matters that need the attention of the Cabinet having studied the Concept Paper, to the attention of the Cabinet and thereafter, it was decided to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill based on the said recommendations and the Concept Paper submitted by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment pertaining to this matter."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Construction of a floating solar photovoltaic (PV) power plant in the water\tsurface of Samanala Wewa Reservoir",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12235",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Generation of solar power energy on the surface of reservoirs through the construction of floating solar power plants deemed as a better alternative for land limited countries. Accordingly, it has been identified that there is a good potential on the surface of the reservoirs that are under the purview of Ceylon Electricity Board and the Mahaweli Authority of Sri Lanka, to implement solar energy generation projects and have confirmed that there is a possibility of utilizing approximately 100 Hectares of the water surface of Samanala Wewa Reservoir under Ceylon Electricity Board for the construction of a floating solar photovoltaic (PV) power plant of 150-200 MW.  Accordingly,  the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to call requests for proposals from the interested proponents to construct and implement the proposed solar power plant adhering to National Procurement Guidelines applicable for the implementation of infrastructure projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "The Grant assistance provided by the Government of Japan for the development of the\tFisheries Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12234",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Japan has agreed to provide a grant of Japanese Yen 200 million (approximately LKR 435 Million) under the Economic and Social Development Programme of the Government of Japan, with the objective of developing cold chain facilities and empowering the fisheries sector with modern electrical equipment to ensure a high value addition to the marine products to upgrade the living standard of the fishermen in the Northern and Eastern Provinces of Sri Lanka. It is expected to secure ice making machines for the Department of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources, digital platform scales for Ceylon Fishery Harbours Corporation, fishing nets for the National Aquaculture Development Authority, prefabricated refrigerators/freezers and refrigerator Cargo trucks for the Ceylon Fisheries Corporation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to obtain the said grant assistance and to enter into the respective agreements thereto, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Amendment of the Shop and Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act, No.19 of 1954 to meet the current needs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12233",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted its approval at the meeting held on 2022\u201108\u201108 to amend  the Shop and Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act, No.19 of 1954 in a manner that enables the women employed at night in offices engaged in information technology based businesses, knowledge process outsoucing businesses, business process outsourcing institutions and offices which handle accounting,\tadministrative and technical work for the business organizations located in the other\tcountries.  The Shop and Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) (Amendment) Bill prepared  accordingly by the Legal Draftsman has received the clearance of the Attorney General. The proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, submit it to Parliament for approval,was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Amendment to the Powers of Attorney Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12232",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Steps had been taken to amend the Powers of Attorney Ordinance by the Act, No.28 of 2022, with the objective of preventing fraudulent activities committed by the Power of Attorney holders relating to lands. Subsequent to the enforcement of the said amendments, several legal complications have arisen especially on the foreign Powers of Attorney, cancellation and revocation of Powers of Attorney and the time period given to register a Power of Attorney prepared before the enforcement of the respective amendments.  Therefore, the approval was granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2023\u201105\u201108 to prepare a Bill to further amend the Powers of Attorney Ordinance. The Powers of Attorney (Amendment) Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman as per the said approval,  has received the clearance of the Attorney General. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, submit it to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Amending the Sri Lanka Transport Board Act No.27 of 2005",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12231",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The necessity of amending the certain provisions in the Sri Lanka Transport Board Act No.27 of 2005 has been identified taking into consideration the need of making adequate legal provisions to take legal action against offenses committed by passengers and other parties depriving of revenue to be received by the Sri Lanka Transport Board and new reforms and trends which have taken place in the passenger transport service after introducing the Sri Lanka Transport Board Act, No.27 of 2005.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to amend the Sri Lanka Transport Board Act, No.27 of 2005, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Amending the Motor Traffic Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12230",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201106\u201105 has granted approval to implement the recommendations of the Report submitted by the Officials' Committee appointed under the Chairmanship of the Secretary to the Prime Minister to examine the matters relating to the implementation of the e-Motoring Project and submit recommendations to the Cabinet. It has been identified the necessity of amending the the Motor Traffic Act as appropriate to provide for necessary interim provisions for the implementation of the said Project and for matters incidental. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Acting Minister of Transport and Highways to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill for the said purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Establishment of an Independent Parliamentary Standards Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12229",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Ensuring accountability, credibility, clarity and professionalism of Members of Parliament are essential factors in enhancing the public trust in the efficacy, transparency and equity of the legislature. Therefore, Members of Parliament should, at all times, exercise their powers, privileges, functions and duties with probity and integrity. Taking into consideration that there is a mechanism for the implementation of a Code of Conduct for the Members of Parliament in most countries in the world and and for monitoring such activities, It has been identified the necessity of establishing an independent institution for preparing a Code of Conduct for the Members of Parliament in this country as well and for monitoring the same. Accordingly, the proposal jointly submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister and the Minster of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to obtain the views of the Speaker of Parliament and all Party Leaders on the initial draft prepared for the above purpose and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to formulate a Bill taking also into account the said views, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Signing a Memorandum of Understanding between the International Centre for Migration Policy Development and the Ministry of Labour and Foreign Employment",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12228",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish a Migrant Resource Centre in the Eastern Province for providing adequate, timely, reliable information and guidance to migrants, returned migrants and prospective migrants to enable them to make informed decisions to reduce the risks and challenges they face when traveling, working and living abroad, and the Government of New Zealand has expressed its willingness to grant required assistance for the purpose. Accordingly, the Government of New Zealand has agreed to provide a grant of 350,000 New Zealand dollars for the implementation of the proposed project by the International Center for Migration Policy Development through the Ministry of Business, Innovation and Employment of New Zealand. The proposal made by the Minister of Labor and Foreign Employment to sign a memorandum of understanding between the International Center for Migration Policy Development in New Zealand and the Ministry of Labor and Foreign Employment of Sri Lanka in order to establish the proposed Centre, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding between the National \tArchives of \tSri Lanka and the National Archives of the Netherlands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12227",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Archives of about 310 liner meters consisting of approximately 7,500 volumes created by the Dutch East India Company, which have been included in the Memory of the World Register by UNESCO recognizing the importance of the same for the study of both Asian history and world history are in the custody of the National Archives of Sri Lanka. Under 04 joint Agreements entered into between  the  National Archives of Sri Lanka and the National Archives of the Netherlands during the period from 2001 to 2013, 1,701 copies of negative microfilms of 5066 volumes have been sent to the Netherlands and microfilms made using them have been preserved by the National Archives of Sri Lanka at present. It has been proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding Concerning Archives Cooperation for a period of five years from 2024 to 2028 to continue this cooperation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to sign the relevant Memorandum of Understanding between the National Archives of the Netherlands and the National Archives of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Extension of the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Ministry of Education and the Peace Corps of the United States of America",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12226",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Peace Corps programmes supported by the United States Congress have been implemented in Sri Lanka during the periods from 1962 - 1964, 1983 - 1998 and 2004 - 2006. According to a memorandum of understanding signed between the Ministry of Education and the Peace Corps in 2018, a consensus has been reached between the two parties to implement a programme to improve English language education in Sri Lanka by providing volunteers for a period of five (05) years. However, due to the Easter Sunday attack and the Covid\u201119 pandemic situation, Peace Corps has not been able to implement the programme as scheduled. Since the Peace Corps has now agreed to re-implement the said programme in Sri Lanka, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to extend the MoU signed between the two parties for a further period of 05 years with effect from August 2023, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Implementation of Enhancing Small and Medium-sized Enterprises Finance Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12225",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the financial assistance of the Asian Development Bank amounting to US$ 165 million, the Government has implemented the 'Small and Medium sized Enterprises Line of Credit Project' to provide investment and working capital loans to small and medium sized entrepreneurs, at concessionary interest rates. Also, the necessary steps have been taken to establish the National Credit Guarantee Institution as a solution to the issues faced by small and medium sized entrepreneurs, owing to the banks giving priority to collateral\u2011based lending rather than cash flow\u2011based lending. The Government has planned to implement a new project called 'Enhancing Small and Medium\u2011sized Enterprises Finance Project' for entrepreneurs who have found it more difficult to secure funds for their businesses, and for the purpose, the Asian Development Bank has agreed to provide funds of US$ 100 million. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to obtain the said loan and to enter into related agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-23-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-10-23",
    "description": "Implementation of short term strategies for the promotion of Tourism Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12224",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Many Asian tourist destinations have entered into a tough competition to regain the tourism market share diminished in the wake of Covid\u201119 pandemic and many countries are taking measures to grant visas to tourists free of charge.  Therefore, several new tourism promotion programmes have been planned to implement for the revival of the tourism industry of Sri Lanka, which experienced a setback owing to the Easter Sunday attack, the Covid\u201119 pandemic and the subsequent severe economic downturn. Accordingly, with the objective of increasing the number of tourists visiting Sri Lanka to 05 million during the next 03 years, the Cabinet approved the following proposals jointly submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister, Minister of Tourism and Lands, Minister of Foreign Affairs and the Minister of Public Security.\n\ni. \timmediate implementation of a  programme to issue free visa for the tourists from China, India, Russia, Thailand, Indonesia, Malaysia and Japan for the period up to 2024\u201103\u201131, as a pilot project.  \n\nii. \tProviding the opportunity for tourists to purchase a one-time ticket package at the airport or through online platforms for all locations where fees are levied, enabling them to access the world heritage sites seamlessly and unobstructedly.\n\niii. \tProviding the opportunity to purchase tickets for tourist compartments of the Sri Lanka Railways via online platforms or at the airport itself as a unified ticket."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Extension of Sri Lanka - Australia Trade and Investment Framework\tArrangement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12223",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Australia is an important Foreign Direct Investment partner of Sri Lanka and the 5th source of tourist arrival destinations. The Trade and Invetment Framework Arrangement has been signed between Sri Lanka and Australia on 2017-11-02 with the perspective of enhancing bilateral trade and investment relations between the two countries. The proposal made by the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security to extend the said Agreement for the next five (05) years from 2023-10-10 enabling the continuous maintenance of trade and investment cooperation as mentioned in the said agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Investment Promotion and the National Development and Reform Commission of the People's Republic of China",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12222",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Development and Reform Commission of the People's Republic of China and the Ministry of Investment Promotion of Sri Lanka has expressed their concurrence to enter into an Memorandum of Understanding in order to promote production capacity and investment cooperation between the two parties. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to sign the said Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "National Hydrographic Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12221",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023-05-08 has granted approval to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to impose required provisions to develop a Maritime Hydrographic Unit with the objective of improving Sri Lanka as the Marine Center of South Asia region. The Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman accordingly has received the clearance of the Attorney General. The Joint proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence and the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, submit it to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Bill titled as 'Secured Transactions'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12220",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2018-06-19 has granted approval to repeal the Secured Transactions Act, No. 49 of 2009 and introduce a fresh Act imposing provisions to establish the Secured Transaction Registration Authority and amend the  Acts concurrently as follows. \n\n    \u2022 Prescription (Amendment) Bill\n    \u2022 Trust Receipts (Amendment) Bill\n    \u2022 Mortgage (Amendment) Bill\n    \u2022 Finance Leasing (Amendment) Bill\n    \u2022 Inland Trust Receipts (Amendment) Bill\n    \u2022 Companies (Amendment) Bill\n    \u2022 Registration of Documents (Amendment) Bill\n\nAccordingly, the Secretary, Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies has been instructed at the Cabinet meeting held on 2021-05-03 to examine further on Bills prepared by the Legal Draftsman along with the relevant authorities. The relevant Bills have been updated by the Legal Draftsman and have received the clearance of the Attorney General. The proposal made by the Hon.President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to publish the said Bills in the Government Gazette and thereafter, submit them to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Enactment of the Microfinance and Credit Regulatory Authority Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12219",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2021\u201103\u201123 to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill to repeal the Microfinance Act, No.6 of 2016 and enact the Microfinance and Credit Regulatory Authority. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Formulation of the National Land Commission Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12218",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the Appendix II of the List 1 of the Ninth Schedule to the Thirteenth Amendment to the Constitution, provisions have been made that a Land Commission should be established. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism and Lands to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill, based on the preliminary draft prepared for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "En-route Navigation Facility Charges Regulations No.01 of 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12217",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- En-route Navigation Facility Charges Regulations have been promulgated in 1981, \tenabling to impose an En-route Navigation Facility Charge for the aircraft navigating through the Colombo Flight Information Region. Those regulations have not been \tamended during last period of years. Therefore, taking into account the Convention on International Civil Aviation Policies and the current global trends, En-route Navigation Facility Charges Regulations have been amended \tand said new regulations have been published as En-route Navigation Facility Charges Regulations No.01 of 2023 through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2319/64 and dated 2023\u201102\u201116. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to table the Regulations so published, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Conducting outer boundary survey and preparation of boundary maps of the estates managed under the Regional Plantation Companies, Sri Lanka State Plantation Corporation and Janatha Estates Development Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12216",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The project for conducting outer boundary survey and preparation of boundary maps of the estates managed under the Regional Plantation Companies, Sri Lanka State Plantation Corporation and the Janatha Estates Development Board has been commenced in 2018 and surveying has been done covering a considerable extent of the relevant lands. The proposal made by the Minister of Industries to extend the said project until 2027, enabling to cover the remaining extent of lands that remains to be surveyed, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Payment of compensation for the damaged crops in the Yala Season 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12215",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approximately 58,770 acres of paddy and other crops have been damaged in the Yala Season 2023 due to the inability to supply of adequate water upon the adverse weather condition which prevailed recently thereby affecting about 53,965 farmers. Accordingly, the Cabinet, taking into consideration a proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture pertaining to the payment of compensations to the farmers so affected, decided to allocate necessary provisions for the payment of compensations, under the Crop Insurance Scheme which is currently in operation, despite the severe financial condition encountered by the country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Providing Housing Units under the Urban Regeneration Project to the \tfamilies occupying in the settlement with less facilities in the land called \tHathbodhiyawatta, Narahenpita and developing the said land",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12214",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- There is a low-income settlement on a land block of Government-owned land called Hathbodhiyawatta located in the Kirula Grama Niladhari Division, Narahenpita in extent of 01 Acres 03 Roods and 10 Perches and those housing units are often subject to disasters during the rainy seasons. It has been proposed to provide the families occupying in the said settlement, with the alternative housing units from the housing schemes constructed by the Urban Development Authority under the Urban Regeneration Project. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to provide housing units from the housing schemes constructed in the Colombo city under the Urban Regeneration Project, to the occupants of the said land and thereafter to transfer the said land to the Urban Development Authority under section 6(1) of the State Land Ordinance to implement a mixed development project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Sale of Housing Units of Lake Crest Residencies Housing Project at Angoda, \tMandawila on freehold basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12213",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The possession of housing units of the Lake Crest Residencies Housing Project at Angoda, Mandawila comprising of 500 units implemented by the Urban Development Authority, has been handed over to the housing recipients in the year 2018. The proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to grant freehold deeds to the housing recipients who have completed the relevant payments, according to the Condominium Property Law and to the other housing recipients after completing the relevant payments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-10-09",
    "description": "Recognition of Medical Degree Courses of Internationally Recognized \tUniversities in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12212",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201105\u201102 has granted approval to appoint a Committee chaired by the Secretary to the Prime Minster to submit appropriate recommendations to formulate a National Policy with standards and criteria to be based for the recognition of Medical Degree courses of internationally recognized Universities, in Sri Lanka and to amend the provisions of the Medical Ordinance to suit the present day needs. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Hon. President and the Minister of Health to take necessary action to impose required legal provisions enabling to recognize the Medical Degrees awarded by foreign universities ranked 01 to 1000 as per the international ranking systems, based on the Report containing the recommendations of the Committee so appointed, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Appointment of an Advisory Committee to the Department of Community \n\tBased Corrections",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12211",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been recommended at the Committee on Public Accounts held on 2023\u201106\u201109\tto appoint an Advisory Committee, since a continuous supervision and a follow up is necessary to discharge the duties carried out by the Department of Community Based Corrections coming under the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms. Accordingly, The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to appoint the proposed Advisory Committee under the chairmanship of the Secretary, Ministry of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms and consisting of other relevant Heads of Institutions and experts in the relevant field, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
