    "date_str": "2023-07-17",
    "description": "Amendments to the Inland Revenue Act, No. 24 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12116",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201106\u201128 has granted approval to introduce relevant amendments to the Inland Revenue Act No. 24 of 2017 to revise the income tax rate applicable on the income earned from investment made in Treasury Bonds by the Employees Trust Fund, Employees Provident Fund (EPF), Pension Fund or Gratuity Fund and similar Funds in order to facilitate the Domestic Debt Optimizing process.  The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the draft prepared by the Legal Draftsman accordingly. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-07-17-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-07-17",
    "description": "Introduction of a Standard Operating Procedure for granting Diplomatic Clearance for Foreign Seaborne Vessels arriving in Sri Lanka and Foreign Military or State Aircrafts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12115",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the geostrategic location of Sri Lanka in the Indian Ocean, foreign seaborne vessels and foreign military or state aircrafts frequently visit Sri Lanka. Further, States and competent International Organizations are interested in carrying out Marine Scientific Research in the Exclusive Economic Zone and the Continental Shelf of Sri Lanka. In this context, it has been found necessary to prepare a Standard Operating Procedure so as to grant diplomatic clearance for such activities. Accordingly, the Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs has submitted the Standard Operating Procedure prepared in consultation with all parties to the Cabinet and it was decided to grant approval for the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
