    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2023-07-10",
    "description": "Provision of Welfare Benefit Payments for Elderly Beneficiaries,  Chronic Kidney Patients with unknown etiology (CKDu) and Differently-Abled Persons",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12104",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Lists with about two million names identified for the implementation of the Aswesuma Welfare Benefit Payment Scheme have now been published at the Divisional Secretariat and Grama Niladhari Divisional levels for submitting appeals and objections. Accordingly, Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies for making welfare benefit payments for the 3 social groups of Elderly Beneficiaries, Chronic Kidney Patients with unknown etiology (CKDu) and Differently-Abled Persons, stated in the Gazette Notification which has already been published, until such persons who have applied for obtaining welfare benefits are determined based on the most appropriate criteria and guidelines for obtaining such benefits under the said Programme."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-07-10-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2023-07-10",
    "description": "Preparation of a Master Plan for development of the Hambantota District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12103",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although, approval of the cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2018\u201106\u201126 to assign the task of obtaining consultancy services for the preparation of a Greater Hambantota Regional Structure Plan and a Detailed Master Plan for Key Growth Centres to Surbana Jurong (Private) Company, action have not yet been taken as per the said decision. The Government has decided to give priority to the development of the Hambantota district, and it has been identified that it would be more appropriate to assign the task of preparing a master plan for the development of Hambantota district to Surbana Jurong (Private) Company itself, which has been entrusted with the responsibility of preparing master plans for the development of the Colombo city and the Western Province, and the development of the Eastern Province Strategic Tourism Zone. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to assign the said task to  to Surbana Jurong (Private) Company, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-07-10-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2023-07-10",
    "description": "Enrollment of the 07th intake under the Interest Free Student Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12102",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meting held on 2023\u201104\u201124 to enroll the 07th intake under the Interest Free Student Loan Scheme, to follow degree courses in Non-State universities. The Bank of Ceylon and the Peoples' Bank have expressed their concurrence to implement this loan scheme with a minimum interest rate of 13% for the entire loan duration. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to implement the Interest Free Student Loan Scheme for the students who have fulfilled requisite qualifications from among the students selected to follow degree courses upon the GCE(A/L) results in the years of 2019, 2020 and 2021, under the 07th intake, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-07-10-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-07-10",
    "description": "Mid-Year Fiscal Position Report",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12101",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of section 10 of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No.3 of 2003, the Minister in charge of the subject of Finance is required to release the Report of Mid-Year Fiscal Position to the general public by the end of June of each year and thereafter to table the same in Parliament. Accordingly, the Mid-Year Fiscal Position Report up to 2023\u201106\u201130 has been published on the website of the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to table the said Report in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-07-10-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-07-10",
    "description": "Bill to amend the approved Borrowing Limit for the Financial Year 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12100",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meting held on 2023\u201106\u201128 to amend the approved borrowing limit for the financial year 2023. Accordingly, a Bill has been drafted by the Legal Draftsman to amend the Appropriation Act, No.43 of 2022 and the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the same. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette, and thereafter present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-07-10-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-07-10",
    "description": "Order under subsection (2) of Section 29A of the Judicature Act, No. 2 of 1978",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12099",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Section 29A(2) of the Judicature Act, No. 2 of 1978 indicates the provisions that the monetary value of all actions specified in the Seventh Schedule over which the Small Claims Court will have exclusive original civil jurisdiction, shall be designated by the Minister in-charge of the subject of Justice from time to time. The Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms has published an Order in the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No. 2328/16 dated 2023.04.21, which states that the monetary value up to Rs. 1.5 million excluding the interest, which has been fixed to the said courts, shall be Rupees two million or not exceeding Rupees two million, excluding the interest. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to submit the said Order in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
