    "doc_id": "2023-06-26-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2023-06-26",
    "description": "Obtaining support of the World Bank for the implementation of Economic Stabilization and Recovery Programme through the Development Policy Financing Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12078",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Negotiations to seek the support of the World Bank under the Development Policy Financing Programme  for a period of two years from 2023 to 2024 have been held on 2023\u201105\u201117. Under the said programme, it has been agreed to grant Special Drawing Rights (SDR) 371.2 million equivalent to US$ 500 million in 02 tranches for the year 2023. The clearance of the Attorney General and the concurrence of the Monetary Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka have been obtained for the proposed financing facility. Accordingly, the  proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to enter into an Agreement with the International Development Association of the World Bank Group in relation to obtaining the said financing facility, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-26-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-06-26",
    "description": "Submission of Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No. 1 of 1969",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12077",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Regulations to temporarily suspend the importation of certain selected goods have been issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No. 1 of 1969 in order to ease the increasing pressure on external reserves and the financial market due to the unfavorable economic situation prevailing  in the country . The necessity to remove restrictions on the importation of selected goods which could cause a minimum impact on Balance of Payment has been identified by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and other relevant parties through the relaxation of aforesaid  Regulations. Accordingly, it has been decided to remove 286 HS Codes from the list of 1216 HS Codes in the schedule of temporary suspension of imports.  For the said purpose, the Imports and Exports (Control) Regulations, No. 09 of 2023 has been published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No. 2335/26 dated 2023\u201106\u201109. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the said Regulations to Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
