    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Selection of Companies for Importation, Storage, Distribution and Sale of \tPetroleum Products in Sri Lanka, on Long-Term Contracts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11968",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201106\u201127 has granted approval to call for Expression of Interest for importation, storage, distribution and sale of petroleum products on long term contracts. Accordingly, 26 companies have made their proposals and the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Cabinet Appointed Special Committee have recommended 13 companies with qualifications to submit Request for Proposals. As such, 07 companies have submitted detailed proposals. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to enter into Agreements with the following companies for importation, storage, distribution and sale of petroleum products in Sri Lanka as per the provisions of the Petroleum Products (Special Provisions) (Amended) Act, No.33 of 2022, based on the recommendations submitted by the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Cabinet Appointed Special Committee and the Procurement Appeal Board on the said proposals, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tM/S Sinopec Fuel Oil Lanka (Private) Limited\n*\tM/S United Petroleum Pty Ltd.\n*\tM/S RM Parks of USA"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Establishment of a Solar Power Plant at Sampur, Trincomalee by a Joint Venture Company of the Ceylon Electricity Board and the National Thermal Power Corporation of India",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11967",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- An agreement has been reached by the National Thermal Power Corporation of India and the Ceylon Electricity Board to implement a Solar Power Plant of 135 MW jointly in two phases at the same location where the Coal Power Plant at Sampur was scheduled to be constructed. Under phase 01 of this Project, it is expected to develop a 50 MW Solar Power Plant project with a total investment of US$ 42.5 million and to construct a 220 kV transmission line of 40 km length from Sampur to Kappalthurai at an estimated cost of US$ 23.6 million. This phase is scheduled to be completed in 2 years from 2024 to 2025. In phase 02 of the Project, a Solar Power Plant with an additional capacity of 85 MW will be constructed at a total investment of US$ 72 million. Further, it has been planned to construct a transmission line of 76 km length transmission line with a capacity of 220 KW from Kappalthurai to New Habarana at an estimated cost of US$ 42 million to distribute the electricity generated under phase 02. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to take the necessary steps to implement the said Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Procurement of Coal required for the Norachcholai Lakvijaya Coal Power Plant for the Season of 2023/2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11966",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been estimated that 2.25 million MT of coal is required for the Norachcholai Lakvijaya Coal Power Plant for the season of 2023/2024. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister Power and Energy to implement the relevant procurement process, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding for the Corporation in the Field of\tRenewable Energy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11965",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Obtaining a 70% of the total electricity requirement from the renewable energy sources by the year 2030, being energy independent and achieving carbon neutrality by 2050 have declared as a policy by the Government. Aiming to achieve that stability, the Government of the Republic of India has agreed to promote and strengthen corporation in the field of renewable energy by jointly undertaking and /or facilitation power generation projects utilizing solar energy, wind energy including off shore wind, power generation projects relating to Bio mass and dedicated transmission infrastructure at mutually agreed locations in Sri Lanka including locations in the Northern and Eastern provinces jointly by private and public sector enterprises of India and Sri Lanka. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding for the Corporation in the Field of Renewable Energy, between the Republic of India and the Government Of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Holding the State Vesak Festival of the year 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11964",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to hold the State Vesak Festival of 2023 (Sri Buddha Year 2567) at Kebellewala Sri Rathanasiri Pirivena Temple, Madampe, Chillaw in Puttlam District jointly by the Ministry of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government; Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs and the Department of Buddhist Affairs, with the recommendations of the Most Venerable Mahamayake Theros of Tri\u2011Nikaya and the Samastha Lanka Sasanarakshaka Mandalaya. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to declare from 2023\u201105\u201102 to 2023\u201105\u201108 as the Vesak Week and simultaneously carry out different religious and social programmes, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Submission of Orders made under the Sri Lanka Export Development Act,\tNo.40 of 1979, for approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11963",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to present the Orders made under section 14 of the Sri Lanka Export Development Act, No.40 of 1979 and published by the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2312/76 dated 2023\u201101\u201101, for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "National Programme to Commemorate the International Day of Zero Waste",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11962",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The United Nations General Assembly, under the initiative of the Republic of Turkiye, made the proclamation that 30th March of each year as the International Day of Zero Waste, on 2022\u201112\u201114. The objective of declaring this day is to promote zero waste initiatives to advance the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to conduct a national programme to commemorate the International Day Zero Waste on 2023\u201103\u201130 with the participation of the Ministry of Environment and other stakeholder institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Determination of Deputy Inspector General Divisional Boundaries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11961",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the Policy Statement presented at the opening of the 04th Session of the 09th Parliament, Hon. President pointed out that, since the existing Deputy Inspector General divisional boundaries do not coincide with the existing provincial boundaries, it is necessary to determine the Deputy Inspector General divisional boundaries according to the provinces in order to avoid practical difficulties and issues in administration. Accordingly, it was decided to grant the concurrence of the Cabinet regarding the measures taken by the Hon. President to appoint an\tOfficials' Committee under the Chairmanship of Secretary to the Ministry of Public Security to determine the Deputy Inspector General divisional boundaries."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Incorporation of Sri Lanka Institute of Agriculture",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11960",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is essential to take an integrated approach pertaining to various sectors such as food crops, plantation crops, exports agricultural crops, horticultural crops, animal\thusbandry, environment and forest conservation for the agricultural development\tin Sri Lanka and for what it has been observed that it is appropriate to establish a\tstructure to make agriculture experts highly skilled on relevant subjects serving in different institutions for technological capacity building. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to incorporate Sri Lanka Institute of\tAgriculture which holds the membership of more than 1000 agricultural professionals at present, ensuring the quality of service and ethics of the agricultural professionals enabling to acquire their service widely, efficiently and effectively and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill, was approved\tby the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "To obtain the approval for the establishment of Quality Assurance and \tAccreditation Commission",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11959",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted on 2019\u201104\u201102 to publish the Higher Education (Quality Assurance Accreditation) Bill in the Government Gazette and to present in the Parliament but could not be presented to the Parliament for approval at that occasion. After examining some of the amendments proposed by the Attorney General to move at the Committee Stage of the said Bill and the observations and proposals submitted by various parties subsequently, it has been identified that it is appropriate to further amend the Higher Education (Quality Assurance Accreditation) Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman incorporating the new provisions. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a new Bill, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Amendment to Section 6 (3) (e) of the Civil Aviation Act No.14 of 2010",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11958",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that, opening up the sectors of aeronautical services for public\u2011private participation and investment promotion by private entities in these\tsectors will contribute for the rapid development of such sectors and for the betterment of the Aviation industry as a whole. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Port, Shipping and Aviation to instruct the Legal Draftsman to\tamend the Civil Aviation Act, No.14 of 2010 enabling one or more persons to be appointed as service providers for providing the aeronautical services, was\tapproved by\tthe Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Procedure related to Areca Nut Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11957",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposals on export of locally produced Areca Nuts and importation of\tdried\tAreca Nuts and re\u2011exportation after value addition have been deliberated\tat the\tCabinet meeting held on 2023\u201103\u201113 and an Officials Committee has\tbeen\tappointed under the Chairmanship of Senior Economic Advisor to the\tPresident to submit a report with recommendations to the Cabinet after\texamining the matters thereon.  Accordingly, as recommended by the said \tCommittee, it was decided to grant approval to the procedure for export of \tlocally produced Areca Nuts and the import of Areca Nuts for value added \texports re-exportation after value addition."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Hosting the Fifth Session of the Forum of Ministers of Environment and \tEnvironment Authorities of Asia Pacific",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11956",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The fifth session of the Forum of Ministers of Environment and Environment Authorities of Asia Pacific has been scheduled to be held in the fourth quarter of year 2023 in Sri Lanka in order to provide opinions and proposals on the Regional Environmental Agenda at the 6th session of the United Nations Environment\tAssembly scheduled to be held in February 2024 in Nairobi, Kenya. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to host the fifth session of the said\tForum, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Development of Sigiriya as a Sustainable Tourist Destination",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11955",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sigiriya, a world heritage and one of the major reputed archaeological sites in Sri Lanka is a tourist destination with the highest tourist attraction among local and foreign tourists. Further, it is also the highest income generating tourist destination from among the tourist destinations in this country. However, considering the issues arising when managing Sigiriya as a tourist destination, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism and Lands and the Minister of Buddhasasana, Cultural and Religious Affairs to prepare a Master Plan to develop Sigiriya as a sustainable tourist destination, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Establishment of the Road Maintenance Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11954",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hon. President presenting the budget for the year 2023 proposed to establish a fund for road maintenance and he further proposed to allocate an initial provision of Rs.100 million for the purpose.  The responsibility of formulating a suitable mechanism to establish and maintain the fund has been vested with the Ministry of Transport and Highways. Accordingly, taking into account a proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways, Cabinet granted its approval for the establishment of the proposed Fund by an Act of Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Conversion of National School of Business Management Limited (NSBM) to \ta Company Limited by Guarantee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11953",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- National School of Business Management Limited has been established as a subsidiary of the National Institute of Business Management established under the provisions of the National Institute of Business Management Law No.23 of 1976. The said institute which has been established as a state-of-the-art University in Homagama, presently functions as an institute which offer Degrees and Post Graduate Degrees. Currently, more than 11,500 students have been given the opportunity to study more than 50 degree courses under 05 faculties in that institution. It has been found that by adopting a model equivalent to the models that of the world\u2011renowned educational institutions in the world, it will be possible to maintain the functions of the NSBM in a more effective manner and in accordance with international standards. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to take future measures required to convert the registration status of the National School of Business Management into a company Limited by Guarantee in terms of section 32 of the Companies Act, No.07 of 2007, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Providing facilities to pursue Degree Programmes in Non-State Higher\tEducation Institutes under the Interest-Free Student Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11952",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2017\u201104\u201104 to implement a project for the provision of interest free loans for the students who do not meet the cut\u2011off marks to enter into State Universities, to pursue Degree Courses in accredited Non\u2011State Degree awarding institutes.  At present, five (05) batches of students have been benefited under the said scheme and the qualified students to the 06th batch have been identified. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to further continue that Interest\u2011Free Student Loan Scheme as per the procedure so far followed and to facilitate for 5000 students as the 7th batch of students under the said programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Upgrading the Siddha Medicine Units of the University of Jaffna and the \tTrincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11951",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Having discussed at the Cabinet Meeting held on 2023\u201102\u201106 on the upgrading of the existing Siddha Medicine Units of the University of Jaffna and the Trincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, Sri Lanka as faculties, it had been decided to obtain a Report from the University Grants Commission on whether there are sufficient academic and staff facilities for the purpose. Accordingly, it has been confirmed by the University Grants Commission that there are sufficient human and physical resources to transform the said Siddha Medical Units into Faculties. Taking into account the facts presented by the Minister of Education, the approval of the Cabinet was granted to take the necessary action to upgrade the relevant Siddha Medicine units as faculties in those universities."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-27-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-03-27",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding for the implementation of the Korea's Saemaul Undong Projects in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11950",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Saemaul Undong Programme which was implemented since 1970 by the Republic of Korea has been instrumental to transform the traditional agrarian economy prevailed in the rural areas of Korea into an industrialized and export\u2011oriented economy by improving infrastructure facilities, livelihood, welfare and education. In 2015, the Saemaul programme has also been started in Sri Lanka by the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council after entering into a Memorandum of Understanding with the Saemaul Foundation, which was established in the year 2013 by the Republic of Korea with a view to expanding the Saemaul concept to the other countries as well. The duration of the said MoU has expired by now. It has been proposed to sign a new Memorandum of Understanding enabling to implement projects under the Saemaul Undong concept covering all the provinces of Sri Lanka.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government to sign a Tripartite Memorandum of Understanding among the Ministry of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government; the Department of External Resources and the Saemaul Foundation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-20-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-03-20",
    "description": "Securing the Extended Fund Facility Arrangement during 2023 - 2026 from the International Monetary Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11949",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has entered into a Staff Level Agreement on 2022\u201109\u201101 to obtain a loan facility of US$ equivalent 2.3 billion of SDR for a 48 months arrangement under the Extended Fund Facility to support Sri Lanka's economic policies with a view to ensuring the macroeconomic stability and debt sustainability, safeguarding financial stability, protecting the vulnerable communities, stepping up structural reforms, curbing corruption, and unlocking Sri Lanka's growth potentialities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to enter into the relevant Agreements to obtain the said Extended Fund Facility of the International Monetary Fund for budget financing during 2023\u20112026, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-20-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-03-20",
    "description": "Betting and Gaming Levy (Amendment) Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11948",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201107\u201104 has granted approval to amend the\n\tBetting and Gaming Levy Act No. 40 of 1988. The clearance of the Attorney \tGeneral has been received to the Bill prepared accordingly by the Legal \tDraftsman. As such, \tthe proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as \tthe Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to \tpublish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same \tthereafter, \tto Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-20-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-03-20",
    "description": "Submission of Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports (Control)Act, No.1 of 1969, for Approval of Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11947",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the following regulations enacted under the provisions of Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969, for Approval of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tImports Control Regulations on Payment Terms No.04 of 2023, published in the Gazette Extraordinary No.2320/46 dated 2023\u201102\u201122.\n\n*\tImports and Exports (Control) Regulations No.05 of 2023, published in the Gazette Extraordinary No.2320/47 dated 2023\u201102\u201122."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-20-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-03-20",
    "description": "Submission of the Order in terms of section 2 of the Extradition Law No.8 of 1977 for the approval of the Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11946",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Extradition Law No.8 of 1977 has been enacted to make provision for the extradition of fugitive persons to and from Commonwealth countries and foreign states, to regulate the treatment of persons accused or convicted of offenses committed in\tSri Lanka who are extradited from Commonwealth countries and foreign states, and to provide for matters connected therewith or incidental thereto. The Minister of Defence has the authority to promulgate through an Order published in the Gazette on Commonwealth countries to which the provisions of the section 2 of the said Act apply. Accordingly, an amended Order including 56 countries, in terms of the section 2\tof Extradition Law No.8 of 1977, was published through Gazette Extraordinary No.2319/30 dated 2023\u201102\u201114. The proposal made by the President in his capacity as the\tMinister of Defense to submit the said Order for the approval of the Parliament, was\tapproved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-20-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-03-20",
    "description": "Accession to the Agreement on Privileges and Immunities of the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11945",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has been a founding Member State of the International Atomic Energy Agency since 1957 and it receives technical assistance for the fields such as Medicine, Industry, Safety, Food and Agriculture, Environment and Energy Planning under the Technical Cooperation Programme of the said Institute. Sri Lanka has not yet signed the Agreements to grant immunities and privileges to the experts and other officials who visit Sri Lanka to provide such technical assistance. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs and the Minister of Power and Energy to accede the Agreement on Privileges and Immunities of the International Atomic Energy Agency as agreed by the Attorney General's Department, the Ministry of Power and Energy, the Sri Lanka Atomic Energy Board and the Sri Lanka Atomic Energy Regulatory Council and thereafter table the same in terms of the provisions of the Diplomatic Privileges Act, No.9 of 1996, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-20-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-03-20",
    "description": "Distribution of land plots from the land called Hineford Estate of Pasbage Korale, Nawalapitiya vested with the Land Reform Commission for those who were affected by floods and landslides",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11944",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The land called Hineford Estate in extent of 566 acres situated in the Divisional Secretariat Division of Pasbage Korale of the Kandy district has been vested with the Land Reform Commission. Taking into consideration a proposal made by the Minister of Tourism and Lands, Cabinet granted its approval to distribute about 200 acres of lands from the said land among those affected by floods and landslides and the families residing in high risk prone areas and likely to be affected by such disasters."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-20-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-03-20",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement between the Human Resources Development Service of Korea and the Vocational Training Authority of Sri Lanka to Strengthen Technical Vocational Education and Training Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11943",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Human Resources Development Service of Korea under the purview of the Ministry of Employment and Labour of the Republic of Korea has expressed its willingness to provide a grant of 2.15 billion of Korean Won for upgrading and capacity building of the National Vocational Training Institute at Niyagama operating under the Vocational Training Authority of Sri Lanka. The proposed project has been planned to be implemented for a period of two years commencing from the year 2023 and for the purpose it has been proposed to enter into an Agreement between the Human Resources Development Service of Korea and the Vocational Training Authority of Sri Lanka. The clearance of the Attorney General and the concurrence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Department of External Resources have been received for the draft Agreement. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign the proposed Agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-13-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-03-13",
    "description": "Anti-Corruption Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11942",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201107\u201118 has granted approval to prepare the Anti\u2011Corruption Bill. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received to the said Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Anti-Corruption Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter in Parliament for Approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-13-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-03-13",
    "description": "Amendment to the Carriage by Air Act, No.29 of 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11941",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201108\u201122 has granted approval to amend the\n\tCarriage by Air Act, No.29 of 2018 to modify the legal framework pertaining to the protection of domestic aviation, to ensure the passenger safety and to identify the liability limits for the domestic aviation. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received to the Carriage by Air Bill prepared accordingly by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter in Parliament for Approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-13-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-03-13",
    "description": "Rights of  Persons with Disabilities Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11940",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities was signed by Sri Lanka in the year 2016. As per the Article 4 of the Convention, State \tParties should undertake to ensure and promote the full realization of all human\trights and fundamental freedom for all persons with disabilities without discrimination of any kind on the basis of disability and a committee consisting of Honorable Ministers of Parliament has been appointed to prepare a preliminary draft in this regard. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment and the Minister of Justice, Prisons Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, to\tintroduce a new Act repealing the existing Protection of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, No.28 of 1996 and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill for the said purpose, based on the preliminary draft submitted by the above committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-13-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-03-13",
    "description": "Imposition of Regulations under the provisions of the Employees' Trust Fund \tAct No.46 of 1980",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11939",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Regulations made amending the the Employees' Trust Fund Regulations which had been made under the Employees' Trust Fund Act, No.46 of 1980 and promulgated in the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.125 dated 1980\u201101\u201123, have been published by the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2311/39 dated 2022\u201112\u201122. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance,Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the said amended regulations to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-13-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-03-13",
    "description": "Pilot Project for the installation of Floating Solar power projects on the\tsurface of Chandrika Wewa and Kiri Ibban Wewa in Rathnapura District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11938",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Framework Agreement on Grant Aid signed between the Republic of Korea and Sri Lanka in 2009, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy of Korea has agreed to provide a grant of 6.83 billion Korean Won in order to implement a pilot project for the installation of Floating Solar power panels of 1 MW capacity on Chandrika Wewa in Rathnapura District and Kiri Ibban Wewa in Monaragala District. The Korea Institute for Advancement of Technology functions as the executing agency for this project on behalf of the Republic of Korea. Accordingly, as agreed, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to sign the Record of Discussion among the Korea Institute for Advancement of Technology, the Ministry of Power and Energy and the Department of External Resources in order to commence and execute this pilot project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-13-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-03-13",
    "description": "Transferring of the management of the Ridiyagama Rehabilitation Centre\tto the Central Government",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11937",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Ridiyagama Rehabilitation Centre located in Ambalanthota which was established under the Department of Social Services in 1975, has been transferred to the Social Affairs Division of the Southern Provincial Council in 1990. Although this centre has been built for the detention of around 450 inmates, currently 576 inmates have been detained there causing them to face a difficult and oppressive living condition. Taking into account the aforesaid situation and the detention of inmates in this centre from different parts of the country based on the Orders given by Courts, it has been found more appropriate that this centre be administering under the Central Government as a national level centre instead of managing the same by the Southern Provincial Council. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment; and the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to transfer the Ridiyagama Rehabilitation Centre to the Department of Social Services, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-07-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-03-07",
    "description": "Review of Sri Lanka's 6th Periodic Report under the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11936",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Review of Sri Lanka's 6th Interim Report under the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights is scheduled to be held in Geneva on March 8 and 9, 2023.\tThe matters presented by the Minister of Foreign Affairs regarding the steps taken so far by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for the said review, was taken into consideration by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-07-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-03-07",
    "description": "Establishing a Financial Sector Crisis Management Committee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11935",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is very important to avoiding a financial crisis that can be originated due to the impact on the financial sector owing to fiscal, debt and balance of payment issues and  minimizing the cost of such a financial crisis. Accordingly, critical crisis management and timely decision-making are essential in the face of the economic crisis that Sri Lanka is currently encountered. Therefore, the proposal submitted by \tthe Hon. President\tin his capacity as the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to establish the Financial Sector Crisis Management Committee\tand the Technical Committee on Financial Sector Crisis \tManagement to coordinate\tbetween the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and the Ministry in charge of the subject of Finance in the preparation and management of a crisis in the financial sector, as well as their respective roles and to include the necessary provisions in the Banking (Special Provisions)Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-07-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-03-07",
    "description": "Amending the National Institute of Occupational Safety and Health Act,\tNo.38 of 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11934",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tThe National Institute of Occupational Safety and Health Act,\tNo.38 of 2009 has been enacted aiming to establish an institute on national occupational safety and health for the purpose of formulating a national policy to frame standards for occupational safety and health and to create an occupational safety environment that ensures the safety of both the employers and employees. It has been identified that this Act should be amended so as to suit to the timely requirements. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation to amend the  National Institute of Occupational Safety and Health Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-07-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-03-07",
    "description": "Contribution of Sri Lanka for the \"Commonwealth of Learning\" \tOrganization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11933",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The \"Commonwealth of Learning\" is an international organization established by the Heads of States to strengthen the capacity of member countries to develop human resources required for their economic and social development. The contribution of Sri Lanka as a member country to the \"Commonwealth of Learning\", which is the education sector of the Commonwealth Organization, has been given for the education sector of the Memorandum of Understanding for the Commonwealth Fund signed with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to pay the relevant contribution amount and continue the membership of the \"Commonwealth of Learning\" organization, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-07-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-03-07",
    "description": "Construction of a Water Treatment Plant at Horana Export Processing Zone",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11932",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Water is supplied to the Horana Export Processing Zone and the Wagawatta Industrial Zone through a water supply scheme implemented by the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka and its production capacity is 3,000 m3 per day.  However, since the daily water demand of investors in Horana and Wagawata zones is about 4,350 m3, the National Water Supply and Drainage Board has prepared plans for the construction of a new water treatment plant with a capacity of 2,000 m3 per day to meet the said water demand. The Board of Directors of the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka has agreed to make necessary provisions for that. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to construct and operate the said new water treatment plant in the Horana Export Processing Zone by utilizing the allocations of the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-03-07-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-03-07",
    "description": "Identification of the Limits of the Continental Shelf of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11931",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has presented its technical and scientific data and other material to the United Nations Commission on the Limits of the Continental Shelf to establish the outer limits of  the Continental Shelf beyond 200 nautical miles Exclusive Economic Zone under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea. Accordingly, the said Commission has appointed a Sub-Commission to consider the Sri Lanka's claim. The National Ocean Affairs Committee has been appointed under the Ministry of Foreign Affairs as per the approval of the Cabinet to work with the above Sub Commission to identify the  limits of the Continental Shelf for which claims are preferred by Sri Lanka. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to call for Expression of Interest to reconstitute the said National Ocean Affairs Committee with a view to identifying the outer limits of the continental shelf with supporting evidence to establish the shelf, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Anti-Terrorism Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11930",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has previously granted approval for the introduction of a new Act to replace the existing Prevention of Terrorism (Temporary Provisions) Act No.48 of 1979. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman.As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Introduction of the Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11929",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201103\u201108 has granted approval to introduce a new Act incorporating the most suitable provisions to replace Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Actcurrently in force, so that the internationally accepted best standards and practices can be followed. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Exemption of the purchase of paddy, production and sale of rice from the Social Security Levy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11928",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval ofthe Cabinet has been granted to implement a programme toprovide rice to the low income earners free of charge by purchasing Nadu paddy by the Governmentat Rs 100/-per kg in view of giving a reasonable price to the paddy farmer. The rice producers has pointed out that an additional cost has to be incurred for the water, electricity, storage and transportationetc. until one kg of rice is produced and delivered to the consumer in the process of rice production in addition to the amount of money paid to the farmer for 01kg of paddy and apart from that approximatelyRs.6.00/7.00 for 01kg of rice has to be spent as social security contribution levy. They have further pointed out that if any relief can be given to reduce the said cost, there is a possibility of giving a higher price to the farmers. Taking into consideration the said matters, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to amend the Social Security Contribution Levy Act, No.25 of 2022 to exempt the purchase of paddy, production and sale of rice from the social security levy so as to provide farmers with a price higher than Rs.100/- per kg of Nadu paddy by maintaining the current price of paddy in the market as it is, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Submission of the Order enacted under the provisions of the Export\tDevelopmet Act, No.40 of 1979 to Parliament for approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11927",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into account the impact of depreciation ofrupee and the global market price/ cost and CIF value, the specific unit rates of the CESS levy on selected goods under HS Code 677 has been revised, and for that the Order imposed under section 14 of the Sri Lanka Export Development Act No.40 of 1979 has been published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2022\u201111\u201114. Such Order imposed as per the provisions of the said Act should be submitted to Parliament for approval within 04 months from the date of its promulgation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to submit the said Order which has been published through Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2022\u201111\u201114, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Establishment of National Contributory Pension Fund Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11926",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been recognized that it would be appropriate to establish a fund called the National Contributory Pension Fund to provide a pension with some benefit to the pensioners of the Public service for their retirement life and to ensure a suitable environment for the pensioner to spend his retirement life without being a burden to the country. Accordingly, after joining the public service, 8% of the basic salary as a Government employee and 12%as the employer's contribution should be credited to the proposed fund monthly. An independent body governed by the Board of Management will be set up to manage the proposed Contributory Pension Fund and a Fund Manager with special qualifications will be appointed to manage the funds. The proposed National Contributory Pension Scheme will be applicable to the Government employees who will be recruited in future. Further, since the provisions to the effect that employees recruited to the public service after January, 2016 should be subject to a Pension Scheme determined by the Government, are included in their Letters of Appointment, they are also able to join the proposed National Contributory Pension Scheme at their discretion. Accordingly, theproposal made by the Hon. President to instruct a Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill, enabling to make the necessary provisions, was approved by the Cabient."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Expanding market opportunities for supply of Jet A-1 fuel being used for \taircrafts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11925",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Jet A-1 fuel used for airplanes is currently supplied by the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation. Since it has become unable to ensure the supply of Jet A-1 fuel required for cargo and passenger air service, due to disruption of operations of the Sapugaskanda Oil Refinery, where Jet A-1 fuel is produced and becoming the import of Jet A-1 fuel a challenging task for the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation as a result of the current foreign exchange crisis facing by the country, attention has to be drawn on alternative methods to secure Jet A-1 fuel for the aircrafts that reach airports in Sri Lanka. Accordingly, it has been observed appropriate to provide the opportunity for the parties supplying Jet A-1 fuel to airlines in other countries under maximum supply limits, without hindering the supply of Jet A-1 fuel processed at Sapugaskanda Refinery of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy for the provision of market opportunities for the supply of Jet A-1 fuel to the other parties, who are capable of supplying Jet A-1 fuel , was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Implementation of a Pilot Project to deploy buses charged with batteries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11924",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the face of the international energy crisis, as a measure to minimize the cost incurred for the importation of fossil fuels, it has been found appropriate to introduce buses that can be run on solar power, which is a renewable energy source. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways on the implementation of a public-private partnership project for the deployment of electric buses for the Sri Lanka Transport Board covering the Western Province, centered on Colombo Commercial City and Gampaha District, Cabinet granted its approval to implement a pilot project based on a formal feasibility study, in the first instance."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Sri Lanka becoming a Party to Two Major International Conventions on\tNuclear Liability",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11923",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to consider nuclear Power as an option to meet Sri Lanka's future energy needs. In keeping with the said decision, a Steering Committee and 09 Working Groups have been appointed to study the matters related to generating electricity using nuclear power. According to the recommendations given by the International Atomic Energy Agency regarding the Self Evaluation Report prepared by the said Working Groups, Sri Lanka has the ability to continue the Project of generating electricity from nuclear power. As such, it has been recognized that being a party to the Vienna Convention on Civil Liability for Nuclear Damage and the Convention on Supplementary Compensation for Nuclear Damage would be appropriate to enable taking necessary measures. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs and the Minister of Power and Energy to take future action to become a party to those conventions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement between the 'Sight for All' Company of \tAustralia and the Ministry of Health",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11922",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Sight for All', Community Project Institute of Australia has extended its willingness to donate medical and surgical eye equipment to the eye units of the selected hospitals in Sri Lanka and provide a grant to enhance skills of health staff. Under that, it is expected to secure modern health facilities required for ocular surgeries in Provincial General Hospital Badulla, Teaching hospitals of Ratnapura, Batticaloa and Kalubowila and the Base Hospital of Tangalle and to enhance the skills of Eye Health Workers and to upgrade equipment of the regional eye units. A grant of Rs. 92.44 million will be receivedunder these projects. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to enter into an Agreement between the 'Sight for All', Community Project Institute of Australia and the Ministry of Health to obtain the proposed grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-004-en",
