    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "National Policy on Gender Equality and Women Empowerment",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11921",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval was granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022\u201109\u201105 for the preparation of a National Policy for Women Empowerment by minimizing gender imbalances. Accordingly, the \u201cNational Policy on Gender Equality and Women Empowerment\u201c has been prepared under 08 key thematic areas with the contribution of all the relevant parties. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment to implement the said policy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "National Action Plan on Women, Peace and Security",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11920",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The United Nations Security Council has adopted a resolution on Women, Peace and Security in the year 2000 and many developed and undeveloped countries in the world have introduced National Action Plans to implement this resolution. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment to implement the \"National Action Plan on Women, Peace and Security - 2023\u20112027\" which has been drafted with the contribution and concurrence of all the stakeholders, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Expediting the investigations and inquiries pertaining to goods detained by the Sri Lanka Customs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11919",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that a long time is taken to complete the investigation, inquiries and other related processes pertaining to goods including vehicles, detained by the Sri Lanka Customs. As this results in many economic losses including damage and destruction to such goods, it is important to expedite the existing processes followed by the Sri Lanka Customs on such detained goods. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence for the measures taken by the Hon. President to appoint a Ministerial Committee consisted with the following composition to study those matters and identify the amendments to be made to the Customs Ordinance if any and to submit recommendations on that regard to the Cabinet.\n\n* \tHon. Nimal Siripala de Silva\n\tMinister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation\n\n*\tHon. (Dr.) Ramesh Pathirana\n\tMinister of Plantation Industries and Minister of Industries\n\n*\tHon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya \n\tState Minister of Finance\n\n*\tHon. Dilum Amunugama\n\tState Minister of InvestmentPromotion\n\n*\tHon. Shehan Semasinghe \n\tState Minister of Finance"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-27-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-02-27",
    "description": "Proposed Preferential Trade Agreement with Bangladesh",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11918",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Enhancing market access opportunities for Sri Lankan exporters by removing current trade barriers, attracting investments to address the concerns of the domestic supply and enhancing economic cooperation are the main objectives that are expected to achieve through strengthening connectivity with the main regional trading partners. The Cabinet of Ministers at its meeting held on 2021\u201106\u201114 granted approval to enter into a Preferential Trade Agreement between Sri Lanka and Bangladesh in parallel. It has been identified bilateral trade can be further enhanced by entering into a Preferential Trade Agreement with Bangladesh can further enhance beyond existing trade agreements. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to expedite the negotiations on the proposed Preferential Trade Agreement with Bangladesh, on the guidance of the International Trade Office, was granted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
