    "doc_id": "2023-02-20-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-02-20",
    "description": "Preparation of a Development Plan for the development of Kandy City",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11917",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hon. President drew the attention of the Cabinet to the need to develop the Kandy city under a proper plan by reducing the existing congestion in the city. Accordingly, the approval of the Cabinet was granted to appoint a Committee consisting of Ministers in the Kandy district and officials of the relevant institutions to submit appropriate plans and recommendations for the development of Kandy city from Kandy to Kundasale."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-20-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-02-20",
    "description": "Financing the Budget for the year 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11916",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Appropriation Act, No.43 of 2022 has authorized a gross borrowing limit of Rs.4,979 billion for the year 2023. Accordingly, it should be utilized for the debt repayment, interest payments and financing of development projects in this year. The total gross borrowings of Rs.4,979 billion will be secured from domestic and foreign sources and it has been estimated to obtain Rs.3,526 billion from local sources and Rs.1,453 billion from foreign sources. Necessary borrowings will be secured through Treasury Bills, Treasury Bonds and Foreign Currency Banking Unit Loans and Sri Lanka Development Bonds under the domestic sources. Adhering to the policy declared by the Government of Sri Lanka in April 2022 pertaining to the interim external debt servicing, the total debt service payments to be made in foreign currency within the first six (06) months in the year 2023 has been estimated as US$ 2,609 million. Out of which US$ 2,069 will be for repayment of foreign debt and US$ 540 million will be for the payment of interest. Further, debt service payments made in foreign currencies includes Sri Lanka Development Bonds of US$ 709 and US$ 46 as their interest. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to authorize the Secretary to the Treasury to take necessary action to secure necessary provisions within the approved borrowing limit, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-20-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-02-20",
    "description": "Conferment of National Honours",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11915",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tConferring National Honours to evaluate the service rendered through various aspects in Sri Lanka and outside takes place since 1986. As per the Gazette Notification dated 1995\u201103\u201120, Honours named Sri Lankabhimanya, Desamanya, Desabandu, Vidya Jyothi, Kala Keerthi, Sri Lanka Shikamani, Vidya Nidhi, Kala Shuri, Sri Lanka Thilaka and Veera Prathapa are conferred by the Presidents according to a proper procedure. Further, Sri Lanka Ranjana, Sri Lanka Rathna and Sri Lanka Ramya Honours are conferred to foreigners as per the Gazette Notification dated 1990\u201109\u201112. Also, in accordance with the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2008\u201102\u201108, the Sri Lanka Mitra Vibushana Honour is conferred to the Heads of State having cordial relationships with Sri Lanka, in recognition of their cooperation towards the Sri Lankan community. This Honour holds the topmost position in the order of the excellence of the National Honours conferred to non-Sri lankans. At present, there are considerable number of vacancies in those National Honours and the same have to be conferred to the selected individuals following the proper procedure. In addition to said Honours, it has been found appropriate to award Sri Lankans with Vishishta Kaushalyabhimani in order to evaluate the service rendered to the advancement of the fields of art, literature, science and technology and the Vishishta Janaraja Abhimani for the dedication made to the nation and also to grant the topmost rank in the order of excellence of the above mentioned National Honours. Accordingly, the Cabinet concurred with the proposals made by the Hon. President  to select honourees calling applications in keeping with the procedures set out in the relevant Gazette Notifications and to have a Parliament Act passed by making provisions to prevent conferring the National Honours irregularly by other institutions."
  },
  {
