    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Implementation of a Community-based Tourism Development Project \tfocusing on the Central, Northern and Eastern regions of Sri Lanka \tUnder a financial grant of the Korea Tourism Organization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11845",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority has proposed to implement a \"Community\u2011based Tourism Project\" under the financial assistance of the Korea Tourism Organization, focusing the Kuchchaweli Tourism Development Zone owned by the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority. A delegation of the Korea Tourism Organization has conducted a feasibility study on the relevant project proposal and extended its willingness to grant a financial assistance of  2.172 billion Korean Won for the implementation of the proposed entire project. A consensus has also been reached to provide a sum of  of 400 million  Korean won for preparation of the overall plan of the relevant Tourism Development Project, training program and for the implementation of a pilot training program as its first phase. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism and Lands to enter into an agreement between the Korea Tourism Organization and the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority for the implementation of the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Invitation for the Expression of Interest to commence business activities  by \tusing the facilities of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11844",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the layout of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport, there is a potential for converting the said Airport into a multi-purpose business center by implementing business opportunities related to aviation and as well as non-aviation related activities. Therefore, attention has been focused on taking measures to effectively utilize the facilities and assets in the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport by creating public-private partnership investment opportunities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to invite Expressions of Interest from investors and strategic entrepreneurs in direct and indirect aviation related ventures to carry out aeronautical and non-aeronautical businesses at the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Proposal for the revision of Electricity Tariff 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11843",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet considered the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies; and the Minister of Power and Energy on the revision of electricity tariff. Cabinet further considered that the General Treasury is no longer possible to provide required funds to the Ceylon Electricity Board within the existing fiscal space and as such there is no alternative other than the revision of the existing electricity tariff in order to cover only the cost incurred for the supply of electricity while minimizing the impact caused to the electricity consumers as much as possible in order to ensure an uninterrupted supply of power in the country. After discussion, it was decided to grant approval:\n\n* \tThe Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka to further study on the proposed electricity tariff revision submitted by the Sri Lanka Electricity Board in consultation with the relevant parties, and if any revisions are to be made, submit the same on or before 2023\u201102\u201115.\n\n* \tUntil then, the Ceylon Electricity Board and the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka to take necessary action jointly to implement the Electricity Tariff \tamendment proposed by the Ceylon Electricity Board to be effective from \t01\u201101\u20112023 as an interim measure in accordance with the amendments of the Policy Guidelines currently in force regarding the electricity industry.\n\n* \tIf any amendments will be presented by the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka, the Ceylon Electricity Board to take necessary action to implement those amendments and make the necessary adjustments by the next monthly electricity bills."
  },
  {
