    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2022-08-08",
    "description": "Establishment of Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living and \tEstablishment of the Food Security Committee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11673",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-08-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. President to establish the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Cost of Living under the chairmanship of the Hon. President to recommend necessary policy and pragmatic solutions to the Cabinet of Ministers for maintaining the stability of the cost of living, whilst ensuring that food and other essential materials are supplied to the market without shortage in the face of the current economic situation in the country and to establish the Food Security Council to assist the said committee, under the chairmanship of the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-08-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2022-08-08",
    "description": "Establishment of Cabinet Sub-Committees",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11672",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-08-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found appropriate to establish Cabinet  Sub\u2011Committees, enabling to devote more time at the Meetings of the Cabinet of Ministers to take policy decisions and to submit recommendations on Cabinet Memoranda forwarded in relation to the fields where decisions have to be taken after an in\u2011depth study pertaining to legal and other issues contained therein. Accordingly, Cabinet approved the proposals made by the Hon. President to establish the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Public Expenditure Management under the chairmanship of the Hon. President to submit policy recommendations regarding public expenditure proposals such as commencement of new projects and procurement activities to the Cabinet and to establish the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Establishment Matters under the chairmanship of the Hon. Prime Minister to submit policy recommendations to the Cabinet having studied on the proposals submitted  regarding the establishment matters such as appointments, promotions, transfers and disciplinary actions in the public service."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-08-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2022-08-08",
    "description": "Amending the Shop and Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act No.19 of 1954",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11671",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-08-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, a host of businesses such as Knowledge Process Outsourcing Institutions, Business  Process Outsourcing Institutions, Back Offices which handle accounts, administrative and technical activities of institutions located in other countries and Businesses Institutions enabling Information Communication Technology services have been established in major cities of the country. Owing to the nature of such businesses, the employees employed therein have to work according to the time of those countries. However, according to the  Shop and Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act No.19 of 1954, only limited number of employments are allowed for female employees to work after 6.00 pm. Under this backdrop, existing restrictive legal provisions regarding the employment of women at night have found to be amended. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment for taking necessary action to amend the  Shop and Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act No.19 of 1954, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
