    "doc_id": "2022-05-02-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-05-02",
    "description": "Creation of a Digital Channel for departing passengers in Terminal - 1 of the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA), Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11571",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Airport & Aviation Services (Sri Lanka) (Private) Limited (AASL) has planned to implement several multi-dimensional improvements to enhance the efficiency of the operations of the Bandaranaike International Airport, Katunayake. Accordingly, a proposal has been made to implement a pilot project for introduction of a digital channel for the passengers departing from Terminal-1, based on the concept \u201cIATA One ID\u201d of the International Air Transport Association. As such, by installing e-gates/Face pods at the entrance to the departure terminal and verifying that they are with possession of a valid e-ticket to confirm their identity, it will be convenient to complete the check-in process of the passengers. Therefore, the Cabinet decided to grant its approval to implement a pilot project for the purpose as proposed by the Minister of Tourism."
  },
  {
