    "date_str": "2022-04-25",
    "description": "Drafting the Twenty First Amendment to the Constitution based on the Nineteenth and Twentieth Amendments to the Constitution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11558",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-04-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Several parties representing different strata of politics, profession and society have emphasized that it would be appropriate to introduce proper amendments to the Constitution in view of establishing political, economic and social stability to find solutions for the current economic crisis that has emerged within the prevailing atmosphere in the country. The Cabinet, having taken into consideration this situation, reached the following decisions as per a proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister: \n\n*\tto appoint a Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee to provide necessary guidance to the Legal Draftsman to prepare a preliminary draft Bill expeditiously, based on the constructive matters      in the Nineteenth and Twentieth Amendments to the Constitution to introduce the Twenty First Amendment, conferring more powers to Parliament while further strengthening democracy.\n\n*\tto authorize the Hon. Prime Minister to move a resolution in Parliament to appoint a Parliamentary Select Committee to discuss the Preliminary draft Bill to be prepared as above and the proposals on Amendments to the Constitution that have already been submitted to Parliament and prepare a draft on a reached consensus."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-04-25-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-04-25",
    "description": "Establishment of a mechanism to appraise financial proposals related to foreign exchange and energy supply presented by various parties",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11557",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-04-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Various friendly countries, international suppliers and local private sector offer various types of bilateral concessional loans, proposals pertaining to the energy supply and the energy sectors as remedies for the foreign exchange crisis prevailing in the country. Although, it was observed that certain proposals so submitted are effective to overcome the foreign exchange crisis experienced by country at present, there is no room in the existing procedures in order to approach further action on such proposals. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister to appoint a Committee chaired by the Secretary to the Prime Minister and with participation of four (04) Ministry Secretaries to analyze those proposals considering the timely importance of the same and submit recommendations on action be taken, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-04-25-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-04-25",
    "description": "Awarding Research Grants from the Eurasia Foundation in Japan to \tGeneral Sir John Kotelawala Defence University",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11556",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-04-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Measures have been taken by the  Eurasia Foundation in Japan to provide a Grant of US$ 42,000 as a Research grant to General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University for the conducting a course under the title of 'Cultural Linkages towards an Asian Ideology'. As such, the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to recruit 200 students under the said Grant and conduct the relevant Course, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-04-25-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-04-25",
    "description": "Issuance of Long Term Residence Visa for Foreign Investors",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11555",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-04-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201103\u201107 has granted approval to introduce a new methodology for the issuance of long term Residence Visa in lieu of the previously implemented methodology. Accordingly, the proposals pertaining to the issuance of long term Residence Visa under the said methodology submitted by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence as follows, were approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tIssuance of long term Residence Visa for 5 to 10 years for foreigners and Directors of Foreign Companies together with their spouses and dependents, who invest at least US$ 75,000 or more in Condominium property, depending on the amount of US dollars so invested.\n\n*\tImplementing a programme called \u201cGolden Paradise Visa Programme\u201d enabling to issue Visa for expatriates for a period of 10 years who deposit at least US$ 100,000 in a Commercial Bank recognized by the Central Bank of Sri lanka."
  },
  {
