    "doc_id": "2022-02-14-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-02-14",
    "description": "Integrating non-motorized modes of transport with the transport system of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11463",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The present active vehicle fleet of Sri Lanka is over 05 million, showing a three-fold increase than the year 2000. It is observed that this is due to the increase in the import of private vehicles particularly Three Wheeler, Motor Bikes and Motor Cars. Further, it appears that there is a great tendency for the use of private vehicles due to the increase of income level and the difficulties encountered when using the existing public transport service and the rapid increase of the use of private vehicles has resulted in decrease of the use of non motorized modes of transport. The use of non-motorized modes of transport will cause a positive impact on minimizing air pollution, the physical health, air quality, environment, climate change and personnel finance. Therefore, it has been identified that integrating the non-motorized modes with the existing transport system would be appropriate  to accrue the economical and environmental benefits.  Accordingly, the Cabinet having taken into consideration the matters submitted by the Minister of Environment, granted its concurrence for the relevant Ministries and Institutes to take the following action  under an integrated approach:\n\n    \u2022 Marking bicycle lanes for existing roads in an appropriate manner and upgrading of the existing walking paths.\n\n    \u2022 Inclusion of bicycle lanes and walking paths for roads to be constructed in future\n\n    \u2022 Taking necessary action to promote the use of bicycles among the government officers; and\n\n    \u2022 Providing necessary facilities including bicycle parking facility and accessibility for the bicycle users in the offices."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-14-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-02-14",
    "description": "Preparing a Road Map and a Strategic Plan to make Sri Lanka a Carbon Net Zero Country in 2050",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11462",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- For a country to become a net zero in carbon, it must essentially reduce the  greenhouse gases emitted to the atmosphere and the ecosystems that absorb the carbon should be developed. It has been found the necessity of preparing a Road Map and  a Strategic Plan to convert Sri Lanka a Carbon Net Zero Country by 2050. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to prepare a Road Map and five year Strategic Plan where the progress is reviewed once in five years and amendments are made and to appoint a Committee comprising of experts with expertise in the field, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-14-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-02-14",
    "description": "Strengthening Sri Lanka Climate Fund (Private) Limited functioning under purview of the Ministry of Environment",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11461",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been reported through the Nationally Determined Contributions submitted to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change that the Government of Sri Lanka had taken a policy decision to convert Sri Lank a Carbon Net Zero Country by 2050.  Sri Lanka Climate Fund (Private) Limited functioning under purview of the Ministry of Environment  has been established to contribute the tasks of minimizing the greenhouse gas emission. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to take necessary action to structurally strengthen the duties and functions of the said Institute to meet the present-day needs enabling to obtain the maximum contribution to convert Sri Lanka  a Carbon Net Zero Country, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-14-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-02-14",
    "description": "Green Sri Lanka- \u201cOne Person-One Plant\u201d National Programme - 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11460",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A provision of Rs.2000/- million has been allocated under budget proposals - 2022, to implement a suitable programme to increase the forest cover up to 30% by 2025 while preserving the existing forests in Sri Lanka and to increase the forestation through beneficial plants having removed invasive plants while  protecting water catchment areas. Accordingly, the Ministry of Wildlife and Forest Conservation has taken measures to implement a National Programme  on \u201cOne Person-One Plant\u201d. Under the said programme, it is expected to implement following projects.\n\n* \tEstablishment of 200 forest villages\n\n* Implementation of Tree Plantation Programms in Schools and National   Educational Institutes in Sri Lanka.\n\n* \tEstablishment of Island Wide Herbal Gardens\n\n* \tImplementation of Tree Plantation Programms in Religious Places.\n\n* \tImplementation of Tree Plantation Programms in watersheds of reservoirs, irrigation reserves and catchment areas.\n\n* Implementation of Tree Plantation Programms in the lands owned by Government Institutions, Semi-Government Institutions, Corporations, Boards and Statuary Boards.\n\n*\tImplementation of Tree Plantation Programms in the lands owned by Plantation Companies and privately owned lands.\n\n*\tEstablishment of Island wide Nurseries.\n\n*\tImplementation of a series of publicity campaigns to educate school children and the Community on the Wildlife and Forest Conservation.\n\n* \tIdentification of suitable plant species for forestation and implementation of a research programme to carry out development programmes together with the Universities.\n\n\tIt is expected to implement these projects under the guidance of the District Sectaries and Divisional Secretaries. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence to implement the said programme as per the proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Conservation."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-14-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-02-14",
    "description": "Providing a wheat flour subsidy for Estate Workers' Families",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11459",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2022\u201101\u201118 has granted approval to the proposals in the memorandum submitted by the Minister of Finance on \u201cTo notify the Cabinet of Ministers on implementation of Key proposals to mitigate the impact of the economic difficulties encountered by the people\u201d. Among those proposals, the proposal on the provision of a wheat flour subsidy for Estate Worker's Families was considered by a Committee headed by the Minister of Trade and submitted recommendations. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to provide 15 kg of wheat flour per month for 115,867 beneficiary families identified as per the recommendation of the said committee, under concessionary prices, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-14-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-02-14",
    "description": "Establishment of a Mini Super Market Chain (Home Shop) for Women Entrepreneurs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11458",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A provision of Rs.15,000 million has been allocated under the budget 2022 for the programme for the Establishment of  a Mini Super Market Chain (Home Shop) for Women Entrepreneurs with the objective of \u201ccreating a woman entrepreneur in every village\u201d by offering entrepreneurial guidance and assisting them in finding seed capital, having identified women entrepreneurs in rural family units who are interested in entrepreneurship. The identification of the relevant entrepreneurs is done by the Divisional Secretaries under the guidance of the Divisional Development Committee on the instructions of the Presidential Task Force on Poverty Alleviation. The selected woman entrepreneur will be able to set aside some space for this purpose, under one of the following methods,  either by allocating 200-400 square feet from a part of her home or renovating the house or by getting newly constructed by the Urban Development Authority or the National Housing Development Authority. Relevant Mini Super Markets are to be connected through a computer network and equipment and furniture needed for those shops will be provided by the Government. Plans have been made to supply consumer items for sale to women entrepreneurs through cooperative societies. Relevant beneficiaries will be able to purchase essential commodities including locally produced food items amounting to Rs.2000/- under the proposed Relief Basket Programme through a digital card given for low income earning families selected on special criteria. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to take necessary action to implement the said programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-14-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-02-14",
    "description": "Home Economy Security (Relief Basket) Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11457",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Provisions have been allocated to implement an Extensive Home Economy Security National Programme, through the National Budget proposals 2022.  Home Economy Security (Relief Basket) Programme has been identified as one amongst them. Under the said programme, 40 low income earning families are selected on the recommendation of the Divisional Secretary, based on special criteria, from each Grama Niladhari Division in order to ease the pressure of the hike of cost of living and such beneficiaries are issued a digital card worth of Rs 2000/- enabling to purchase goods thereby paving the way to purchase locally produced essential items and other consumer items, using that digital card, through mini super markets which are established under the Home Economy Security National Programme and operated by women entrepreneurs and. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to take necessary action to implement the said programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
