    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Commercial Law Reforms Sub-Committee appointed under the Special Unit of the Ministry of Justice has found the need to study on the matters related to the field of arbitration in Sri Lanka and introduce a new Act for arbitration. The said Sub\u2011Committee has further recommended the necessity of imposing provisions by the proposed Act so as to resolve the current impediments both at the stage of arbitration and at the stage of the enforcement of arbitration decisions, enabling to encourage large scale local and foreign investments, in Sri Lanka.  Accordingly, the the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft an Arbitration Bill, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-07-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-02-07",
    "description": "Investment Disputes High Court Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11453",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Minister of Justice has instructed the Commercial Law Reforms Sub\u2011Committee appointed under the Special Unit of the Ministry of Justice to submit recommendations on the legal reforms to be made to create a legal environment in Sri Lanka which is conducive to investment. Accordingly, the said committee has proposed to establish an Investment Disputes High Court with a judicial power to hear and give verdicts relating to the cases of 'disputes' within the financial limits of Rs.50 million which may arise from an initial investment of Rs.100 million or more. Therefore. the the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a bill for the purpose, incorporating relevant provisions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-07-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-02-07",
    "description": "Construction of an Organic Fertilizer Manufacturing Yard for the Mahaweli Knuckles Organic Agriculture Zone",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11452",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Moragahakanda, Kalu Gaga Mahaweli \u201cF\u201d Zone has been declared as a sustainable development zone where the organic agricultural products are produced, through a Gazette Extraordinary Notification as per the provisions of the Mahaweli Authority Act. It is expected to increase the income of farmer community through the production of agricultural crops using non-toxic organic inputs and to achieve the targets of national organic agricultural crops products with the contribution of the farmers with the high knowledge on organic farming.  It has been planned to construct 02 Organic Fertilizer Manufacturing Yards equipped with the necessary laboratory facilities in Wallawaya and Guruwela Mahweli Zones with a view to manufacturing organic fertilizer required for long term crop cultivation within the same zones. As the first phase of the same, the Wallawaya Organic Fertilizer Manufacturing Yard has been planed to be established  and it has been predicted that 2000 MT of fertilizer could be produced from the said yard annually. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation to award the contract for the construction of the said Organic Fertilizer Yard to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau as a direct contract, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-07-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-02-07",
    "description": "Implementation of the Sri Lanka Unique Digital Identity (SL-UDI) Framework",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11451",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has decided to implement the task of establishing the  Sri Lanka Unique Digital Identity (SL-UDI) Framework prioritizing as a national level programme. Under the said proposed Digital Identity Framework, it is expected to introduce an irrefutable foundation/physical identity instrument based on biometrics, digital credential enabling the representation of persons within the Cyber space and the unique identification within Digital, Physical and hybrid environments by tight coupling of the said two devices. It has been agreed during the bilateral discussions held between the Hon. Prime Minister of India and H.E. the President of Sri Lanka in December, 2019 to provide a grant of the Indian Government for the implementation of the Sri Lanka Unique Digital Identity. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to make the relevant arrangements to sign an MoU for obtaining the said grant and to implement the proposed project under the said grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-07-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-02-07",
    "description": "Entering into Agreements for the implementation of a Research Project between the La Jolla Institute, USA and General Sir john Kotelawala Defence University (KDU)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11450",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- An education collaboration is maintained  between  the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University (KDU) and La Jolla Institute, USA for the Allergy and Immunology, from 2017 and accordingly, funds amounting to US$ 505,840 have been received to the General Sir john Kotelawala Defence University (KDU) for implementing research projects. Both parties have reached a consensus to develop the existing education collaboration further with a view to promoting research tasks for early detection, understanding and reduction of Tuberculosis and exchanging of students and staff. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to sign a Sub-award Agreement and Material Transfer Agreement pertaining to the implementation of the relevant Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-31-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2022-01-31",
    "description": "Rural Development Programme of \u201cGama Samaga Pilisandarak (Dialogue with the Village) - Hundred Thousand Works through the Budget\u201d",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11449",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-31",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to a proposal made by the Budget - 2022 with a view to strengthening the production economy, it has been planned to implement the Rural Development Programme \u201cGama Samaga Pilisandarak (Dialogue with the Village) - Hundred Thousand Works through the Budget\u201d covering 14,021 Grama Niladhari Divisions in 336 Divisional Secretariat Divisions countrywide.  Under this programme, the projects identification process has been entirely decentralized so as to identify the public requirements by the public itself. Accordingly, the Cabinet noted the matters furnished by the Minister of Finance informing that arrangements have been made to commence the planned programme on 03rd February 2022."
  },
  {
