    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Green Power Development & Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Project is implemented under the funds of the Asian Development Bank and it has been planed to develop the Ambalngoda and Pannala Grid Substations and to provide 02 Spare Transformers under lot B of the Package 8 of the said Project. International Competitive Bids have been invited for this under the Single-Stage Two Envelope procedure and 04 Bids have been received. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power to award the relevant procurement to the M/s Ceylex Engineering (Pvt) Ltd as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Progress of Mega Scale Development Projects by the end of Third Quarter - 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11343",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- 332 Mega Scale Development Projects are being implemented under 47 Ministries exceeding Rs. 1000 million in the year 2021 and their duration will expand up to 2030. The total investment value of these projects is Rs. 6899 billion. 95 projects out of which amounting to Rs. 2642 billion in value are new projects commenced in the year 2021 to achieve the goals of the Government Policy Framework \u201cVistas of Prosperity and Splendour\u201d. Under this, projects have been commenced pertaining to the fields of health, education, potable water supply, road network development, improvement of irrigation system and township and rural development. The smooth functioning of these projects has been hampered by the shortage of building materials and labours, restrictions on imports as well as  immigration and emigration due to  the COVID-19 pandemic situation prevailing in the country. Nevertheless, an amount of 63% out of the targeted expenditure of Rs 448 billion has been spent for these projects. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Development Co-ordination and Monitoring to seek the participation of the Ministry of Economic Policies and Plan Implementation, Ministry of Finance and the senior officials of other relevant Government institutions for the progress review meetings conducted monthly with a view to solving the problems which arisen pertaining to the said projects enabling to implement the said projects within the stipulated time frames and to receive the benefits of the same to the General public, was approved  by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Submission of the Interim Report of the Committee appointed on Digital Banking, Blockchain Technology and Crypto-currency",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11342",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet was granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201110\u201105 to appoint a Committee to submit recommendations to the Cabinet, on the possible laws and regulations for attracting investments to the Digital Banking, Blockchain Technology and Crypto\u2011currency related Companies. Accordingly, a Committee has been appointed comprising 8 members under the chairmanship of Mr. Sujeewa Mudalige.  The Interim Report submitted by the said Committee was brought to the notice of the Cabinet at this meeting. As such, it was decided to grant its concurrence to the proposals made by the Minister of Development Co\u2011ordination and Monitoring, to submit the final report of the said Committee by 2022\u201106\u201130 and to appoint another two technical professionals working in the relevant field as its members to assist the Committee."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Oil & Gas Company",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11341",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been confirmed that there are petroleum and natural gas deposits available in the country, according to the explorations conducted in the M2 block of the Mannar Basin during the period from 2011 to 2013. Opportunities may arise in reducing reliance on importation of fossil fuel to meet domestic requirements by producing petroleum and natural gas and in earning foreign currency by becoming an exporter of natural gas in future. It has been declared by the \u201cNational Policy on Natural Gas of Sri Lanka\u201d that action will be taken by the Government to establish a National Gas Company under the Public\u2011Private Partnership Model in respect of storage, construction of pipelines, development, ownership and operation of transport and distribution infrastructure facilities including local gas exploration and production, enabling to engage in exploration and production activities of commercial viability. It has been planned to establish the said Company as a Subsidiary Company of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation and the said Company will be vested with the responsibility of discharging the duties and functions assigned by Part V of the Petroleum Resources Act, No.21 of 2021. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to establish the \u201cNational Oil & Gas Company\u201d under the Companies Act, No.7 of 2007."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Agreement on Co-operation and Mutual Administrative Assistance in Customs Matters between Sri Lanka and Vietnam",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11340",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Consequent to a series of bilateral discussions held between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Vietnam, it has been proposed to enter into an Agreement on Co\u2011operation and Mutual Administrative Assistance in Customs matters between the two countries. Accordingly, this proposed trade agreement will contribute for reducing trade transaction cost, accurate valuation and collection of border taxes and enforcement of regulations on prohibition, restriction and controlling of movement of restricted goods. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to sign the proposed agreement agreed to between the two parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Enhancement of the National Traffic Database and Capacity Building",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11339",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the increase in volume of traffic, the necessity has arisen to establish a mechanism for the management of traffic on national highways, especially on roads within the City of Colombo. With a view to updating the existing data at the Road Development Authority for the purpose, a request has already been made through the Department of External Resources to seek the assistance of the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA). Under the proposed programme, the Ministry of Highways intends to formulate a national level Traffic Data Management Plan, establish a foundation for collecting traffic data, design an automated Traffic Database Management System and enhance the Traffic Demand Analysis Capability. For this, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways to implement the \u201cEnhancement of National Traffic Database and Capacity Building Project\u201d by securing a grant from the KOICA and to sign a Record of Discussions between the Ministry of Highways and KOICA confirming the implementation of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Digitalization of Expressway Manual Toll Collection via LANKAQR",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11338",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to reducing the use of physical currency in Sri Lanka, action is being taken by the Government in association with all licensed financial institutions to popularize the LANKAQR payment method. As one of its steps, it has been proposed to introduce LANKAQR also for the Manual Toll Collection gates of the Expressways managed by the Road Development Authority (RDA). This will enable the drivers using the Expressways to make the relevant payments within 8-10 seconds by entering the respective amount in his mobile phone and scanning the QR Code at the toll collection gate through a LANKAQR enabled mobile payment app of any Bank. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways to implement the said payment mechanism, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Revision of laws relating to journalists and media institutions and formulation of policies and ethics",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11337",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the global growth in the mass media and communication sectors and paying special attention to the existing laws for media standardization in Sri Lanka, international laws and the performance of national and international media institutions and socio\u2011cultural identity, focus has been paid towards presentation of a Sri Lankan Mass Media Policy, setting up the background for moulding media professionals with esteemed professionalism parallel to that, socialization of knowledge, comprehension and communication strategies on the use and behaviour of new media including social media and facilitating the adaption to digital technology. For this, the necessity of amending the prevailing laws and preparation of the policies and ethics pertaining to journalists and media institutions to suit the present needs, has been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to appoint a Committee with the representation of intellects in the Public and Private sectors and in the fields such as media, marketing, education, law, administration and economics, to submit recommendations to the Cabinet for the said purposes, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-23-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-11-23",
    "description": "Declaration of new boundaries of the Ampara Sanctuary",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11336",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Galoya Valley North\u2011East Sanctuary also known as Ampara Sanctuary with an area of 9,323.96 hectares has been declared as a Sanctuary in the year 1954 as per the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance. The Ampara town, which was thereafter established as a Central City under the Galoya Farmer Colonization Project, has developed extensively by now. Approval of the Cabinet has been granted on 2009\u201105\u201120 to remove the plots of lands identified as developed in the Ampara Development Plan for having developed the lands located in the Sanctuary for providing various common amenities of the Government and Government Affiliations such as Municipal Council grounds and temples and some plots of lands handed over to private parties under State sponsorship for development and declare new boundaries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife & Forest Conservation to further maintain the densely forested area which is frequented by elephants and other wildlife and identified in the territory pertaining to the Ampara Development Plan as a part of the Sanctuary Zone, remove and declare the densely populated and developed areas in the extent of 46.81 hectares belonging to the Sanctuary and to publish the new boundaries in the Gazette and submit the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Appointment of a Committee to identify the Maritime Law related legal provisions to suit the local and international requirements",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11335",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- In promoting Sri Lanka as a maritime hub considering its strategic location in the middle of the Indian Ocean, it has been identified the necessity of setting up the legal infrastructure facilities, taking into consideration the international requirements in terms of enacting domestic laws in line with the international treaties and ratifying the international treaties. Previously, a Committee has been appointed under the chairmanship of President's Counsel Mr. P.A. Rathnayake, a former Judge of the Supreme Court to study the related matters and action has not been pursued on the recommendations made by the said Committee. When the damages caused by the accidents of the vessels, MT New Diamond and MV X\u2011Press Pearl within the Sri Lankan waters recently are considered, the necessity of introducing new laws has been highlighted. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Ports & Shipping and the Minister of Justice to appoint a Committee comprising the representatives of the relevant institutions under the chairmanship of President's Counsel Mr. Chandaka Jayasundere, to identify the laws either existing or to be introduced anew or to be amended and submit a Report including recommendations in this regard, also taking into consideration the Report submitted by the former Committee appointed under the chairmanship of Mr. P. A. Rathnayake, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Amendment to the Provincial Councils (Transfer of Stamp Duty) Act, No.13 of 2011",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11334",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet of Ministers has been granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201102\u201115 to amend the Provincial Councils (Transfer of Stamp Duty) Act, No.13 of 2011, incorporating the provisions enabling to refund the Stamp Duty or Penalty payment made in excess or erroneously, when such request is made to refund such Stamp Duty or Penalty remitted by a person in excess or erroneously. Accordingly, clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to publish the said draft Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Personal Data Protection Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11333",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Personal Data Protection Bill has been drafted to provide for ensuring the security of the personal data of institutions such as Government Institutions, banks, telephone facilities providers and hospitals in accumulating and using such data and developing the digital economy in Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity of the Minister of Technology to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Implementation of Tourism Promotional Campaigns aiming the upcoming Holiday Season",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11332",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- In view of restoring tourism affected due to the COVID\u201119 pandemic situation, during the tourism season of 2021/2022 and attracting tourists, collective efforts are being taken by all tourism related stakeholders including airlines. Approval of the Cabinet of Ministers has been previously granted to appoint Destination Representation Companies (DRC) and Public Relation (PR) Companies in key tourism markets for a period of 05 years as part of the Global Communication Campaigns to be implemented by the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau (SLTPB). As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to implement a tourism promotion campaign targeting the United Kingdom, Germany and France which require special attention as tourism markets and India, the prominent source market in the region of Asia as an interim measure in the said Global Tourism Promotion Campaign, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Awarding procurements for supply of Aviation Fuel for SriLankan Airlines at 21 destination Airports",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11331",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been called following the Limited International Bidding process to select institutions that supply fuel for the flights of SriLankan Airlines at 21 destination airports, worldwide. The validity period of the relevant procurement is 12 to 24 months and 26 responsive bids have been received for 21 airports. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism, to award the relevant procurements to the  suppliers selected for 21 destination airports, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Agreement on Cooperation and Mutual Administrative Assistance in Customs Matters between Sri Lanka and Russia",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11330",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Following a series of bilateral discussions conducted between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Russia, the two countries are in agreement to enter into a bilateral agreement to facilitate legitimate trade through transparent and predictable customs procedures. The proposed agreement would envisage the reduction of trade transaction cost, accurate valuation and collection of border taxes, ensure enforcement of regulation on prohibitions, restrictions and control of movement of restricted goods. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance, to sign the proposed agreement between the two parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Implementation of Multi - purpose projects in the plots of land reserved for  the construction of post offices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11329",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Department of Sri Lanka Posts is a network of  654 main post offices and 3,410 of sub post offices while 154 of 654 main post offices are maintained in rented out private buildings. Although a few plots of land have been allotted in several provinces to construct buildings for post offices, the Department has not been able to construct the proposed buildings due to the insufficient funds available. At present, the Department has focused its attention on minimizing the deficit between their income and expenditure, under which the need has been found to identify new income generating sources. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to implement multi-purpose projects in the lands allotted for the department under the Public-Private Partnership mechanism in order to secure required accommodation facilities for the Department of Posts as well as to secure an additional income generating source, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Presidential Media Awards Ceremony - 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11328",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government  policy statement \u201cVistas of Prosperity and Splendour\u201dhas identified that it is a responsibility of the Government to secure a clear and independent environment required for the performance of media institutions and the professionals engaged in the media institutions to act for safeguarding the freedom of speech and publication to the most with a view to creating a society that suits to the 21st century. Accordingly, the Presidential Media Awards Ceremony has been planned to conduct more properly with the objective of encouraging media persons for maintaining the exquisite standards of media as well as the electronic, print and web media contents in an accountable and independent manner so that the subscriber expectations could be achieved. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to  conduct the Presidential Media Awards Ceremony- 2022 to evaluate journalists based on their creations made in 2021 in all the three languages, sinhala, Tamil and English, covering six (06) fields of broadcasting, television, printed media, web sites, school media and media researches, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-11-15-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-11-15",
    "description": "Recognition of Cinema as an Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11327",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-11-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Several outstanding films have been produced in the cinema industry of Sri Lanka and many internationally reputed and talented film makers also have been introduced to the world cinema from Sri Lanka. However, due to not being legally declared the local cinema as an industry, its extent and development have been restricted to the small-scale local market. Also, the local cinema industry is facing immense crises amidst the Covid-19 global pandemic situation. It has been identified that development and promotion of cinema industry can bring about several benefits such as  generation of a number of livelihoods, modernization in social, cultural and as well as in economic spheres, and making a contribution to the tourism and education sectors with a considerable contribution to the economy. It has also been observed that, in most of the countries where a developed cinema industry can be found, the development has taken place after the recognition of cinema as an industry by those countries. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs and the Minister of Industries, to register cinema as an industry so as to promote the cinema industry in Sri Lanka and gain international recognition for the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
