    "date_str": "2021-05-17",
    "description": "Amendment of Land Acquisition (Payment of Compensation) Regulations - 2013",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11067",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to pay compensation for 20 identified projects under Land Acquisition and Resettlement Committee (LARC) and Land Acquisition and Resettlement Special Committee (SUPER LARC) systems and relevant regulations have been enacted for the purpose as per the provisions of the Land Acquisition Act. The Cabinet has granted approval to adopt the same system to pay compensation for the lands so acquired under the following projects:\n\ni. \tMetro Colombo Urban Development project.\nii. \tRailway Track project from Kurunegala to Habarana via Dambulla.\niii. \tStrategic City Development Programmes.\niv. \tGrid Sub\u2011Stations and Transmission Lines project under the funds of the Asian Development Bank.\n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by the Minister of Lands to submit the amended Land Acquisition (Payment of Compensation) Regulations\u2011 2013 published in the Gazette dated 2021\u201103\u201118 for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-17-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-05-17",
    "description": "Conservation of the environment through promotion of Green Entrepreneurship",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11066",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tThe Government Policy 'Vistas of Prosperity and Spelndour' has proposed to increase the total forest layer of the country up to 30%. Accordingly, 'Surakimu Ganga' National Environment Conservation Programme and 'Husma Dena Thuru' Tree Planting Programme are being implemented under the Ministry of Environment, through a number of stakeholders including Government Institutions, Private Sector, Non-Government Organizations (NGOs') and Voluntary Organizations islandwide. In view of meeting the sapling need of the said programmes and creating green entrepreneurs while encouraging the rural community, it has been planned to generate 650 new plant nursery operators all over Sri Lanka. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to provide a formal training to 650 low\u2011income families to be selected under the said programme as nursery plant operators and grant opportunity to function as green entrepreneurs, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-17-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-05-17",
    "description": "Vesting a land belonging to the Department of Irrigation to the Institute of \tIndigenous Medicine, University of Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11065",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Irrigation has extended its concurrence to transfer a land in extent of 0.1765 hectares located at No.330 of Dr.N.M Perera Road, Colombo 08, to the Institute of Indigenous Medicine. The Board of Management of the said Institute has decided to construct a multi-purpose building complex with 08 stories comprised of a clinical skills development laboratory and study hall, an indigenous food processing training centre with a restaurant and concurrence of the Urban Development Authority has been given for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to transfer the said land to the  Institute of Indigenous Medicine, University of Colombo, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-17-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-05-17",
    "description": "Granting insurance entitlements for Sri Lankan migrant workers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11064",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- A migrant worker insurance coverage had been made by the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment for Sri Lankan migrant workers and compensations will paid through this cover subject to a maximum of Rs.600,000/-and Rs.400,000/- respectively in the event of death or permanent disability of a migrant worker. However, it does not provide any insurance coverage for industrial or domestic accidents caused, diseases and also for taking medical treatments for mental and health issues caused due to harassment or abuses by employers and for the loss of jobs due to the Covid-19 pandemic. Therefore,  the proposal made by the Minister of labour to introduce a suitable insurance coverage for Sri Lankan migrant workers taking into consideration the above facts, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-17-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-05-17",
    "description": "Establishment of Welikada Prison Complex at Millewe, Horana and utilization of the premises of Welikada Prison for a Mixed Urban Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11063",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Welikada Prison Complex, located on a 42-acre land, is planned to be relocated on a land called Millewa Watta, Horana in extent of 200 acres. Taking into consideration the future needs, it has also been planned to construct a new prison complex on the said land and transfer the land on which the Welikada prison is located at present to the Urban Development Authority to grant the same to the formally selected local and foreign investors on long term lease basis to carry out development projects. Accordingly, proposals of the Memorandum submitted jointly by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing and the Minister of Justice to implement the proposed project, were approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-17-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-05-17",
    "description": "Investment Strategy and Policy Framework - Selendiva Investment (Pvt.) Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11062",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the Cabinet approval granted on 2020\u201103\u201104 to form a state-owned Property Development Company with the objective of transforming the State-Owned Hospitality Portfolios to optimum performance level through appropriate restructuring, action was taken to establish the  Selendiva Investment (Pvt.) Ltd. with 100% ownership of the Treasury. State-owned Canwill Holdings (Pvt) Ltd., Hotel Developers (Lanka) PLC and Hotels Colombo Ltd have been vested in Selendiva Investment (Pvt.) Ltd at present. An Investment Facilitation Model based on Public Private Partnership has been planned by  Selendiva Investment (Pvt.) Ltd. with a view to facilitating the identified state-owned institutes and investments and under this, it has been identified to implement three (03) investment portfolios as 'Heritage Square in Colombo Fort', 'Real Estate Development' and 'State-Owned Hospitality Sector'. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to take necessary action for the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-10-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-05-10",
    "description": "Submission of the Gazette Notification published under Sri Lanka Export \tDevelopment Act No. 40 of 1979 to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11061",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Any good imported for any project with an investment of 50US$ million or more which implemented on 2019\u201103\u201106 or later has been exempted from CESS prior to the commencement of the commercial operations of that project. However, since some large scale projects commence its commercial operations in stages before the completion of the entire project, the relevant provisions for CESS exemption have not been made available for such projects. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to submit the Gazette Notification No.2219/36 dated 2021\u201103\u201117 published under Sri Lanka Export Development Act No. 40 of 1979 imposing the provisions for CESS exemption of such projects as well, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-10-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-05-10",
    "description": "Project of Silting of Reservoirs controlled by the Sri Lanka Mahaweli \tAuthority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11060",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Among the primary objectives of the construction of the Mahaweli Reservoirs, priority has been given to the supply of drinking water, providing water for agriculture and the generation of renewable energy. Nevertheless, the capacity of many of such reservoirs has been significantly reduced due to siltation, making it difficult to achieve the desired objectives of such reservoirs. It has been planned to implement a programme to remove silt and classify such silt in order to use them. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation to obtain a local or international Consultancy Service to prepare a basic feasibility report obtaining required data for surveying including all details pertaining to Polgolla, Victoria, Randenigala, Rantambe, Kalawewa and Bowathanna Reservoirs and to call for competitive bids nationally or internationally to select a suitable entity to remove silt in such reservoirs based on the above feasibility report, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-10-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-05-10",
    "description": "Providing relief for continuing inter - provincial bus operations in the face of the COVID-19 pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11059",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet of Ministers had been granted previously to grant relief identified for the continuation of inter-provincial bus operations in the face of the COVID-19 pandemic, up to 2021\u201103\u201131. Taking into consideration the fact that bus operations do not function properly as the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic still remains, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to grant the following relief to the bus operators from 2021\u201104\u201101 to 2021\u201109\u201131, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n    \u2022 Charging only 50% of annual tender fees.\n    \u2022 Charging only 50% of the Expressway temporary permit fee."
  },
