    "date_str": "2021-04-19",
    "description": "'Youth Hub' - The Project for the establishment of the  High Impact Youth Community Centres",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11035",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- To lead an efficient social life by sharing ideas, existing facilities for Sri Lankan youth community to find solutions through negotiations for their educational, health, civil and political issues are inadequate. Specially, the opportunities and the locations available at divisional level for organizing and engaging voluntarily in such activities are very limited. As a remedy to this situation, it has been identified that it would be appropriate to create suitable locations for youths to gather at a familiar environment and to engage in productive activities by sharing experiences. For this purpose, it has been planned to identify the underutilized government schools and other buildings with sufficient spaces at divisional and district level and launch a programme to establish High Impact Youth Community Centres creating multiple opportunities and activities. It is also expected to construct Youth Community Centres in each Divisional Secretariat Divisions of the country within five years implementing as public private joined project and facilitating for various activities within 04 zones such as Youth Development Zone, Youth Entertainment Zone, Economic Zone, and Green Zone in the same centre. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Youth and Sports to implement the said programme at phase out level and to establish 25 centres covering all districts as the first phase of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-19-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-04-19",
    "description": "Implementation of Digitization of Terrestrial Television Broadcasting Project in Sri Lanka under the Japanese Loan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11034",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Terrestrial Television Broadcasting is evolving from Analog to Digital and it has been found necessary to adapt this system according to the world trend. Accordingly, required decisions had been made at several occasions to move to Analog to Digital Terrestrial Television Broadcasting system, but those decisions have not been implemented so far. It has been decided to introduce ISDB-T Technology to suit Sri Lanka, subsequent to a feasibility study conducted by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA). Adaption to the Digital Technology will enable to use a part of Frequency Spectrum utilized at present for wireless broadband services thus increasing  internet access in rural areas. Accordingly,  the joint proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Technology and the Minister of Mass Media to implement  Digitization of Terrestrial Television Broadcasting Project utilizing modern technology, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-19-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-04-19",
    "description": "Establishment of Hardy Institute of Technology",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11033",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- In line with the development needs in 1960s, the Hardy Institute of Technology has been set up as a Technical Training Institute to provide systematic engineering knowledge to the Technical Officers aiming the Galoya Development Project, the first multipurpose reservoir project of Sri Lanka. Subsequently, the scope and the structure of the said Institute has been changed at many occasions and at present, it functions as two separate institutes such as Hardy Technical College, offering National Diploma (NVQ - 5 Level) and Higher National Diploma (NVQ - 6 Level) to provide those who have missed the mainstream higher education with alternative higher education opportunities and as Hardy Advanced Technological Institute established under  Sri Lanka Institute of  Advanced Technological Education  conducting NDT Agricultural Programme which was conducted by the said Hardy Technical College earlier. Since it has been identified that the structure and the course content are required to be changed in order to create entrepreneurs enriched with high technical knowledge assisting to expedite the economic development  and expand the economy according to the economic programmes of the present Government, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to establish an independent institution named \u201cHardy Institute of Technology\u201d combining the said two institutions and to amend the relevant Acts for the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-19-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-04-19",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the University of Sri Jayewardenepura and the University of Sungkyunkwan in Republic of Korea",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11032",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to enter into an MoU between the University of Sri Jayewardenepura and the University of Sungkyunkwan in Republic of Korea for academic and cultural exchange in the areas  of Immunology and Molecular Medicine through enhancing the collaboration in undergraduate curriculum development in Immunology and Molecular Medicine, assisting in commencing the study programme and development and operation of innovative research programmes for secondary and junior college students in the community. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign the relevant MoU, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-19-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-04-19",
    "description": "Establishment of City Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11031",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Creation of globally competitive professionals equipped with competencies has been identified as a timely requirement in order to enhance the quality of highly demanding professions in the job market. Only about 20% out of the students who passed G.C.E. (A/L) and qualified for universities, get opportunities to enter into the state universities for studies and inclination of the rest of students towards the vocational education is not at a considerable level. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to establish City Universities as universities awarding degrees to suit with employment opportunities developing skills required for the production sectors in the relevant Districts and to get provided necessary legal provisions for the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Purchasing another 6 million doses of \u2018Sputnik V\u2019 Vaccine to prevent the spread of Covid \u2013 19",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11030",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201103\u201123 to purchase 7 million doses of \u2018Sputnik V\u2019 Vaccine at a cost of US$ 9.95 each to a sum of 69.65 US$ million upon the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee. The Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Health to purchase another 6 million doses of \u2018Sputnik V\u2019 Vaccine at the same price in addition to the aforesaid doses of vaccines."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Further extension of the validity period granted to open 'Special Deposit Accounts' under the Foreign Exchange Act No.12 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11029",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Relevant regulations have been issued under the Foreign Exchange Act No.12 of 2017, making provisions to open Special Deposit Accounts to be effective from April, 2020 with a view to encouraging the foreign exchange inflows into the country. Moreover, Cabinet approval has been granted to pay an additional interest with a view to further retaining the available deposits of the said accounts. Accordingly, as at March, 2021, total deposits in the said accounts amounted to US$ 360.3 million. Since the validity period granted for opening the said Special Deposit Accounts is due to be ended on 2021\u201104\u201107, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to further extend the validity period to encourage those are interested in making deposits in such accounts further and to issue regulations for the purpose in accordance with the provisions of the Foreign Exchange Act , was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Repealing the Tourism Act No 38 of 2005 and enacting a New Tourism Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11028",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau, Sri Lanka Convention Bureau and the Sri Lanka Institution of Tourism and Hotel Management were established, having divided the entire tourism sector into four major entities in terms of the provisions of the Tourism Act No 38 of 2005. However, due to the tourism sector being separated into 4 entitiess, it is observed that there have been negative impacts such as delays in coordinating relevant entities and wastage of resources etc. Therefore, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to repeal the Tourism Act No 38 of 2005 and to draft a bill to enact a New Tourism Act in order to ensure the sustainable development of the Tourism industry thereby taking necessary action to establish a new authority by the name of \u201cSri Lanka Tourism Authority\u201d having confederated the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau, Sri Lanka Convention Bureau."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Award of contracts to the suppliers for the supply of food items to the Department of Prisons for the year 2021/2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11027",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- National competitive bids have been called to select contractors for the supply of food items for the Department of Prisons for the year 2021/2022. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to award the relevant contracts for the selected suppliers for the supply of food items to the Department of Prisons for the period of 2021\u201104\u201116 to 2022\u201104\u201115, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Implementation of an Accelerated Procurement Process for implementing the Projects of Corporate Plan 2020-2025 of the National Water Supply and Drainage Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11026",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2021\u201101\u201111 granted approval to implement water and sewerage projects which included in the Corporate Plan 2020-2025. It has been planned to meet 78.8% of drinking water requirement of the households in the country by 2025 through the implementation of the proposed projects. In order to achieve this target, It has been scheduled to increase the present production capacity by 2.35 million cubic metres per day and supply and laying of around 40,000km of transmission and distribution pipe lines. Further, it has been found that the National Water Supply and Drainage Board takes more time for the procurement process than the time taken by the other institutions due to the complex nature of the water sector projects. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply to procure pipes and fittings under a centralized procurement system and to introduce a unit price system for the same and to introduce a Unit Rate procedure when awarding pipe laying contracts as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Revision of Tea Planting Subsidies currently paid to encourage the Tea Cultivation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11025",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The total tea production in the year 2019 was 300 million kg and approximately 75% out of which amounting to 225 million kg were manufactured by tea smallholdings sector. It has been identified the necessity of enhancing the productivity of tea smallholdings lands in order to maintain the tea production at the optimum level. It is required to encourage farmers to obtain the production target of 360 million kg of tea by the year 2025, since the attention of farmers for tea cultivation and replanting is insufficient due to the fact that it takes nearly 04 years to generate income by the replantation of tea and it will cost a lot of money. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to increase the Tea Replanting Subsidy and the Tea New Planting Subsidy of Rs. 400,000/- per hectare to Rs.500,000/- per hectare, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Opening of Batticaloa, Vauniya and Jaffna Dedicated Economic Centres",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11024",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Dedicated Economic Centre Programme has been initiated so as to sell the agricultural products of the farmers directly and to implement the price mechanism more efficiently through competition and 15 such Economic Centres are functioning countrywide at present. Accordingly, construction work of Batticaloa and Vauniya Dedicated Economic Centres have been completed and the construction work of the phase I of the Special Economic Centre in Jaffna has been completed by now. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to establish the Management Committee for the administration of the said Special Economic Center and to allocate business premises of such Economic Centres following a formal methodology, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-04-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-04-05",
    "description": "Establishment of Trusted Digital Repository at the National Archives",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11023",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-04-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of National Archives holds valuable archives from the Dutch and British administration since the year 1640 and those created after independence and the legal deposits of all publications including newspapers published from the the 19th Century. This Department receives a large number of documents daily including digital publications and documents, radio and television broadcasting, websites and emails etc. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to establish a trusted digital repository, following the international standards on digital preservation in order to ensure the reliability and authenticity of the said digital records, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Amendment to the Civil Procedure Code",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11022",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "Recently, motor traffic accidents have alarmingly increased. In order to seek reliefs against such an accident, a case has to be filed in a Civil Court. Here, the victim or his heir has to produce Medico Legal Report and other medical reports and those reports will then be inevitably marked as 'subject to proof'. The victim or his heir is responsible to ensure that the Medical Officer will appear in Courts to testify to prove the contents in the said reports. Since such a motor traffic accident case takes 10 or 12 years of prolonged period for its conclusion, the Government has to incur an unnecessary expenditure burden to summon the relevant Medical Officer to the Court if he serves at a distant location and at the same time, he loses the opportunity to engage his precious time in professional activities. Taking into consideration these matters, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation to amend the Civil Procedure Code, to provide for considering the Medico-Legal Report, Post Mortem Report and the Bed Head Ticket as prima facie evidence and to enable to provide for shifting the burden of rebutting the Medico-Legal evidence when the defendant contests such evidence, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Preparation of the National Drinking Community Water Development Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11021",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "Subsequent to the establishment of the Department of National Community Water Supply, the said Department regulates and empowers the Community Based Organizations managed by the Community. Yet, the said Department has faced with a number of issues for not possessing the legal power required for the purpose. Taking into consideration these matters, the proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply to draft the National Drinking Community Water Development Act to enable formal and effective functioning of the Department of National Community Water Supply, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Amendment to the Firearms Ordinance, No.33 of 1916 (Chapter 182) amended by the Act, No.22 of 1996",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11020",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2007 06 13 to draft a Bill for further amending the Firearms Ordinance, No.33 of 1916 (Chapter 182) as last amended by the Act, No.22 of 1996. However, drafting of the said Bill has been delayed due to amendments proposed from time to time. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill incorporating all the relevant amendments to meet the present requirements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Awarding four civil works contract packages on rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance of the Colombo - Kandy Road (A001) (44+300 km to 100+000km)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11019",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "National Competitive Bids have been called for 04 civil works contract packages for rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance of the Colombo - Kandy Road (from 44km to 100 km) under the Asian Development Bank funded Integrated Road Investment Programme. Accordingly, 15 bidders have submitted 47 bids. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways to award the said relevant contract packages to the substantially responsive bidders selected as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Procurement of Design, Manufacture, Supply, Installation, Commissioning and handing over of a Single Sleeper Multiple Tie Tamping Machine for the Department of Sri Lanka Railways",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11018",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "With a view to enhancing the maintenance capacity of the Department of Sri Lanka Railways and reducing the maintenance cost, International Competitive Bids have been called for manufacturing and handing over of a Single Sleeper Multiple Tie Tamping Machine. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to award the relevant procurement to M/s Matisa Mat\u00e9riel Industriel S.A. - Switzerland, for a sum of US$ 4.96 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Introduction of a mechanism for the protection of consumers of petroleum",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11017",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "At the initial stage, the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation (CPC) was responsible for all petroleum industry related activities. However, a number of parties are currently involved in these activities. Even though the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka (PUCSL) has been appointed as the regulatory body of the petroleum industry, the functions of the said Commission has been limited to providing advice to and assisting the Ministry regarding policy and regulation of the lubricant industry. Under this condition, a practical mechanism has not been established for the protection of rights of the consumers of petroleum. Therefore, it has been proposed to establish an independent and transparent mechanism for handling and resolving consumer complaints under the supervision of the Ministry of Energy and the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka (PUCSL). In the implementation of the said mechanism, the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka (PUCSL), Consumer Affairs Authority, Sri Lanka Customs, Sri Lanka Police, Sri Lanka Standards Institute, Industrial Technology Institute and other relevant Government Institutes will join. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to implement the drafted 'Statement of Rights and Obligations of Consumers' and the 'Procedure for Handling Compliants and Resolution of Disputes' and to sign a Memorandum of Understanding with the relevant Government Institutes for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Allocation of land blocks from Regional Industrial Estates to set up industries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11016",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "The Regional Industrial Services Committee and the Project Evaluation Committee of the Ministry of Industries have recommended the allocation of 16 land blocks in the 09 Industrial Estates of Nalanda (Matale), Bataatha, Karandeniya, Udukawa, Embilipitiya, Kalutara, Batticaloa and Nawagampura, for investors to start up new industries. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to allocate the said land blocks on 35 year lease basis and subject to the condition of 'not transferable to other parties' and other relevant conditions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Establishment of Cyclotron Based Radio - Pharmaceutical Production Centre in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11015",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "Fluoro Deoxy Glucose (18F-FDG) which is a radioactive drug, is used for PET and CT tests to diagnose cancers. A special device called Cyclotron is used to produce this drug and this radioactive drug is imported from India since the required facilities are not available in Sri Lanka. Due to its radioactive decaying nature, about 97% of the strength of the drug losses when it is imported from India. Only 10 patients can be treated from the remaining capacity. Although, about 30,000 patients are required to undergo the relevant test annually,  only 1600 patients can be tested due to the above reason. It costs Rs. 54,000 to the government to test one patient using the imported drug and If the drug is manufactured locally, the cost can be reduced to Rs. 14,000. Taking into consideration this situation, the Government has planned to set up a Cyclotron based Radio-pharmaceutical Production Centre in Sri Lanka in the premises of Kotelawala Defence University Hospital, Werahera in collaboration with the Atomic Energy Board of Sri Lanka and Sir Jhon Kotelawala Defence University. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power to implement the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Obtaining service facilities from Sri Lanka Telecom to promote the services of the Department of Motor Traffic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11014",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "A large number of clients arrive in the Head Office of the Department of Motor Traffic, Werahera office and district level offices in order to obtain services rendered by the said Department. Since both clients and the staff of the Department are faced with difficulties in certain occasions due to the above reason, it has been planned to redress this matter by utilizing modern information and communication technology for reserving a time for the duties in advance, obtaining a number for the same, guiding to reach the relevant divisions for services according to service requirement of clients and notifying the relevant information to the client by SMS etc. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to implement the proposed project in association with Sri Lanka Telecom and to implement the same in the offices of Narahenpita and Werahara and 05 Districts offices where online facilities are available as the first phase and  thereafter implement in the rest of 19 District Offices as the second phase of the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Faculty of Agriculture, University of Ruhuna and the Graduate School of Environmental and life Sciences, Okayama University, Japan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11013",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "It has been proposed to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Faculty of Agriculture, University of Ruhuna and the Graduate School of Environmental and Life Science, Okayama University, Japan with a view to enhancing higher education cooperation and international relations. It has been planned to launch programmes for exchange of students, exchange of faculty and staff and to conduct collaborative research and to exchange research  information. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to enter into the said MoU for a period of five years initially, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Entering into a Cooperation Agreement between the University of Peradeniya and the International Development Research Center (IDRC), Canada",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11012",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "Various strategic methods have been  adopted by countries to control the spread of Covid - 19 pandemic and to minimize its damage. In this instance, it has been planned to implement a research project on the impact caused to women, children and less privileged social groups  due to the various strategies used by certain countries for the said purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to enter into a Cooperative Agreement between  the University of Peradeniya and the International Development Research Center (IDRC), Canada to implement the said project based on Sri Lanka and Malaysia, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Implementation of a Research Project on the use of Nitrogen based Chemical Fertilizer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11011",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "Taking into consideration the environmental pollution caused due to the mismanagement of chemical fertilizer (Nitrogen in particular) in the South Asian region, it has been planned to implement a multitask research proposal based on South Asian region on the use of nitrogen based fertilizers in different farming systems led by the United Nation Environmental Programme (UNEP) in association with the International Nitrogen Management Systems (INMS). Under this project, it has been scheduled to carry out the activities such as collecting data on nitrogen losses and greenhouse gas emission from selected farming systems (vegetables-Nuwara-eliya and Kalpitiya), (Rice - Anuradhapura) making the farmers aware on such  things, identifying atmospheric pollution on lower plant diversity of montane forests and educating farming communities and stakeholders for creating best nitrogen management systems to minimize Nitrogen losses, within a period of 05 years. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to enter into a Collaboration Agreement among the University of Peradeniya, Sri Lanka and United Kingdom Research and Innovation (UKRI), Global Challenge Research Fund  (GCRF) and South Asian Nitrogen Hub (SANH), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "Implementation of Flood Mitigation Projects in the year 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11010",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "The Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation (SLLDC) has identified flood mitigation projects to be implemented in the year 2021 in order to minimize floods that occurred in Colombo, suburb areas and out of Colombo and to ensure the environmentally sustainable urbanization. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to implement the said projects through the provisions of Rs.2800 million allocated to the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation for the year 2021, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-29-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-03-29",
    "description": "'e-Grama Niladari' Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11009",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-29",
    "decision_details_body": "The e-Grama Niladari (eGN) Project is implemented to formulate a database to store and search information required to day today duties pertaining to the services rendered by the Grama Niladaris to the general public. As per the outcome of a pilot project implemented in 162 Grama Niladari Divisions in 04 Divisional Secretariat Divisions during 2016 and 2017, the approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to implement the same in 7000 Grama Niladari Divisions as the Phase II of the said project. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to implement the said project by the State Ministry of Home Affairs with the consultancy support of the Information and Communication Technology Agency of  Sri Lanka (ICTA), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Cremation Ceremony of the late , Most Venerable Kotugoda Dammawansa Thero, Maha Nayake Thero of the Sri Lanka Amarapura Maha Nikaya\u201d",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11008",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approved the proposal made by H.E the president to declare a Day of National Mourning on 2021\u201103\u201125 the date of conducting the cremation ceremony of late Dharmapala Wansalankara Saddharma Keerthi Sri, Thripitaka Visharadha Pravachana Keerthi Sri, Sasana Shobhana, Sri Sumangala Vidyawathansa, Aggamaha Panditha Most Venerable Mahopadyaya Kotugoda Dammawasa Thero, Maha Nayake Thero of the Sri Lanka Amarapura Maha Nikaya, and close the slaughterhouses and meat and fish shops in the Colombo district where the cremation ceremony is conducted treating the day as a day of mourning and to close liquor shops as well, considering the great service rendered to the nation and the religion by late Thero."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Establishment of the \u201cAnuradhapura Pharmaceutical Manufacturing Zone\u201d",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11007",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish the \u201cAnuradapura Pharmaceutical Manufacturing zone\u201d in Oyamadu where the \u2018Deyata Kirula\u2019 was held under the local businessmen and investors encouraging programme with a view to providing high quality pharmaceuticals at a low price for the people by manufacturing all pharmaceuticals in Sri Lanka which could manufacture according to the International Standards. A Committee of Experts has selected 24 investors having called for project proposals from qualified local investors who are interested in this regard. The investors are expected to invest approximately Rs.28,200 million for the project. Accordingly, the land plots will be leased to selected local investors for a period of 35 years with a tax exemption for the first five years. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to implement the proposed pharmaceutical manufacturing zone, as a strategic project under the State Ministry of Production, Supply and Regulation of Pharmaceuticals, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Colombo Port City Economic Commission Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11006",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201101\u201104 to establish a special economic zone called Colombo Port City. Accordingly, in order to make legal provisions for the purpose, the Legal Draftsman has prepared the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Bill. Therefore, the proposal made by H.E the President to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "International Promotion Campagin to attract Foreign Direct Investment to Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11005",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although foreign direct investments are crucial driving forces of the economic development, the process of attracting foreign direct investments have become weaken with the absence of a focused strategy that could target direct potential investors during the last few years. Although Sri Lanka and other several competitive countries have taken measures to attract foreign direct investments, Sri Lanka could gain only US $ 1.5 billion of foreign direct investment during the year 2019. Therefore, it has been found the necessity to implement a well-orchestrated, coherent and focused marketing and coordination strategy in order to showcase the attractiveness of Sri Lanka as the most suitable investment destination. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to take necessary action to obtain the service of a high level global consultancy firm which contributes for foreign direct investment for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Proposed Special Goods and Services Tax Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11004",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Budget proposals for the year 2021 pointed out the necessity of expediting the process of tax collection by introducing a Special Goods and Services Tax Act. Under the provisions to be imposed by the proposed new Act, it has been planned to make more simpler the charging of Goods and Services Tax relating to the fields of alcohol, cigarettes, vehicles, telecommunication and betting. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft the Special Goods and Services Tax Bill, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Purchasing seven (07) million Sputnik - V Vaccines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11003",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Health has planned to vaccinate 14 million of the total population of the Sri Lanka to protect from the Covid-19 virus and as its inception, the Ministry is taking measures to vaccinate 05 million of the population. The National Drug Regulatory Authority has granted permission for the emergency use of Sputnik V vaccine in Sri Lanka. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to purchase 07 million of Sputnik V vaccines to a sum of US $ 69.65 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Presentation of Regulations made under section 34(1) of the Convention Against Doping in Sports Act No.33 of 2013, in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11002",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Youth and Sports to present the regulations made under section 34(1) of the Convention Against Doping in Sports Act No.33 of 2013 and published in the Gazette (Extraordinary) Notification No 2216/4 dated 2021\u201102\u201123, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Amendment to the Major Statutes relating to Local Authorities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11001",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Legal Draftsman has formulated the relevant legislation to update the Municipal Councils Ordinance,  Urban Councils Ordinance and the Pradeshiya Sabhas Act, the major Statutes relating to the Local Authorities,which have been enacted decades ago. The Attorney General has pointed out several further amendments to be made to these Bills. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Services, Provincial Councils & Local Government to take necessary action to further amend the said Bills already formulated incorporating the said amendments and to seek the views of the Provincial Councils in terms of the provisions of Article 154G of the 13th Amendment to the Constitution, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Presenting the Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 for the approval of Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11000",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to present the Gazette Notification No.2214/56 dated 2021\u201102\u201111 issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969, incorporating the provisions enabling to permit the importation of ceramic products which had been suspended temporarily, on 180 day Credit basis and to permit the importation of sarees other than Batik, Handloom and Apparels on 90 day Credit basis, in Parliament for approval in terms of Section 20 of the said Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "The proposed Assets Utilization Reform Commission Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10999",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- In line with the Budget Speech of 2021, expeditious measures have to be taken for ensuring the maximum and effective use of under utilized assets including lands in the national interest and advancement of the national economy. Especially, it has been a priority requirement to introduce an appropriate procedure for the use of under utilized state lands given on long term lease basis, condominium property of which the construction activities have been delayed due to many reasons and under utilized lands including State Enterprises with assets in maximum productive manner. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President to establish an institute as the Assets Utilization Reform Commission and provide for the required legal provisions to the said Commission to take necessary action for effective utilization of the under utilized assets so identified and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to formulate the Assets Utilization Reform Commission Bill incorporating the provisions required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Declaring the National Sports Day",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10998",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- It was decided by the Cabinet at the meeting held on 2014\u201107\u201110 to declare 06th April of every year as the National Sports Day of Sri Lanka. However, it is difficult to attract the attention of people towards this day due to the festive season and preparation for the New year celebrations in the country. Since athletes and the entire public should be made aware of and interested in sports by declaring a Sports Day, varied sports related groups have pointed out the necessity of declaring another suitable day as the National Sports Day. Taking into consideration this matter, the proposal made by the Minister of Youth and Sports to declare 31st July, the day Mr. Duncan White won the Silver medal in 400m Hurdles at an Olympics adding a dignity to Sri Lanka, as the National Sports Day, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Establishment of the Youth Enterprise Development Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10997",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- A major challenge faced by the community of youth entering the field of business as new entrepreneurs is the dearth of sufficient financial resources for investing in their businesses. And, the young entrepreneurs already involved in the field of business also confront various issues in securing the required financial resources. It has been made clear that the youth entrepreneurs face several difficulties consequent to their attempts to secure the required financial resources through various informal methods. It has been proposed through the national policy framework of the Government, 'Vistas of Prosperity & Splendour', to initiate a Youth Development Fund and a Youth Development Lottery for promoting the said Fund. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Youth and Sports to establish the said Fund through a Parliamentary Act and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Obtaining Assistance from Radio Broadcasting Services for continuous implementation of the Learning - Teaching Process in the Education System during the period of COVID-19 pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10996",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'Gurugedara' Educational programmes are telecast through 'Channel Eye' and 'Nethra TV' covering the subjects from Grade 3 to Grade 13 for continuation of education activities of school students without interruption in face of the COVID-19 pandemic situation. Accordingly, it has been made clear that it would be appropriate to use radio channels to broadcast the educational programs which are being telecast through television, to the areas those are not covered. As it is able to listen to the educational programs through smart phones in addition to the radios while such educational programs are aired through radio, a large number of students are able to listen to those programs. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to broadcast such educational programs through national radio channels and regional radio channels of Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-23-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-03-23",
    "description": "Implementation of a research project for Improved Productivity, Efficiency and Sustainability of the Culture-based Fishery for Fin-fish and Giant Freshwater Prawn in Sri Lankan Reservoirs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10995",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Rearing of giant freshwater prawns in Sri Lanka has been identified as a field that can be improved as a high potential business and provide benefits to the rural fisheries community. As releasing those freshwater prawn fry to the freshwater reservoirs is not carried out in a scientific manner, it has been identified appropriate to conduct a scientific research in this regard. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to implement the said research project between the Wayamba University of Sri Lanka, University of Ruhuna, University of Jaffna, National Aquaculture Development Authority, National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency (NARA) with the James Cook University of Australia and to enter into a Research Agreement among the said institutes for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Provision of adequate stocks of Rice to the market",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10994",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Attention of the Cabinet was focused on the non availability of adequate stocks of Rice at controlled prices in the market and the Cabinet discussed possible alternatives that can be taken in this regard. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to convert the stocks of paddy purchased from farmers by the Paddy Marketing Board into rice initially and distribute them continuously through the network of sales outlets of Sathosa and to consider alternative measures to be taken further considering the progress of the said arrangement."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Procurement of Construction Machines and Equipment and other Logistics and Transport Vehicles and supply of the same to the State Owned Entities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10993",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has planned to implement many development projects in the fields of Highways, Irrigation, Buildings and other sectors. However, when considering the capacity of the construction industry and the local construction contractors, it has been observed that implementation of such development projects as expected can be difficult. Under this circumstance, a number of important projects identified are expected to be handed over to the government institutions engaged in construction works for implementation. Accordingly, it has been planned to increase the capacity of the Government owned institutions engaged in the construction related work by procuring and supplying earth moving and construction machinery and equipment, road and building construction machinery and equipment, other equipment related to such activities, pre-fabricated buildings and goods transportation and service supply vehicles and maintenance vehicles required to implement these projects. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways to purchase the said machineries by following the relevant procurement procedure under the Supplier\u2019s Credit Facility scheme awarded by such equipment manufactures in collaboration with local counterparts, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Implementation of New Tax Proposals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10992",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bills have been drafted by the legal draftsman to amend the Inland Revenue Act, No.24 of 2017 and the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002 in order to implement tax reforms made by the \u201cEconomic Revival Initiative\u201d presented to introduce a simple, transparent and an effective tax system as pledged by H.E the President to the people along with the tax reforms and policy decisions relating to the budget proposals for the year 2021. Clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the said bills and therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to publish the said bills in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Enacting an Act for the Preservation of Thripitaka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10991",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has been recognized as the centre of Buddhism and it is a responsibility of the Government to protect and foster Buddhasasana while giving the foremost place for Buddhism. In 1956, the Thripitaka has been printed with sinhala translations to commemorate the Sambudhha Jayanthi of the 2500th year of Buddhist Era. By the Gazette Notification dated 2019\u201102\u201107, Thripitaka has been declared as a National Heritage whereas by the same Gazette Notification it has been prevented the opportunities of revising, making wrong interpretations and translating Thripitaka without the permission of the Government. The proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs, to pass an Act for the Preservation of Thripitaka for protecting the same for future generation and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Obtaining a Cargo Freighter for SriLankan Airlines Limited (SLA) on lease basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10990",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The fleet of SriLankan Airlines Limited contained a grater share of economical narrow-body aircraft. In consequence of that, more attention has been drawn on predominantly passenger route network in the recent years which resulted in under utilization of cargo potential due to the non-availability of suitable aircraft to cater to the cargo operations. With the COVID \u2013 19 outbreak, most of the Aviation Companies have paid attention on cargo transportation due to the limitation of passenger transportation. SriLankan Airlines maintains its cargo operations for 26 destinations and it has been found that this is a great opportunity to access to cargo market share on key routes, taking into consideration the present market changes. Accordingly, taking into account the potentiality of cargo operations, it has been planned to strategically change the current business model of SriLankan Airlines Limited. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to obtain a Cargo Freighter for SriLankan Airlines Limited on lease basis, following the International Competitive Procurement Procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Programme to establish a Homeshop in one household in every Grama Niladhari Division, targeting young women entrepreneurs selected from Samurdhi families",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10989",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Highways has planned to implement a programme by the name of Homeshop in every Grama Niladhari division in association with the relevant line ministries and other institutions targeting 25,000 young women entrepreneurs selected from Samurdhi families to strengthen the food distribution network. National level guidance for this project will be provided by the Task Force on Economic Revival and Poverty Elevation while monitoring of the project will be carried out by the State Ministry of Samurdhi, Household Economy, Micro Finance, Self Employment and Business Development. This programme is planned to be implemented through the 100,000 km development pogramme under the Ministry of Highways covering the entire island. The proposed Homeshops will be constructed adjoining the roads those are proposed to be constructed under 100,000 kilo meter of roads development project and are to be constructed with a floor area of 200, 300, 400 and 500 square feets depending on the requirement. Accordingly, the proposal submitted by the Minister of Highways for implementation of the said programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Acquisition of \"Anderson Golf Links Ground\" where Shalika Stadium and Sports Complex is located, by the Sri Lanka Transport Board through a Free Grant",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10988",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The land called \"Anderson Golf Links Ground\" in extent of 3.4125 hectares, where the Shalika Stadium and Sports Complex is located, has been in the custody of the Sri Lanka Transport Board since 1966. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence to the joint proposal made by the Minister of Transport and the Minister of Lands to transfer the said land to the Sri Lanka Transport Board through a Free Grant in accordance with the provisions of the State Land Ordinance, subject to non awarding the right of selling the land to another party and charging its unimproved value to the Government."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Obtaining assistance of Television Services for continuous implementation of the Learning - Teaching process in the Education System during the period of Covid 19- pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10987",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Guru Gedara' programme, prepared by the National Institute of Education was telecast combining the 'Channel Eye' and 'Nethra TV' of Sri Lanka Rupawahini Corporation to continue the academic activities of the students, sitting for Grade 5 Scholarship Examination, G.C.E (O/L) Examination and G.C.E (A/L) Examination, during the period when schools were closed due to the Covid-19 pandemic from March, 2020. In order to prevent the disruption of students' education due to the delay caused in the commencement of the third school term in 2020, telecasting Sinhala and Tamil medium educational programmes from Grade 3 to Grade 13 under the phase 2 of 'Guru Gedara' programme has been started on 16 November, 2020. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to continue the 'Guru Gedara' educational programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-15-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-03-15",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation in the field of Higher Education between the Ministry of Education of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Higher Education Commission of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10986",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Ministry of Education of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Higher Education Commission of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan in order to implement an Educational and Scientific Knowledge Exchange Scholarship Programme in the field of higher education for a period of five years, enabling to strengthen mutual corporation in the field of education and to enhance the educational opportunities between two countries. The Government of Pakistan has agreed to grant 1000 Scholarships as 800 Full Scholarships and 200 Tuition Fee Waiver Partial Scholarships for undergraduate degrees under this MoU within the relevant period. Further, it is expected to exchange 50 Sri Lankan/Pakistan University Faculty members between two countries for research, seminars and other academic activities for a specific period of time. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign the said MoU, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Amendments to the Industrial Promotion Act No.46 of 1990",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10985",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that the provisions of the existing Industry Promotion Act, No.46 of 1990 is inadequate to make industrial policies which assist to fulfil timely requirements of the industrial sector relating to technology, trade, skills and environmental concerns. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to appoint a Steering Committee chaired by the Secretary to the Ministry of Industries and comprising of representatives of relevant government institutions, private sector industry organizations / chamber of industries with a view to preparing a draft Bill to amend the Industry Promotion Act, No.46 of 1990 to suit with the present, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Amending legislations to require security deposit when filling appeals, revisions and writ applications against grants and decisions granted under the Termination of Employment of Workmen (Special Provisions) Act No. 45 of 1971 and Industrial Disputes Act No. 43 of 1950",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10984",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Termination of Employment of Workmen (Special Provisions) Act No. 45 of 1971 has been introduced with a view to preventing the termination of employment of employees and it has ensured the job security of workmen by constituting legal action against employers who act deviating from the provisions of the said Act. Similarly, the Industrial Disputes Act, No.43 of 1950 has been introduced with a view to solving industrial disputes between employers and employees expeditiously in a reasonable manner. Further, in the circumstances where orders are made in favour of employers under the above two Acts, it has been observed that there is a tendency of constituting legal action by employers to prevent the enforcement of such orders. In this context, it has been observed that there are instances where nearly 15-20 years have lapsed for the implementation of relevant orders and that the employees could not receive the expected relief due to the death of employers, migration, avoidance of courts and liquidation of companies during the aforesaid period, Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour to amend the Termination of Employment of Workmen (Special Provisions) Act No. 45 of 1971and the Industrial Disputes Act, No.43 of 1950, enabling to initiate the litigation process only after furnishing security deposit when employers institute legal actions against an Order of the Commissioner General of Labour under\u00a0 the Termination of Employment of Workmen (Special Provisions) Act, No.45 of 1971 or a decision of the Magistrate\u2019s Court to enforce such Order or against Industrial Arbitration award or an Industrial Court award under the provisions of the Industrial Disputes Act No.43 of 1950, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Setting up a Pharma Zone in Millewa, Horana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10983",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- In line with the policies of the new government, strategic measures are being used by the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation to manufacture most pharmaceuticals locally. Accordingly, the establishment of pharma zones in Arabokka in the Hambantota District and Oyamaduwa in the Anuradhapura District has now been initiated. In addition, another Pharma Zone is scheduled to be established in Millewa, Horana. Orthopedic and Neuro-Surgical Implants, Oncology drugs, Oral Solid Dosage products and Cardiac Stents and Intra Ocular Lenses are expected to be manufactured in this Pharma Zone. The project is scheduled to be implemented under two phases and the first phase of the project is expected to commence in March 2021 with an estimated investment of Rs. 8 billion. A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) has already been entered into between the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation and the Urban Development Authority to allocate a block of land in extent of 64 acres and 83.3 perches in Millewa area belonging to the Urban Development Authority to establish the proposed Pharma Zone. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Housing and Urban Development and the Minister of Health to appoint a Steering Committee chaired by the Secretary to the Ministry of Finance, comprising of the representatives of other relevant Ministries and Institutions enabling to implement the proposed project expeditiously and to appoint a Project Management Committee headed by the Chairman of the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation to provide the necessary technical matters to the said Steering Committee and to appoint Selendiva Investment Company, a fully state-owned company, as the Project Manager to provide pre- and post-contract and financial consultancy services, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Modernization of Sri Lanka Police",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10982",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka Police is a leading entity empowered to ensure the safety and security of the public and to maintain law and order. It also provides multiple services to people across the country. It has been found the necessity to modernize the Sri Lanka Police by changing the traditional systems followed at present. In this context, it has been identified that the traffic handling process should be made effective and efficient through modern methods. In particular, priority should be given to streamlining the work of the Police Traffic and Road Safety Division using digitization solutions to reduce existing traffic congestion in urban areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Security to appoint a steering committee to design a project to monitor the overall modernization process of the Sri Lanka Police and implement the same, giving priority to the aforesaid purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Establishment of a new company to direct local products to foreign \tmarkets",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10981",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a concept of the State Ministry of Batik, Handloom Fabric and Local Apparel Productions, it has been found the necessity of setting up a leading institution to promote Sri Lankan products by establishing overseas showrooms thereby creating a strong international trade network through the selected representatives from those countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to establish a new company with 100% shares of Lanka Salusala Limited for the purpose and to implement a programme to promote local products including Batik products, Handloom Fabric products, and local apparel products through the foreign agents appointed by the said company and showrooms, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Carrying out surveys to mark the reserve boundaries of tanks/ anicuts under the 'Wari Saubhagya' Program",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10980",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been scheduled to rehabilitate approximately 5000 tanks/ anicuts under the 'Wari Saubhagya' Program during the period of next 04 years. The Survey Department has informed that the adequate human resources are not available in the Department at present to complete the surveys of such a large number of tanks within period of 03 years. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and the Minister of Lands to recruit 70 students who have graduated from Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka or Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and are awaiting for survey training, to the Department of Survey for a period of three years on temporary basis and attach them to the Department of Irrigation with a view to conducting surveys under the supervision of two senior surveyors of the Survey Department, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Allocation of a block of land for the construction of Rakwana Veterinary Office",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10979",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hapugasthenna Plantation Ltd has granted its concurrence to allocate a block of land without compensation to construct a new building to the Rakwana Veterinary Office functioning under the Department of Animal Production and Health of Sabaragamuwa Province, since the building in which the said office maintains is in very dilapilated condition. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Services, Provincial Councils and Local Government to allocate a block of land in extent of 0.15 hectares from Haderly part of Haderly Estate belonging to the Hapugasthenna Plantation Ltd without paying compensation for the construction of Rakwana Veterinary Office, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Continuation of Inter-Provincial Passenger bus operations in the face of the COVID-19 pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10978",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted by the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2020\u201111\u201109 to release the permit renewal fees, late fees, tender fees, log fees, entrance fees and Expressway Temporary Permit fees which are charged from bus operators until the end of year 2020, in order to continue the Inter-Provincial Passenger bus operations in the face of the COVID-19 pandemic situation. As it seems that it may take more time for bus operations to return to normal condition, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to provide the following reliefs out of those mentioned above, further up to 2021\u201103\u201131, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n* Charging a 10% of the annual tender fee or a sum of Rs.15,000/-, whichever is higher out of them.\n\n* Charging a 10% of the Expressway Temporary Permit Fee.\n\n* Exemption from log and entrance fees."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Implementation of Phase II of the Project for Improving Management of the Marine resources in Sri Lanka with the Technical Assistance from the Government of Norway",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10977",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Phase I of the Project for 'Improving Management of the Marine resources in Sri Lanka' has been implemented under the Bilateral Corporation between the Governments of Sri Lanka and Norway, within the period from 2017 to 2020. It has been proposed to implement the Phase II of the said project also under the Norwegian Grant Assistance. Under the proposed project, it has been planned to pursue action in collaboration with the Institute of Marine Research (IMR) of Norway and the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency (NARA) of Sri Lanka for the purpose of improving management of the marine fishery resources in Sri Lanka. Improvement of collection, storage and use of fisheries data and enhancing the capacity of fisheries research for sustainable management of marine fishery resources are to take place under the said Phase of the project. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency (NARA) of Sri Lanka and the Institute of Marine Research (IMR) of Norway for the implementation of the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Establishment of the 'National Management and Regulatory Committee on Early Childhood Education'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10976",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the existing legal framework, the Early Childhood Education System of Sri Lanka is steered under the coordination of several institutional layers belonging to the Central Government and Provincial Councils and the need for empowering the process of maintaining and monitoring the standards of the field at national level, has been recognized. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to appoint a Committee titled as the 'National Management and Regulatory Committee on Early Childhood Education' comprising the field experts and decision-making officials, to regulate, monitor and provide guidance for Pre-schools, Early Childhood Development Centres and Day Care Centres at national level, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Institutionalisation of the National Innovation Agency (NIA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10975",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- In view of coordinating the Ministries, Institutions and the Private sector for creating, improving and sustaining a national innovation eco-system and providing support required for the relevant innovations from idea to market, the National Innovation Agency (NIA) has been established by the Parliamentary Act, No.22 of 2019. Institutionalisation of the NIA has been recognized as a priority task of the State Ministry of Skills Development, Vocational Education, Research and Innovation, which falls under the purview of the Ministry of Education. Approval has been granted by the Cabinet in 2017 to formulate a Bill for establishing the Coordinating Secretariat for Science, Technology and Innovation (COSTI), which has been set up for the Science, Technology and Innovation related tasks and functions under the said State Ministry, as the National Science Technology and Innovation Coordinating Authority (NASTICA). The aims and functions of the proposed NASTICA are also more similar to the functions of the NIA. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to suspend the establishment of the said Authority and to institutionalise the NIA by using funds and other resources allocated for the COSTI, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Establishing the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious & Cultural Affairs and the institutions falling under its purview, in one dedicated building",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10974",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious & Cultural Affairs and the Departments and Institutions under its purview are being maintained at different locations, need has arisen to establish the Ministry and the said institutions in one dedicated building. The 09 storeyed building being constructed for the Department of Muslim Religious and Cultural Affairs at D. R. Wijewardena Mawatha, Colombo 10 has been identified suitable for this purpose. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious & Cultural Affairs to transfer the said building and the land on which it is located, to the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious & Cultural Affairs and to complete its construction activities thereafter and, establish the Ministry and all institutions under its purview in the said building, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Document of Understanding between the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and COMSATS University, Pakistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10973",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Interdisciplinary Research Center in Biomedical Materials (IRCBM) of COMSATS University, Pakistan is an institute that sustains a number of international Patent Licenses pertaining to the field of Biomaterials Tissue Engineering. It has been proposed to sign a Document of Understanding to exchange knowledge on the fields such as Biomaterials, Tissue Engineering, Regenerative Medicine, Sensors and Biosensors and to conduct cooperative researches on the sectors that are mutually important to both countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to sign the proposed Document of Understanding between the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and the COMSATS University, Pakistan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-08-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-03-08",
    "description": "Accreditation of the National Defence College under the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10972",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted by the Cabinet at its meeting held on 18\u201112\u20112019 to draft the 'Sri Lanka National Defence College Act' for the purpose of incorporating the 'National Defence College' through a Parliamentary Act. The academic activities of the College are to commence in May, 2021 and the above Act will provide the legal provisions required for awarding the ndc qualification to the students who complete a full-time course of 11 months successfully. Many countries around the world, through their National Defence Colleges, offer MSc or MPhil degrees in affiliation with the National Universities. As such, taking into consideration this matter, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to accredit the National Defence College under the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University, to enable the University to offer Postgraduate degrees to the students who are taking the course at the National Defence College, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Report on the progress of the Development Projects implemented under the Line Ministries by the end of the financial year 2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10970",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Cabinet decision dated 2018\u201104\u201125, the Ministry of Finance should submit a report on the physical progress of the projects implemented by the Line Ministries through the Capital budget, to the Cabinet on quarterly basis. As such, the progress report pertaining to the large scale projects implemented in the year 2020 was submitted by the Minister of Finance to the Cabinet. The following information was brought to the notice of the Cabinet through the said report:\n\n* \t289 development projects of which the estimated cost exceeds Rs. 01 billion in the year 2020, have been implemented under the purview of 40 Line Ministries.\n\n*\tAn allocation of around Rs.710 billion has been made for the said projects and its financial progress amounts to 72%.\n\n*\tA further allocation of Rs.2.9 trillion has to be made approximately for future activities of the said 289 development projects.\n\n*\tThere have been various issues and impediments during the implementation of these projects and although around Rs.08 billion has been spent for the additional staff dedicated for the project, it has been observed in this report that the expected results could not be achieved within the approved cost and duration pertaining to certain projects.\n\n*\tCertain weaknesses have been observed since the per-preparatory stage of certain projects and the delay caused in obtaining the required approvals from Public Institutions has sometimes become a problem in the implementation of the projects.\n\nTaking into consideration also the information furnished in the said report by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Cabinet decided to appoint a Committee comprising the Senior Secretaries and headed by the State Minister of Money & Capital Market and State Enterprise Reforms, to resolve the issues regarding the large scale Capital budget projects and to conduct monthly reviews on obtaining the optimum and timely assistance from the relevant parties."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Recruitment to Grade III of the Sri Lanka Principals Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10969",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, there are 4,600 vacancies in Grades I, II and III of the Sri Lanka Principals Service and it has been observed that, due to the COVID-19 pandemic situation prevailing in the country, it will take more than one year to conduct a competitive examination and structured interviews for the purpose of granting formal appointments. Taking into consideration these matters, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to take necessary action to conduct a structured interview in place of a competitive examination to select the qualified persons and appoint them to Grade III of the Sri Lanka Principals Service, limiting it only to this occasion, providing the opportunity to the qualified officers belonging to the Teachers Service who have been acting and covering the duties in the post of Principal for a long period and also to the other officers belonging to the Teachers Service who fulfill qualifications in terms of the Service Minute, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Report of the Cabinet Sub-Committee on Legislation held on 2021-01-12",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10968",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The concept papers submitted for the purpose of drafting the following Bills, have been referred to the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Legislation on approval by the Cabinet, to examine and submit its recommendations. Taking into consideration the recommendations of the said Sub\u2011Committee, the proposals referred to in the Cabinet Memoranda submitted by the Minister of Education in his capacity as the Chairman of the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Legislation to draft the relevant Bills, were approved by the Cabinet.\n\n* \tEnactment of a new legislation in place of the Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Act \n\n*\tMuslim Marriage and Divorce (Amendment) Bill\n\n*\tAmendment to the Penal Code (Chapter 19) (Protection of Human Dignity and Social Harmony, Fake News and Hate Speech)\n\n*\tAmendment to the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No.15 0f 1979 (Protection of Human Dignity and Social Harmony, Fake News and Hate Speech)"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Repealing sections 285, 286 and 286A of the Penal Code",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10967",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted at the Cabinet Meeting held on 2020\u201109\u201129 to draft a Bill on Prohibition of Obscene Publications. Upon passing the said Bill, the Obscene Publications Ordinance of 1927 will be repealed and at the same time, sections 285, 286 and 286A of the Penal Code will be redundant. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to draft a Bill for repealing the said sections of the Penal Code, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Repealing the Youth Corps Act and establishment of the Youth Corps as an Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10966",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted at the Cabinet Meeting held on 2011\u201112\u201115 to repeal the Youth Corps Act, No.21 of 2002 and draft a Bill for the establishment of the Youth Corps Authority. Although the Legal Draftsman has accordingly drafted a Bill, no further action has been taken in this regard. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Youth & Sports to instruct the Legal Draftsman to finalise drafting the said Bill incorporating the further amendments to be made to enable to repeal the Youth Corps Act, No.21 of 2002 and to establish the Youth Corps Authority, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Repealing the Botanic Gardens Ordinance, No.31 of 1928 and introduction of a new Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10965",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Botanic Gardens Ordinance, No.31 of 1928 as amended by the Act, No.32 of 1973 applies largely to the functions of the Department of National Botanic Gardens. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to amend the provisions of the said Ordinance which is around 90 years old, to suit the present needs, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Awarding of six (06) Civil Works Contract Packages for rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance of the Kekirawa - Thalawa - Ganewalpola - Dachchihalmillewa Road",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10964",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Competitive bids have been invited for six (06) Civil Works Contract Packages for rehabilitation, improvement and maintenance of the Kekirawa - Thalawa - Ganewalpola - Dachchihalmillewa Road in the North Central Province, under the Asian Development Bank funded Integrated Road Investment Programme. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways to award the relevant contracts as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Amendment to the authority limits of the Procurement Committees",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10963",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted to provide provisions for the implementation of a large number of projects which provide immediate benefits to the public, within the 2021-2023 Medium Term Budgetary Framework. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to increase the authority limits of the existing contract awarding in respect of the subject matters pertaining to the Ministry of Highways, Ministry of Water Supply, Ministry of Irrigation, Ministry of Power, Ministry of Ports & Shipping and the Ministry of Urban Development & Housing, to enable the implementation of the said projects expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Three Year Plan for the improvement of the infrastructure facilities in the Judicial Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10962",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The undue delay in the mechanism of the administration of justice in Sri Lanka has become a challenge in ensuring the rule of law within the country. This situation depicts in many of the international indicators and it directly affects for the foreign investments as well. Therefore, it is vitally important to supply adequate human and physical resources to the judicial sector, apply of novel technology, strengthen the dispute resolution mechanism alternative to litigation process as well as introducing necessary law reforms in order to resolve this issue. Therefore, it has been proposed to allocate Rs. 20,000 million from the budget for the year 2021 for the implementation of a three \u2013 year plan for enhancing infrastructure facilities within the judicial sector. Accordingly, the proposal submitted by the Minister of Justice for the implementation of a project to develop infrastructure facilities in the judicial sector under 06 selected subject areas utilizing the given provisions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Revising the Swashakthi Loan Scheme to provide loan facilities for the development of Small and Medium Scale Business Sector and generating employments",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10961",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2020\u201110\u201126 to implement the Swashakthi Loan Scheme which is functioning under the Ministry of Youth and Sports, with necessary amendments to provide loan facilities for the development of Small and Medium Scale Business Sector and generating employments. Out of the loans granted under this loan scheme, 58% has been granted for the existing enterprises whereas 42% of the loans has been provided to new enterprises. Accordingly, the Cabinet granted its concurrence to the proposal submitted by the Minister of Youth and Sports for providing opportunity to obtain loan facilities under the Swashakthi loan scheme also for the existing enterprises of small and medium scale entrepreneurs who are looking forward to scaling up their business through new product development or market development and to provide loan facilities not exceeding Rs.2 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Establishment of the Proposed Mangrove Botanic Gardens in Akmeemana, Galle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10960",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of National Botanical Gardens has planed to establish a new Mangrove Botanic Garden in a land in extent of 26.71 hectares in close - proximity to the Pinnaduwa Expressway entrance in Nugaduwa Grama Niladhari division of the Akmeemana divisional secretariat division. Since no institution has so far been in operation including the National Botanical Gardens for ex \u2013 situ conservation of mangrove in Sri Lanka, this Mangrove Botanic Garden will fulfil that requirement. Furthermore, establishment of this proposed Mangrove Botanic Garden will pave the way for the upliftment of the tourism industry and will assist the national and international researches on mangrove species. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism for the establishment of the proposed Mangrove Botanic Garden, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Establishment of a Committee for development of the rubber cultivation and related industries in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10959",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The global demand for sanitary devices including the gloves that are manufactured using rubber has been tremendously increased due to the prevailing global pandemic situation of COVID \u2013 19 and therefore, there is a national requirement to produce raw rubber locally to meet the requirement of local rubber products. For the purpose, the need to appoint a coordinating committee which will function consolidating planters and industrialists encouraging the local rubber industry together with the public and private sector institutions directly linked with the manufacturing raw rubber as well as rubber manufacturing industries has been identified. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to appoint a Committee by the name of \u201cInter-institutional Coordinating Committee for Development of Rubber Cultivation and Industries\u201d under the chairmanship of the Secretary, Ministry of Plantation and comprising of the representatives of other relevant Ministries and Institutions to continue and maintain the value chain of rubber industry in Sri Lanka with a sound performance, to discuss and settle the available issues in the sector, and to submit policy recommendations to the Government."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Rename the 'Certification Body for Qualification and Certification of Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) personnel' as 'National Certification Body for Qualification and Certification of Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) personnel'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10958",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Certification Body for Qualification and Certification of Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) personnel functions as an independent entity under Sri Lanka Atomic Energy Board for the certification of non \u2013 destructive testing certification and personnel while promoting non \u2013 destructive testing training and testing services. Each country should establish a National Certification Body for Qualification and Certification of Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) personnel' to achieve international recognition for NDT training and certification. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power to rename the already established 'Certification Body for Qualification and Certification of Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) personnel' as 'National Certification Body for Qualification and Certification of Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) personnel', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Construction of Wattegedara Wewa in Matale District, identified under 'Gama Samaga Pilisandara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10957",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- It was decided at the programme \u2018Gama Samanga Pilisandara\u2019 held at Himbiliyakada in the Divisional Secretariat division of Wilgamuwa in Matale district to open the way for a higher income generation for poor people whose livelihood is Agriculture by taking necessary measures for the supply of water for approximately 1,010 acres of new cultivable lands while making remedies for the prevailing water shortage for land in extent 1,300 acres nourished by Himbiliyakada Wewa. Accordingly, the Department of Irrigation has designed a project to supply water by constructing Wattegedara Wewa and Dodamgolla Wewa across Gemburu Oya and supplying water to both Wattegedara Wewa and Himbiliyakada Wewa through a 1,800 metre long tunnel from the right bank main channel of Kalu Ganga reservoir. The estimated cost for the proposed project will be approximately Rs. 7,155 million while its construction has been planned to be completed within a period of 03 years from 2021 \u2013 2023. The proposals made by the Minister of Irrigation to initiate the construction activities of Watthegedara wewa during the year 2021 with the use of machinery of the Department of Irrigation and labour contribution from the Sri Lanka Army as well as the villagers, and to allocate the provisions required for the project from the medium term budgetary framework 2021-2023, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-03-01-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-03-01",
    "description": "Vesting of the land and buildings owned by the National Housing Development Authority located at Thammannagama, Anamaduwa with the Ceylon German Technical Training Institute",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10956",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-03-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Gam Uda' land in extent of 3.585 hectares and its all buildings located in Thammannagama, Anamaduwa has been vested with the National Housing Development Authority by a special grant. The Ceylon German Technical Training Institute (CGTTI) has made a request for that land and its buildings in order to establish its Aanamaduwa Regional Centre whereas the National Housing Development Authority has given its consent to vest in the same. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to transfer the said land and buildings back to the Government and to vest the same with the CGTTI on a free grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
