    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "COVID - 19 Vaccine Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10945",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Health has planned to vaccinate 14 million people of the total population of the country against the COVID-19 pandemic. Accordingly, the following proposals made by the Acting Minister of Health, were approved by the Cabinet. \n    \u2022 to sign the Standardized Indemnification Agreement forwarded by the COVAX mechanism, enabling to obtain the COVID - 19 Vaccine under the \tCOVAX facility expeditiously.\n    \u2022 to purchase 10 million doses of Oxford AstraZenceca Vaccine from the Serum Institute Life Sciences Private Limited as a direct procurement at a sum of US$ 52.5 million, by the Sri Lanka State Pharmaceuticals Corporation.\n    \u2022 to enter into an Agreement by the Sri Lanka State Pharmaceuticals Corporation to purchase 3.5 million doses of COVID - 19 Vaccines manufactured by the AstraZeneca Institute of Great Britain."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "National Action Plan to Monitor and Combat Human Trafficking",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10944",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Action Plan to Monitor and Combat Human Trafficking to be implemented  during the period from 2021-2025 has been prepared by reviewing the Action Plan operated from 2015-2019 and taking into consideration the experiences gained in the implementation of the said plan and the views expressed by the others parties. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to implement the National Action Plan to Monitor and Combat Human Trafficking 2021-2025, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "Disposal of confiscated sand and timber",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10943",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted its approval to provide sand and timber confiscated by the Courts located countrywide for construction and renovation purposes of the places of religious worship at concessionary prices and the said approval has lasted on 2020\u201112\u201131. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to revise the methodology adopted at present under the said Programme and implement further, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "Expansion of the Kalutara Industrial Estate",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10942",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Kalutara Industrial Estate has been set up in a land in extent of 50 acres called \u201cPullerton Estate\u201d and at present, 33 investors have set up factories and its commercial production activities are successfully being carried out. Those investors have invested at around Rs. 837 million and have provided about 775 job opportunities. Although both local and foreign investors have forwarded to set up industries in the western province, no land blocks remain in any of the 08 industrial estates set up in the western province. Taking these into consideration, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to release the Government owned land in extent of 1.946 hectares located adjacent to the Kalutara Industrial Estate  to expand the said industrial estate and to allocate such lands to the industrialists under the Regional Industrial Estate Development Programme, having fulfilled required infrastructure facilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "Handing over the office premises of the Ministry of Industries to the Urban Development Authority and shifting the Ministry to a new office premises",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10941",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The premises in which the Ministry of Industries is presently being established is in extent of 01 Acre and 7 perches and it is located in a place with high economic and commercial value. According to the estimate of the Government Valuer its current value  amounts to Rs. 2.32 billion. Therefore, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to  hand over the said office premises with the Urban Development Authority, enabling to utilize the land for a more productive task with an economic value and in return, to obtain a furnished building of 50,000 square feet with parking facilities for 75 vehicles to the Ministry of Industries from the said Authority."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "Proclamation of proposed Hambantota Elephant Management Reserve",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10940",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Ongoing rapid development projects in the Hambantota district have caused a severe impact on the Wildlife habitats including that of wild elephants and their foraging ways and it has resulted in increasing human-elephant conflict. As a remedy for the issue, the Department of Wildlife Conservation has taken initiatives to proclaim  an  Elephant Management Reserve for wild elephants and other creatures, having ensured the expansion of their foraging ways through researches. Accordingly, a land in extent of 23,746.55 hectares belonging to the Department of Forest Conservation and Mahaweli Authority of Sri Lanka has been identified for the proposed reserve. The Gazette Notification incorporating guidelines and regulations required for the purpose  has been drafted with the concurrence of the Department of Forest Conservation and Mahaweli Authority of Sri Lanka. Therefore, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Conservation to publish the said Gazette Notification in the Government Gazette after obtaining  the concurrence of the Legal Draftsman for the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "Fast Tracking Investment",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10939",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Recently few internationally recognized investors have shown their interest to invest in Sri Lanka. However, since the existing mechanism to facilitate such investors seems to be  lengthy, relevant investors themselves have to implement projects through the investment authorities of Sri Lanka. Under these circumstances, the Government has found the immediate necessity to initiate a more formal mechanism to encourage such investments. As such the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to appoint a Committee called \u201cCabinet Appointed Management Committee on Investment\u201d under the Chairmanship of the Secretary to the Treasury and with the participation of relevant secretaries to ministries and the Chairman, Board of Investment of Sri Lanka, and to entrust that Committee with the responsibility of taking necessary measures to grant approval for that investment proposals, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "Submission of Regulations for the approval of Parliament issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10938",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Gazette Extraordinary Notifications No 2206/5 dated 2020\u201112\u201114 and No 2207/15  dated 2020\u201112\u201124 have been issued incorporating the regulations published under  the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 for regulating the importation of local handloom and batik textile, regulating the importation of fishing boats, passenger vessels and boats and relaxing the limitations of importing selected goods which are not locally manufactured  to meet the need of domestic industries. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to submit such regulations for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-22-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-02-22",
    "description": "Recommendation of the Finance Commission for the Financial Year 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10937",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Finance Commission established in accordance with Article 154 R of the Constitution of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka shall make recommendations to H.E the President on the policies to be followed in the disbursement of funds granted by the annual budget for the Provincial Councils. Accordingly, the Finance Commission has submitted those recommendations to H.E the President for the year 2021. As such, the proposal submitted by H.E the President to implement such recommendations made by the said Commission and to present the same in Parliament in terms of Article 154 R (7) of the Constitution, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "Amending the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No.15 of 1979 (Empowering the Magistrate to visit Police Stations)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10936",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to amend the Code of Criminal Procedure Act. No.15 of 1979, empowering the Magistrate to visit police stations situated within the judicial division to which he is appointed, enabling him to supervise the suspect who is being held in police custody in such police station at least once in every month. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to publish the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman in the Government Gazette and to present same thereafter in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "Providing special concessions to Mattala Rajapaksha International Airport and Colombo, Rathmalana International Airport to attract airlines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10935",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020\u201112\u201121 granted approval to release the landing and parking charges of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport and the Colombo International Airport as an encouragement for the international charter flight operations implemented according to specific schedules prepared by the Ministry of Tourism and the Civil Aviation Authority of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the proposal made by the\u00a0 Minister of Tourism to extend the said concession up to 2021\u201107\u201119, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "Implementation of Traditional and Rural Industrial Promotion Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10934",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- An allocation of Rs. 2000 million has been made in the Budget 2021 to assist industrialists engaged in traditional industries to expand their production and to facilitate access to specific commodity markets. Accordingly, the State Ministry of Rattan, Brass, Pottery, Furniture and Rural Industrial Promotion has designed a program to be implemented during the period 2021-2025. The Ministry has identified the following projects under this program and the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to implement the said project, was approved by the Cabinet. \n    \u2022 Cultivation of Raw Material Programme for Rural Industries\n    \u2022 Establishment of Raw Material Bank\n    \u2022 One Entrepreneur per Village on Rural Industry\n    \u2022 Establishing a Timber Research and Development Organization\n    \u2022 Integrated Development on Rural and Traditional Industrial Village\n    \u2022 Local and Foreign Market Promotion Programme on Rural Industry"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "100kW Solar Power Generation Programme implementing under private sector investments by connecting to the distribution transformers under the renewable energy promotion",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10933",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to obtain maximum amount of energy from the electricity requirement of the country from the renewable energy sources by the year 2030, while adapting the government policy framework \u201cVistas of Prosperity and Splendour. Further, it is expected to implement the said renewable energy projects mostly under the private sector investments. Accordingly, it has been planned to implement a renewable energy generating project by connecting land based solar power plants to 7000 distribution transformers belonging to the Ceylon Electricity Board and Lanka Electricity Company (Pvt) Ltd. It is expected to implement single solar power project for identified one transformer under this project and to invite bids under competitive procurement process from persons and institutions registered under business names register of the Divisional Secretariat to select investors for this purpose. The investment for the construction of single solar power plant is approximately Rs 12 million and the relevant plant has to be built on a land in extent of 40 perches in close proximity to the transformer. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Power, the Cabinet granted approval to implement the proposed project within 18 months as a rapid project."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "Introduction of a Transit Card for the Public Transport Service of Sri Lanka and implementation of an Electronic Fare Collection System",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10932",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Public Transport Service of Sri Lanka relies on fares and with a view to avoiding the hardships resulting in, approval has been granted at the Cabinet Meeting held on 02nd October 2018, to appoint a Steering Committee comprising of representatives from all the relevant institutions, to implement a project for introducing a Transit Card for the use in Buses and Trains belonging to public transport. As such, a local Company, Lanka Clear (Pvt) Ltd. which is 100% affiliated to the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) with its approval, has submitted a proposal for the proposed Transit Card Project and based on such project proposal, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to take necessary action for the use of Transit Card in the island, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the University of Colombo and the Lahore School of Economics in Pakistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10931",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to exchanging research materials, publications and information mutually benefiting each party, encouraging the joint and individual research projects of the two institutions and providing opportunities to have experiences through the Programme of exchanging students with skills and abilities, it has been proposed to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the University of Colombo and the Lahore School of Economics in Pakistan. An Expert Committee has studied the proposed MoU and submitted its recommendations and, concurrence of the Foreign Ministry and the Attorney General's Department has been granted for the same. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign the said MoU, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "Development of Summit Flats Premises for the promotion of construction of Multi-storied Housing Units",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10930",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to meet the increasing demand on houses due to the dearth of lands available in the City of Colombo, the Government has paid its attention to identify suitable land blocks and construct multi-storied housing units. The Summit Flats, having established in the year 1976, comprising 176 housing units and 15 bungalows constructed in a land block of 12 acres in extent and located in Keppetipola Road, Colombo 05, under the governance of the Ministry of Public Services, Provincial Councils and Local Government, are being used for official residential requirements of the Public Officers. Most of these housing units are in dilapidated condition at present and the National Building Research Organization (NBRO) has recommended that the said housing units should be fully repaired. Further, around 700 Public Officers are in the waiting list in anticipation of official residences. Taking these matters into consideration, the Ministry of Urban Development & Housing and the Ministry of Public Services, Provincial Councils & Local Government have entered into an Agreement to implement a project for constructing 400 official residences for Public Officers, in a block of land of 02 acres of the said 12 acres in extent, as its first stage. 100 housing units from the Middle Income Housing Schemes currently underway by the Urban Development Authority within the purview of the said project, will also be transferred to the Ministry of Public Services, Provincial Councils & Local Government. Accordingly, the remaining land in extent of 10 acres will be transferred to the Urban Development Authority for development. As such, the Joint Proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development & Housing and the Minister of Public Services, Provincial Councils & Local Government to implement the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-15-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-02-15",
    "description": "Presenting the promulgated Regulations on 'Special Deposit Accounts' under the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017, to Parliament for its approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10929",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to encouraging the remittance of foreign currency into the country, approval has been granted to open 'Special Deposit Accounts' and approval of the Cabinet was also granted previously to pay an additional interest for further retaining the deposits in the said accounts. Accordingly, Regulations have been promulgated through the Extraordinary Gazette Notification No.2202/07 dated 2020-11-17 under the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017, to extend the validity period to open the said Special Deposit Accounts for a further period of six (06) months with effect from 08th October 2020. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to present the said Regulations for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Procurement of Chemical Fertilizer - 2021 Yala Season - (Early April Delivery)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10928",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- International competitive bids have been called to procure chemical fertilizer for Ceylon Fertilizer Company Ltd. (Lak Pohora) and Colombo Commercial Fertilizers Ltd. (Commercial Fertilizer) for early April delivery of 2021 Yala Season. Accordingly, the proposals made by the Minister of Agriculture to award the following procurement for the supply fertilizer as per the recommendation made by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee with regard to the said quotations, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n* \tTo procure 40,500+5% MTs of Urea (Granular) under 270 days credit period from M/s Swiss Singapore Overseas Pte. Ltd. at US$343.10 per 1 MT. \n\n* \tTo procure 8,500+5% MTs of Urea (Prilled) under 180 days credit period from M/s Valency International Pte. Ltd. at US$ 364.74 per 1 MT.\n\n* \tTo procure 13,900+5% MTs of Muriate of Potash under 180 days credit period from M/s Agricultural Resources and Investments Pte. Ltd. at US$ 258.74 per 1 MT."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Projects proposed to be implemented by the State Ministry of Livestock, Farm Promotion and Dairy & Egg related Industries for the upcoming 5 years from the year 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10927",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to update the activities of the following projects presently being implemented for the increase of production capacity of the other industries related to local dairy production and livestock development and implement the same during the next 05 years. \n\n* Project for the popularization of liquid milk consumption.\n* Project for the establishment of breeder farms.\n* Swine industry development project.\n* Small and medium scale poultry farms development project.\n* Enhancement of productivity through promotion of small and medium scale diary farms.\n* Medium term livestock development project."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Construction of Rural Roads and Bridges",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10926",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The State Ministry of Rural Roads and other Infrastructure which is coming under the purview of the Ministry of Highways has planned to construct 5000 rural bridges such as pedestrian bridges and vehicular bridges all over the Island. It has been proposed to implement the said construction of bridges process under the project of the rehabilitation of 100,000km rural road network of the Government. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways to implement the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "The Project to provide financial facilities for the sectors mostly affected by the COVID -19 pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10925",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- A project has been designed to implement with the participation of the Bank of Ceylon and the Peoples' Bank under the COVID-19 Emergency and Crisis Response Facility of the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank with the objective of providing required funds for the mostly affected sectors by the COVID - 19 pandemic such as tourism, textile, construction, trade, manufacturing, agricultural exports and health care. The proposed project will assist to increase the liquidity support for the small and medium scale enterprises of those sectors. Under the said project, two credit facilities of US$ 90 million each will be granted for the Bank of Ceylon and the Peoples' Bank and the said two banks will grant sub-loans to their clients. Therefore, the proposal made by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to take necessary action to implement the said project including the entering into relevant agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Removal of scrap metals in the Kankesanthurai Cement Factory Premises",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10924",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Preliminary plans have been made by the Ministry of Industries to launch a Cement Manufacturing Project at the Kankesanthurai Cement Factory premises. Accordingly, a Five -Member Committee has been appointed to conduct a site inspection and make recommendations relating to the removal of scrap metals and cleaning of the said factory premises. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries as recommended by the said Committee to remove the unusable buildings, structures, machinery, scrap metals and steel at the Kankesanthurai Cement Factory Premises, by following the Government Procurement Procedure, based on the valuation made by the Chief Government Valuer, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Procurement of 150MW of Solar Power Capacities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10923",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to implement the procurement process on the establishment of 150MW Solar Power Plants in different locations across the country. Accordingly, approval has been granted at the Cabinet Meeting held on 14th December 2020, to award the procurements in respect of which appeals had not been made against the recommendations of the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee (CANC) and for which International Bids were called under 05 Packages. The Procurement Appeal Board has rejected the appeals made in respect of the rest of the procurements. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power, to award the procurements to the selected bidders for the Anuradhapura, Habarana, Matara, Galle, Deniyaya, Kosgama, Mathugama, Pannala, Mahawa and Kurunegala Grid Sub\u2011Stations for a period of 20 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Granting Long term lease of a land to the Sri Lanka Cashew Corporation for the Cashew Seed Garden",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10922",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- A land block in extent of 86.093 hectares (212 acres 02 roods 23.95 perches) located in the Ralmaduwa Grama Niladhari Division, Wanathavilluwa where the Agricultural Research Unit\u2011 Eluwankulama was maintained, has been transferred to the Sri Lanka Cashew Corporation in July 1998 for development and use. Accordingly, the Sri Lanka Cashew Corporation is using the said land for Cashew cultivation. The Sri Lanka Cashew Corporation has planned to maintain a collection of Cashew varieties available in different areas of Sri Lanka through the Plant Breeding Centre located in the said land, in association with the Faculty of Agriculture of Wayamba University. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Lands, to transfer the said land to the Sri Lanka Cashew Corporation on long term lease basis for a period of 50 years, to implement the said project which is of tremendous economic and social significance, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Allocation of land blocks from the Regional Industrial Estates to set up Industries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10921",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Regional Industrial Services Committee and the Project Evaluation Committee of the Ministry of Industries have recommended the allocation of land blocks from 08 Industrial Estates for 22 investors, subject to a lease period of 35 years, under the Regional Industrial Estates Development Programme implemented by the Ministry of Industries. Those investors are to invest Rs.24,047.85 million and US$ 3 million for the said projects and it has been estimated that 3,326 direct employment opportunities will be generated from these projects. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries, to allocate the said land blocks for the investors subject to the relevant conditions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Sri Lanka's Regional Trade Agreements (RTAs) and Free Trade Agreements (FTAs)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10920",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Regional Trade Agreements and Free Trade Agreements are a key feature in the International Trade and those Agreements have increased in number as well as in complexity over the past few years. Sri Lanka has also entered into such several Trade Agreements and it has been observed that the country could not achieve the expected outcome under some Agreements. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade, to review such Agreements currently under negotiations in order to comply with the National Policy Framework of the 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour' and resume negotiations accordingly and, to take necessary action to explore the feasibility of entering into new Regional Trade Agreements and Free Trade Agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-08-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-02-08",
    "description": "Maintaining the 'Ape Gama' Folk Heritage Exhibition Centre situated in Pelawatta, Battaramulla in Colombo District productively",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10919",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Ape Gama' Folk Heritage Exhibition Centre has been administrated as a project of the Central Cultural Fund from the beginning up to now and the State Ministry of National Heritage, Performing Arts and Rural Arts Promotion conducts its administration under the guidance of the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs. Since neither a specific staff nor a Vote of Expenditure for the maintenance and administration has been allocated for the Centre, which is 13 acres 03 roods 25.1 perches in extent, it has been observed that it is being inactive. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs, to appoint a definite staff for maintaining the 'Ape Gama' Folk Heritage Exhibition Centre and to take necessary action to maintain the Centre in a formal manner, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Development and operation of East Container Terminal and West Container Terminal of the Colombo South Port",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10918",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Memorandum of Cooperation has been entered into between Sri Lanka, India and Japan for the development of the East Container Terminal of the Colombo South Port. The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020-10-26 granted approval to appoint a Negotiating Committee to evaluate an investment proposal submitted by an Indian investor in accordance with the provisions of the said Agreement. Accordingly, the following proposals made by the Minister of Ports and Shipping based on the recommendations submitted by the aforesaid Negotiating Committee, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n    \u2022 to operate the East Container Terminal as a fully owned container terminal of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority.\n      \n    \u2022 to take necessary action to develop the West Container Terminal of Colombo South Port as a Public Private Partnership by the parties nominated by India and Japan in association with the Sri Lanka Ports Authority on the basis of returning the same within 35 years, with a view to developing Colombo Port as a competitive port in this region and to adopt the International Agreements signed by the Government of Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Production of railway passenger coaches domestically",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10917",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The requirement of Railway passenger coaches, as at today is approximately 700 and it has been estimated that this could be increased up to 800 over the next 05 years. The available Railway passenger coaches are of various ages, 30% out of which are over 30 years old, 60% are over 25 to 30 years old and 10% have been in service for 12 years or less. 42% of the total Railway passenger coach requirement could be fulfilled by 160 coaches to be received from India and 140 coaches expected to be received from coach repairing project. Therefore, further 50% of total fleet need replacement or rehabilitation early. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to select an investor adopting the Government Procurement Guidelines to produce 100 Railway passenger coaches with the participation of private sector as a remedy to prevailing situation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Amendments to the Civil Procedure Code",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10916",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Civil Procedure Code makes provisions to set aside the judgment given by a court of law upon a request made by a defendant to the court of law with notice to the plaintiff stating that he has reasonable grounds for such default, within 14 days of the decree entered against him for default. It has been observed that by taking advantage of these provisions, it has enabled the defendant to employ delaying tactics and to resist a just claim of the plaintiff. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to amend the section 88(2) of the Civil Procedure Code, enabling to prevent such adverse conditions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Amending the Industrial Disputes Act, No.43 of 1950 enabling to expedite the measures to be taken in respect of private sector employees subject to disciplinary inquiries or interdiction",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10915",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Labour Laws do not specify the period of time during which a final ruling should be given having conducted a formal disciplinary inquiry on such allegations in the event of an interdiction upon anti-disciplinary acts or acts of misconduct by Private Sector Employees. As a result, it has been found that in some cases, interdicted employees face various economic and social difficulties. Therefore, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Labour to amend the Industrial Disputes Act No.43 of 1950 incorporating provisions for the issuance of a final disciplinary order within 6 months from the date of interdiction of an employee and to pay half of the wage provided that the misconduct is not a financial fraud."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Restructuring of the Prisons Intelligence Unit",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10914",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need to restructure the existing prison intelligence unit so as to perform security duties, protection of special prisoners/suspects, riot control and security duties, without being limited to the functions of the said unit has been identified. Accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to restructure the existing Prison Intelligence Unit as the \"Sri Lanka Prison Emergency Action Tactical Force\" (SPEAT FORCE) enabling to assign identified specific duties in addition to the duties performed by ordinary prison officers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Recommencement of the Bunkering Business by the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10913",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The monopoly of the supply of bunkering oil was upheld by the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation under the \"Lanka Maritime Services Limited\" affiliated to Ceylon Petroleum Corporation and that business was opened to the Private Sector in 2004. Accordingly, the bonding storage facility which is maintained at the Sri Lanka Ports Authority has been sold to the Private Sector by the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation and as such, the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation has ceased to function from such bunkering business. Therefore, few suppliers are dealing in the process of importing bunkering oil in small scale, store that oil stocks at the Jaya Container Terminal (bonding storage) and then they are re-exported to ships sailing across the territorial sea of Sri Lanka. The Ceylon Petroleum Corporation possesses the capacity of importing fuel oil in bulk at favourable prices and supplying the same to licensed suppliers at competitive prices. Therefore, with the possibility of supplying of bunkering oil at competitive prices, it will be possible to increase the number of naval vessels sailing across the territorial waters of Sri Lanka. Under such circumstances, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence for the programme presented by Minister of Energy with regard to the recommencement of the import of bunkering oil business by the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Amending Fertilizer Subsidy Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10912",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approximately 382,000 metric tons of fertilizer for paddy cultivation is provided free of charge to 1.45 million beneficiaries annually. Further, the opportunities have been provided to obtain subsidized fertilizers in the market for other non-paddy crops without any restrictions. It has been found that, under the existing methodology, the fertilizer subsidy for non-paddy crops is being utilized by other parties outside the target farmers, making it difficult for farmers to meet their fertilizer requirements when required. Due to this, it has also been found that, the Government has to incur more than the estimated cost for the fertilizer subsidy program annually. Taking these matters into consideration, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to implement the fertilizer subsidy program in future as follows:\n\n*\tImplementing the fertilizer subsidy scheme for paddy in the same manner as at present for 2 seasons per year, subject to a maximum of 02 hectares per one cultivation season.\n*\tProviding opportunity to purchase fertilizer under the fertilizer subsidy programme up to a maximum of 05 hectares per year, subject to the quantities determined by the relevant research institutes for each non-paddy crops."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Streamlining Government Intervention in the Organic Fertilizer Production and Distribution Sectors",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10911",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need of directing Sri Lanka's agriculture to use organic fertilizer has been emphasized by the Government Policy Statement ''Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour''. In order to monitor the strategic plan of implementing this policy, it has been identified the need of having a Government institute with modern technology and research facilities, capable of carrying out production, marketing, research and development of organic fertilizers in line with international standards for direction of strategical arrangements to implement the said policy. Accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture for the conversion of Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Company Ltd. into an institution for production, formulation and distribution of organic fertilizer and chemical fertilizer of higher generations and undertaking research and development in the relevant field, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Implementation of the Project on Integrated Management of Forestry, Agriculture and Tourism sectors through Community based Ecosystem-approaches",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10910",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Non-eco friendly land use plans have resulted in the breakdown of ecological balance thereby causing a number of social, environmental, economic and health problems at present. In order to control this situation, the Government has initiated various programmes and the need of having a programme with long term plans which is jointly implemented in the sectors of Agriculture, Tourism and Forestry has been identified. Accordingly, the \u201cProject on Integrated Management of Forestry, Agriculture and Tourism sectors through Community based ecosystem approaches\u201d has been designed to be implemented in the Malwathu Oya basin in Anuradhapura, Mannar, Vavuniya and Puttlam districts as a pilot project. It has been agreed to grant a credit facility of US$ 3.34 million under the Global Environment Facility of the United Nations Development Programme for this project. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to implement the said project during the period from 2021-2024, utilizing the said grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Providing lands in the Mahaveli regions on lease basis for commercial agriculture",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10909",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has taken measures to restrict the importation of identified food crops that could be cultivated within the country with a view to controlling unnecessary foreign exchange outflow. Accordingly, the importation of maize has been suspended and approximately 250,000 metric tons of maize required for the production of Thriposha and other animal food has to be produced domestically. In this context, it has been planned to provide underutilized 2,750 acres of Rambukkanoya area managed by the Sri Lanka Mahaweli Authority not belonging to the identified reservations, to the local agricultural investors on lease basis in view of encouraging them to produce maize in large scale domestically. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation to allocate the relevant blocks of land to the recognized local investors on lease basis for a period of one (01) year and to grant the relevant land blocks to the same investors on long - term lease basis as per the provisions of the State Land Ordinance upon the success of the cultivation in future, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Submission of the Gazette Notification No.2160/33 dated 2020.01.30 issued, publishing the Motor Traffic (Restrictions) Regulations to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10908",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been reported that some container vehicles running under the Sedawatte railway bridge of the road section from Thotalanga junction to Kohilawatte junction of Colombo \u2013 Hanwella (AB 010) highway cause damages to the railway bridge due to the negligence of container drivers. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to present the Gazette Notification No. 2160/33 dated 2020.01.30 issued in terms of the provisions of the Motor Traffic Act in Parliament in order to ban the travelling of all the vehicles which transport containers, other vehicles with more than 3.2m in total height above ground level and vehicles with a load height of more than 3.2m above ground level through the said road section, with a view to avoiding dangerous accidents caused by the same and to introduce alternative routes for those restricted vehicles, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Revising the Temporary Permit (MTA 37) issued by a Policeman",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10907",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- When conducting an investigation pertaining to an offence under section 135 (4) of the Motor Traffic Act, a Police officer would take charge the relevant driving license and issue a temporary permit. The specimen form relating to that has been published in the Extraordinary Gazette Notification dated 1951\u201108\u201125. Since, the contents in that temporary permit are inadequate at present, the then Minister in charge of the subject of transport issued the Gazette Notification No 2144/19 dated 2019\u201110\u201109 revising the said format to suit with the present requirements. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to submit the said Gazette Notification to Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Mutual Cooperation between Diplomatic Academies / Training Institutions of BIMSTEC Member States",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10906",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC) has been established in the year 1997 as a forum to further enhance the cooperation within the region of the Bay of Bengal. At present, seven (07) countries including Sri Lanka are members of this organisation. It has been proposed to enter into an MoU on Mutual Corporation between Diplomatic Academies / Training Institutions by the member countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Foreign Minister to adopt the proposed MoU at the 05th BIMSTEC Summit scheduled to be held in Sri Lanka in early of this year, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Resettlement of internally displaced landless families in the welfare centres in Jaffna District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10905",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet of Ministers was granted previously for taking necessary measures for granting a block of land in extent of 20 perches at a cost of Rs. 700,000 per each for 381 landless families living in the welfare centres in Jaffna District, subject to the valuation of the Chief Valuer. 233 families have been identified as landless families out of 409 families currently in welfare centres in Jaffna District and they have made requests to obtain alternative lands in close proximity to their birth places. However, obtaining a 20 perch block of land at a sum of Rs. 700,000/- has been found to be difficult as per the current prices of lands in those areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing, to purchase blocks of land in extent of 10 - 20 perches from private owners subject to the valuation of Chief Valuer without exceeding aforesaid amount of money and provide them to the said families and to take necessary action to settle those families in the said lands expeditiously by preparing a mechanism to construct houses on those lands parallel to aforesaid task, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Hosting 55th Asian Development Bank (ADB) Annual Meeting in Sri Lanka in 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10904",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tApproval of the Board of Governors of the Asian Development Bank has been received to hold its 55th Annual Meeting in Colombo. This meeting would be attended by approximately 3000-4000 participants including more than 30 Ministers of Finance, Governors of Central Banks from member countries, Chief Executives of major global banks and companies and other local and international dignitaries and media personnel. The proposed meeting is scheduled to be held for 04 days from 2022\u201105\u201102 to 2022\u201105\u201105 and a number of other meetings and functions related to this are to be held parallel to the said meeting. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to make necessary arrangements to host the Annual Meeting of the Asian Development Bank in May, 2022 in Sri Lanka and to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) relevant to this with the Asian Development Bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Continues implementation of the Micro-finance Credit Facility Programme for the debt-ridden people of the Northern and North Central Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10903",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The credit scheme with low interest rate introduced through Co-operative Rural Banks and Thrift & Credit Co-operative Societies, with the intention of getting the rural low income people who have become debt-ridden after obtaining loans from various micro finance credit schemes, out of the debt trap, is presently being implemented by 06 District Secretariats in the Northern and North Central Provinces. Under the said scheme, Rs. 542 million, as Rs. 292 million for Northern Province and Rs. 250 million for North Central Province, has been granted to the beneficiaries to the date and this money is maintained as a revolving fund of the said loan scheme. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance for continuous implementation of the relevant credit scheme by using the money of the said revolving fund, for the increase of the maximum credit limit granted under the same up to Rs. 100,000/- and for the reduction of the annual interest rate pertaining to the said loans from 9% to 6% in order to provide the debt-ridden people with a relief, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-02-01-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-02-01",
    "description": "Appointing new members to the National Border Management Committee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10902",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-02-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- ''The National Border Management Committee'' has been established to function as the focal point within the Government responsible for assessing high level risks and setting priorities and goals on all aspects of border management in Sri Lanka. Heads of the other institutions involved in the border management have been appointed as the ex-officio members of this Committee under the chairmanship of the Secretary, Ministry of Defence. The proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to appoint the Chairman of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority, one of the important entity in the boarder management, the Chief of Defence Staff who have been entrusted the coordination activities among Tri Forces and the Ministry of Defence, and the Secretary to the Ministry in-charge of the subject of Fisheries as members of the said Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Providing 500,000 doses of AstraZeneca's COVISHIELD Vaccine by the Government of India to Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10901",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hon. Prime Minister informed the Cabinet that the Indian High Commissioner has conveyed that the Government of India has decided to provide 500,000 doses of AstraZeneca's COVISHIELD vaccine to Sri Lanka taking into account the longstanding relationship between Sri Lanka and India and the cooperation experienced between the two countries during the last year in facing the COVID\u201119 pandemic situation and that the stock of vaccine is scheduled to arrive in the country on the 28th of this month. The Cabinet of Ministers decided to convey the appreciation and gratitude of the Government of Sri Lanka  to the Government of India for  timely cooperation extended in the hour of need."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Amendments to the Regulations and Orders made under the Foreign Exchange Act No.12 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10900",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "In terms of the provisions of the Foreign Exchange Act No.12 of 2017, the Minister in charge of the subject of Finance is entrusted the power of promulgating Regulations in order to implement the said Act subject to the Cabinet approval in consultation with the Monetary Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, Regulations No.01 of 2017, Regulations No.02 of 2017 and Regulations No.03 of 2017 have been promulgated and Orders made under Section 8 and Section 31 of the Act have been issued. It has been found necessary to amend the said Regulations and Orders to suit with the present requirements. As such, the proposal made by  Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to take the following measures in accordance with the provisions of  the Foreign Exchange Act No.12 of 2017, was approved by the Cabinet. \n \n    \u2022 to promulgate the following Regulations and submit the same to Parliament for approval.\ni.\tForeign Exchange  (Classes of Capital Transactions Undertaken Outside Sri Lanka by a Person Resident in Sri Lanka) Regulations \tNo.01 of 2021 \nii.\tForeign Exchange  (Classes of Capital Transactions Undertaken in Sri \tLanka by a Person Resident in Sri Lanka) Regulations No.02 of 2021 \niii.\tForeign Exchange  (Remittance of Funds by Emigrants) \tRegulation No.3 of 2021\t\t\n vi.\tForeign Exchange (Classes of Miscellaneous Capital Transactions) Regulations No.4 of 2021\nv.\tForeign Exchange  (Opening and Maintenance of Accounts for the purpose of engaging in Foreign Exchange Transactions) Regulations \tNo.5 of 2021\n\n    \u2022 to make Orders in accordance with  Section 8 and Section 31 of the \tsaid Act."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-014-en",
