    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Procurement for supply of 14,000,000 bottles of 500ml Sodium Chloride Intravenous Infusion BP 0.9% w/v or Sodium Chloride Injection USP, 0.9% w/v",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10897",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- International Competitive Bidds have been invited for the procurement of the above drug which is used for volume replacement of the patients with Hypovolemia. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to award the said procurement to M/s. Sichuan Kelum Pharmaceutical Co. Ltd., China at a total C&F price of US$ 2.79 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Kuruwita-Erathna Sripada Road Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10896",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Kuruwita-Erathna road, one of the three main routes used by Sripada pilgrims to worship Sripada, is used by more than one hundred thousand of pilgrims during a season. Due to the non repairing of naturally formed stairs situated in this lane for a long time, Sripada pilgrims are faced with difficulties.  Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of National Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management to take necessary action to repair identified areas of the Kuruwita-Erathna road using the sleepers removed from railway rehabilitation activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Proposed Port related logistics sector development in Bloemandhal Area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10895",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka Ports Authority has identified the urgent necessity of developing the   logistics facilities of Colombo Port to meet the growing demand with efficiency to enhance the competitiveness of the Port. Accordingly, Sri Lanka Ports Authority intends to establish a  state of art Port related logistics sector  in  Bloemandhal Area. As the first stage of the said programme, it is scheduled to  establish a large warehouse complex for  Less than Container Load (LCL), Full Container Load (FCL), Multi Country Consolidation (MCC), cold storage facility, entrepot cargo handling and other port related logistics activities. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports and Shipping to take necessary action to call for Request for Proposals to identify a suitable investor/ investors to implement the proposed project on Build, Operate, Transfer basis as a Public Private Partnership Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Construction of Elevated Expressway connecting Outer Circular Highway at Athurugiriyta to Kelaniya New Bridge via Rajagiriya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10894",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Road Development Authority has conducted a feasibility study to construct an Elevated Expressway\u00a0 from the new Kelani Bridge to the Athurugiriya Interchange on the Outer Circular Highway via Rajagiriya along the Port Access Elevated Expressway which is being constructed under the funds of Asian Development Bank. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of  Highways to take necessary action to call for Request for Proposals (RFP) to  implement the above project with 100% foreign financing on Build, Operate, Transfer (BOT) basis, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Conducting the Feasibility Study to implement the first Pumped Storage Hydro Power Plant in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10893",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The intermittent nature and non-firmness of generation of power through certain renewable energy resources make it technically challenging to add more such energy plants into the main electricity grid. In order to face this situation and store excess generated capacity, it has been identified the necessity of establishing the \u201cPumped Storage Hydropower Plant\u201d. Under the Long Term Generation Plan for the period of 2018 \u2013 2037, it has been identified to operate a Pumped Storage Hydropower Plant in 03 phases from the year 2025 onwards. According to a study conducted in association with the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), the Aranayake area  in the Ma oya Valley and Wewathenna area in Kandy, have been recognized as suitable for the construction of the proposed power plant. The Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB) intends to identify the most suitable place out of those two locations and conduct a comprehensive feasibility study  in this regard.  There is a potential of securing the funds required for the purpose, out of the balance funds of the \u201cGreen Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Project\u201d under the Asian Development Bank. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power, to conduct a comprehensive feasibility study on the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Amending the Coconut Development Act to amalgamate all the Regulating State Institutions of the Coconut Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10892",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Coconut Cultivation Board, Coconut Development Authority and the Coconut Research Institute have been established under the Coconut Development Act, No.46 of 1971 for the Coconut cultivation, industry and research areas. And, the Kapruka Fund Management Board has been established under the Kapruka Fund Act, No.31 of 2005. Even though the said institutions have been set up for coordinating all functions related to Coconut cultivation regulation, those institutions have failed to provide services to clients at the anticipated level due to inefficient coordination between the said institutions. Taking into consideration the duplication of certain functions discharged by the said institutions and clients having to liaise with several institutions to meet their requirements and incurring of a considerable cost for its maintenance,  it has been decided to amalgamate these 4 institutions into one establishment. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation, to amend the Coconut Development Act, No.46 of 1971, facilitating the amalgamation of the said institutions and setting up of a new institution namely, ''Coconut Cultivation and Allied Industries Development Authority'', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Enacting a new Petroleum Resources Development Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10891",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though the Petroleum Resources Development Act, No.26 of 2003 has widely identified the requirement of local Petroleum and gas exploration and developing production industry, it has been observed that those sectors have not been interpreted properly for its management. Accordingly, during the deliberations held with the relevant parties, it was identified the necessity of revoking the said Act and formulating a new Act to differentiate the required interpretations, regulations, policy and national operator. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy, to revoke the Petroleum Resources Development Act, No.26 of 2003 and to draft a new Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Obtaining consultancy services for planning of construction of Courts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10890",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the light of administration of justice, a large number of cases are pending before the courts in Sri Lanka and as a relief for the said issue, action is being taken to increase the number of Judges. The other facilities of courts are to be met concurrently and it has been planned to construct 100 new court houses island\u2011wide within the next 3 years. Under this plan, it has also been planned to construct multi\u2011storey court buildings and to improve the existing buildings. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, to obtain the required consultancy services from the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB)   which is fully fledged with experience in constructing court buildings, for the implementation of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Establishment of Diplomatic Relations with Liechtenstein",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10889",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Liechtenstein, a small land locked country situated between Switzerland and Austria is a country with Parliamentary Democracy and a Constitutional Monarch as its Head of State. It is a highly industrialized country which manufactures mainly pharmaceuticals, precision instruments and electronics and is considered as one of the world's richest countries. Last year, its Gross Domestic Product (GDP) was US$ 5.8 billion and the per capita income was around US$ 143,700.   Liechtenstein, being a member of the United Nations' Organization, is also a member state of the European Economic Area with low income tax regime that has attracted investments through developed banking system, and maintains diplomatic relations with many countries including India and Pakistan. With a view to improving the friendship and cooperation between the two countries at the bilateral and multilateral levels, the Government of Liechtenstein has expressed its interest to establish diplomatic relations with the Government of Sri Lanka. It will enable Sri Lanka to attract investments and high spending tourists by establishing diplomatic relations between the two countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Foreign Minister, to establish diplomatic relations with Liechtenstein, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Increasing the Daily Wage of Plantation Sector Workers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10888",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the provisions in the ''Plantation Workers' Wages Collective Agreement 2019 \u2013 2021'', the Plantation sector employees are entitled for a daily wage of Rs.750/- including a Fixed Price Allowance of Rs.50/- and for an another allowance called ''Over kilo rate'' when exceeding the amount of kilos related to the productivity.\n\nIt was proposed to provide a daily wage of Rs.1,000/- to the Plantation sector through the budget proposals presented in Parliament in November, 2020. Even though several deliberations have been conducted with the signatories  to the ''Plantation Workers' Wages Collective Agreement 2019 \u2013 2021'' for the implementation of the said proposal, the Employers' Federation of Ceylon representing the Planters' Association which is one party to the said Collective Agreement, has proposed to increase the daily wage up to Rs.920/-. Taking these matters into consideration, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour, to take necessary steps enabling the increase of the daily wage of the Plantation sector workers up to Rs.1,000/- through the Wages Board, for the implementation of the said budget proposal, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Revising the existing Estate Housing Scheme to provide safer habitats targeting the entire Plantation Community",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10887",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- From the year 2000 up to now, the ''Estate Housing Scheme'' for the construction of new houses to replace Line Rooms for the Estate community has been implemented in different ways. At present, 02 projects are being carried out namely, the project of providing a single house in extent of 550 square feet with 07 perches free hold land ownership under the Government sponsorship and the project for providing a single house in extent of 550 square feet, in collaboration with the Governments of India and Sri Lanka. Since it creates a discrepancy due to the dissimilarity of the criterion applied for providing houses under these schemes, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing, to follow a single common procedure for providing houses to the Estate community and to pursue action as follows under the said procedure, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*  removal of the existing Line Rooms and construction of new houses on the same location.\n\n*\timplementing housing schemes in other locations in case there is a risk of disasters such as floods/landslides and there is insufficient space at the locations of the Line Rooms.\n\n*\tconstruction of the first phase of the house with 550 square feet at a cost of Rs.1.3 million, enabling to convert the same into 02 floors later.\n\n*\tallocation of 03 perches in addition, to each housing beneficiary for  animal husbandry and home gardening purposes.\n\n*\trecovery of only 50% of the value of constructing houses from the beneficiaries and granting of a period of 20 years for the purpose.\n*\tProviding facilities for tentative accommodation at another place in close proximity of those Line Rooms until new houses will be constructed at the same location."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-25-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-01-25",
    "description": "Report of the Auditor General on the President's Fund - 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10886",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of Section 9(2) of the President's Fund Act, No.7 of 1978 to be read with the provisions of Article 154(3) of the Constitution of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka, the Auditor General has audited the President's Fund pertaining to the financial year ended on 31st December, 2018. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to table the said Report of the Auditor General pertaining to the financial year 2018 in accordance with the provisions of Section 10 of the said Fund Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-18-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-01-18",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the Return and Readmission of Persons between the Commonwealth of Australia and the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10885",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between Australia and Sri Lanka incorporating the provisions for the exchange of persons staying in violation of the immigration laws between two countries. The said Memorandum of Understanding ensures a safe and orderly return to their country of residence. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of National Security, Home affairs and Disaster Management to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Commonwealth of Australia and the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka on the Return and Readmission of Persons, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
