    "description": "Sign Language Draft Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10878",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2010\u201109\u201108 to accept the Sign Language as a recognized language. As a considerable number of hearing impaired people reside in Sri Lanka, making provisions to accept sign language as a recognized mode of communication would empower the hearing impaired people, in accessing their educational requirements, legal affairs, health facilities, public and personal services. Accordingly, the need to establish the sign language as a recognized language in Sri Lanka has been identified. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to make necessary provisions enabling to accept the sign language as a formal mode of communication by an act of Parliament and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-18-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-01-18",
    "description": "Amendments to the Financial Transactions Reporting Act, No.6 of 2006, Prevention of Money Laundering Act, No.5 of 2006 and the Convention on the Suppression of Terrorist Financing Act, No.25 of 2005",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10877",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet was granted at its meeting held on 05th May 2010 to make amendments to the Financial Transactions Reporting Act, to address the deficiencies recognized by the Legal Review Committee and Asia Pacific Group on Money Laundering (APG) as approved by the National Coordinating Committee (NCC) on Anti Money Laundering and Combating the Financing of Terrorism and in compliance with the recommendations of the Financial Action Task Force (FATF).\n\nAccordingly, the task of formulating draft amending legislation has been initiated and subsequently, the Asia Pacific Group on Money Laundering has identified several further amendments to be made in addition to those which have already been recognized during its mutual assessment. The draft prepared by a Committee comprising the representatives of the relevant agencies such as the Attorney General's Department, Legal Draftsman's Department and the Financial Intelligence Unit (FIU) was also revisited by the International Monetary Fund Technical Assistance Mission in March, 2017. As such, with a view to addressing the issues so identified, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to amend the following Acts and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n* \tFinancial Transactions Reporting Act, No.6 of 2006\n* \tPrevention of Money Laundering Act, No.5 of 2006. \n* \tConvention on the Suppression of Terrorist Financing Act, No.25 of 2005-"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-18-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-01-18",
    "description": "Recommendations of the Cabinet Sub Committee on Legislation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10876",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposals submitted to the Cabinet regarding the amendment of the following Acts, have been referred to the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Legislation for its recommendations. As such, taking into consideration the recommendations made by the said Sub\u2011Committee, Cabinet decided to instruct the Legal Draftsman to formulate the amending legislation for the purpose.\n\n* \tImmigrants and Emigrants Act (repealing the existing Immigrants and Emigrants Act, No.20 of 1948 and the relevant amendments and replacement of a new Act)\n\n* \tStamp Duty (Special Provisions) Act, No.12 of 2006 and Provincial Councils (Transfer of Stamp Duty) Act, No.13 of 2011\n\n* \tNational Minimum Wage of Workers Act, No.3 of 2016\n\n* \tCommunity Based Corrections Act, No.46 of 1999\n\n* \tSection 53 of the Penal Code (provisions relating to death sentence on minors)"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-18-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-01-18",
    "description": "Collaboration between M/s CINEC Campus (Pvt.) Limited., Mahapola Ports & Maritime Academy of Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA) and Sri Lanka Port Management and Consultancy Services Limited (SLPMCS) for design and delivery of Maritime Training Programmes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10875",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is essential to have a highly skilled and disciplined labour force which may be utilized for the ports and maritime industry for the growth and rapid expansion of the ports and maritime sector. The Mahapola Ports & Maritime Academy within the purview of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority is discharging the said functions. With a view to securing the related port services and other services, the Sri Lanka Port Management and Consultancy Services Private Limited (SLPMCS) was established with the contribution of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA), Ceylon Shipping Corporation, Colombo Dock Yard PLC, Ceylon Association of Shipping Agents (CASA) and the Ceylon Shipping Lines Ltd.. \n\t\nAnd, M/s CINEC Campus (Pvt.) Ltd. is another approved maritime training institute in Sri Lanka.\n\nIt has been proposed to share knowledge and resources between the Sri Lanka Ports Authority, Mahapola Ports & Maritime Academy, Sri Lanka Port Management and Consultancy Services Private Limited and M/s CINEC Campus (Pvt.) Ltd. for achieving the purposes of promoting the seafaring career within the country, providing financial facilities to the trainees enrolled to the courses and promoting the Sri Lankan seafarers in foreign countries. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports and Shipping to authorize the Sri Lanka Ports Authority to enter into a collaboration with M/s CINEC Campus Pvt. Ltd. for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-18-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-01-18",
    "description": "Granting relief to electricity consumers affected from COVID-19 Outbreak",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10874",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the proposals submitted by the Minister of Power pertaining to provision of reliefs to electricity consumers affected by COVID-19 pandemic situation and those submitted by the Minister of Tourism regarding provision of reliefs to the tourism related institutions on payment of electricity and water bills, approval of the Cabinet was granted to pursue action as follows:\n\n* \tto provide a grace period of 06 months from the date of electricity bill to the domestic, commercial and industrial electricity consumers in the areas which were under the continuous lockdown for more than 14 days, to pay the electricity bills for the relevant period and not to disconnect the electricity supply until such time.\n* \tto allow the Cinema Halls registered at the National Film Corporation to settle the electricity bills from March to December, 2020 in 12 equal installments from the date of electricity bill and not to disconnect the electricity supply until such time.\n\n* \tto allow the registered accommodation providers of the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority (SLTDA) to settle the cumulative electricity and water bills from 01st March 2020 to 28th February 2021 in 12 equal installments and not to disconnect the relevant supplies until such time."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-18-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-01-18",
    "description": "Providing Tariff Concession to Mongolia under the Asia Pacific Trade Agreement (APTA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10873",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mongolia has officially become a party to the Asia Pacific Trade Agreement (APTA) on 29th September 2020 to which Sri Lanka has also been a Participating State. Accordingly, Sri Lanka as a Participating State, is supposed to reciprocally exchange tariff concessions with Mongolia. Mongolia, as similar to Bangladesh and Laos who are parties to the said trade agreement, is also entitled to acquire the same tariff concessions provided under the relevant agreement. As such, the proposal made by the Foreign Minister to provide the said tariff concessions and to conduct negotiations with Mongolia to identify the reciprocal tariff concessions to be further agreed on between parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-18-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-01-18",
    "description": "Establishment of a dedicated unit for International Cooperation under the purview of the Foreign Ministry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10872",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to achieving a robust economic diplomacy approach in the context of changing global economic and political environment along with the emerging Asia-centric economic landscape, it has been identified the essentiality of establishing a dedicated unit for formulating policies relating to economic diplomacy within the purview of the Foreign Ministry for the purpose of coordinating the functions of all key economic institutions. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Foreign Minister to establish a special unit for International Cooperation comprising the experts in the relevant fields, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Construction of a bridge across Benthara river along the Ittepana Horawala Thotupola road in Ittepana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10871",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Road Development Authority (RDA) has planned to construct a new bridge and its approaches across Benthara River along the Ittepana\u2011Horawala\u2011Thotupola road in Ittepana. The proposed bridge is about 160m in length and the total carriageway width is 10.4 m. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways, to construct the said bridge under the \u201c100,000 km of Roads Improvement Project\u201d, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Project for the establishment of a Trade Centre on the State land adjoining the Rajarata University, Mihinthale",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10870",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Through the \u201cVistas of Prosperity and Splendour\u201d, the Policy Statement of the Government, medium term plans are being formulated for increasing the number of students who have sat the G.C.E. (Advanced Level) Examination and gained entrance to universities and in this backdrop, the number of students gaining admission to the universities will increase. This will consequently escalate the expenditure incurred on the financial facilities provided by the Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund. Attention has been paid to invest funds of the said Scholarship Fund in other investment avenues with the objective of developing the Fund, generating income through long term stable stream of revenue and achieving direct development through investments. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade, to appoint a Committee representing the other relevant Ministries and institutions to implement a project for the establishment of a Trade Center on a plot of State land of 300 acres adjoining the Rajarata University, Mihinthale in the Anuradhapura District and to formulate an integrated plan on the implementation of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the implementation of the Project regarding \u2018Connecting the Sri Lankan Villages to the International Market\u2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10869",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of the project on \u201cConnecting the Sri Lankan Villages to the International Market\u201d is to develop a network between the local industrialists and the international market aiming at People Centric Economic Development in the country. The State Ministry of Samurdhi, Household Economy, Micro Finance, Self\u2011Employment and Business Development has implemented the \u201cEconomic Empowerment and Rural Development Programme \u2013 2020\u201d under the Department of Samurdhi Development and, the \u201cModel Village on Samurdhi Products\u201d is one of its major sub programmes. Through this sub programme also, it is expected to recognize the local industrialists intending to move quality products of the rural community to the international market. As such, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence to the proposal made by the Foreign Minister, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) by the State Ministry of Samurdhi, Household Economy, Micro Finance, Self\u2011Employment and Business Development with the State Ministry of Regional Cooperation, for the implementation of the \u201cConnecting the Sri Lankan Villages to the International Market\u201d project through an institutional network which has the potential of building a mechanism for covering all districts in the country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
