    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10866",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- International Competitive Bids have been called for the procurement of Enoxaparin Sodium that has been used for treatment of patients with heart diseases. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health, to award the procurement for the supply of 1,000,000 Pre\u2011filled Syringe of Enoxaparin Sodium Injection, 6,000IU in 0.6ml, to Ms. Slim Pharmaceuticals (Pvt) Ltd., at a total delivered price to Medical Supply Division (MSD) of Sri Lanka Rupees 695 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement for a research project to eliminate toxic chemicals in drinking water",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10865",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to enter into an Agreement between the University of Peradeniya and the University of Sri Jayawardenapura in collaboration with the Robert Gordon University, United Kingdom, pertaining to the research project funded by the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council (BBSRC). Through the proposed project, it is expected to invent an inexpensive and hygienic biological solution that can be produced using natural organisms to eliminate the highly toxic Cyanotoxin released from the Blue-Green Algae that has grown due to contamination of drinking water sources which is considered to be the cause for spreading of kidney disease in Sri Lanka. It is proposed to provide Sterling Pounds 0.3 million by the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council for the said project. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education, to enter into the relevant Agreement between the University of Peradeniya and the University of Sri Jayawardenapura in collaboration with the Robert Gordon University, United Kingdom, for the implementation of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Establishment of the Pirivena Development Fund Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10864",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government makes an allocation of Rs.4,500 million per year, in respect of the Piriven education. At present, the Pirivenas have been classified and registered as Maha Pirivenas, Mulika Pirivenas, Vidyayathana Pirivenas, Bilingual Pirivenas, Special Pirivenas and Buddhist Seela Matha Education Institutes and, currently 62,240 students are studying at those institutes. With a view to conducting Piriven education in a more formalized manner, the proposal made by the Minister of Education, to take necessary action to establish a Piriven Development Fund, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Design, Purchasing, Testing, Supervision of Installation and Commissioning of two (02) Nos. of Generator Stators in Unit 01 and Unit 02 machines at the Victoria Power Station - (Agenda Item No.25)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10863",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Victoria Power Station was commissioned in 1984, with an installed capacity of 210MW comprising three (03) 70MW units. A Technical Committee has been appointed to study the refurbishment to be made for the smooth functioning of the said Power Station in the next 30 years. The above Committee has recommended the installation of two (02) Generator Stators in Units 01 and 02 at the Power Station. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power to adopt the procurement process and select a suitable institution for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Procurement of 200 Nos. New Low Floor Buses for the Sri Lanka Transport Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10862",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The State Ministry of Vehicle Regulation, Bus Transport Services and Train Compartments and Motor Car Industry has planed to launch a public transport service with modern facilities in Colombo and suburbs with park and ride facility. For this purpose, it has been identified the need to purchase 200 buses suitable for short distance travel with more passenger comfort than the existing buses. Accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to purchase 200 high quality low floor buses following the limited competitive bidding procedure from reputable local companies and to secure necessary funds for this purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Amendment to the Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crimes and Witnesses Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10861",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Act, No.4 of 2015 provides a host of benefits to victims and witnesses. However, in accordance with the provisions of Section 10 of the Act, a request should be made to the Court of Appeal for bail causing severe inconveniences to the suspects and the accused. In particular, since the Court of Appeal is located in Colombo, the suspects residing in remote areas have had difficulty in filing the bail application, it has been found appropriate to amend the Act by substituting the High Court for the Court of Appeal for the purpose of granting bail to such persons. Further, it has also been identified that it is appropriate to amend the provision that \"A suspect shall be placed on remand till the end of the trial in respect of the offence which he had been enlarged on bail\" by substituting the phrase \"A suspect placed on remand for such period as may be considered reasonable by the court\". Accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to initiate necessary measures to amend the Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Act, No.04 of 2015, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Family Law Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10860",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The law relating to marriage, divorce, separation and the procedure thereto is laid down in the Marriage Registration Ordinance No.19 of 1907 and in the Civil Procedure Code. The need to amend the provisions of the Ordinance to suit to the present has been identified. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of justice to study the legal situation prevailing in other countries on family law by an of experts committee and take necessary action to draft a detailed Family Law bill covering all areas such as divorce, nullity, separation, alimony, custody of children and division of property."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Amendments to the Tea Control Act, No.51 of 1957",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10859",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2016\u201105\u201110 to amend the Tea Control Act, No.51 of 1957. Accordingly, the Legal Draftsman has prepared a draft bill and the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to further amend the said bill incorporating the following provisions, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tTo incorporate an interpretation as \u201cReclaimable Tea\u201d for tea that is separated after grading in the manufacturing process of Tea Factories.\n\n*\tTo designate the remnant after further reclaiming made tea from reclaimable tea as \u201cRefuse Tea\u201d.\n\n*\tTo incorporate legal provisions affected to tea processors including registration of them, issuance of licenses to them and administration."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Amendment of the Land Acquisition Act, No.9 of 1950",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10858",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The long period of time taken to follow the provisions of the Land Acquisition Act, No.9 of 1950 presently being in force, has caused impediments for various accelerated development activities implemented by the Government. The absence of following an unitary methodology in paying compensation for the lands acquired under the provisions of the said Act and having to spend a lot of time for paying compensation are the leading factors from among them. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Lands to take necessary action to amend the said Act to suit to the present day requirements enabling to acquire lands following a simple procedure and to pay compensation under an unitary methodology accordingly by minimizing the time taken to acquire lands, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Amending the maximum limit of compensation of the compensation formula implemented under the Termination of Employment of Workman (Special Provisions) Act, No.45 of 1971",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10857",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Termination of Employment of Workman (Special Provisions) Act, No.45 of 1971 amended by the Act No.12 of 2003 has been enacted to grant relief in terminating the service of workmen. In terms of the provisions of the said Act, a formula has been introduced to determine the compensation to be paid to the workmen when terminating their service. Accordingly, based on the Regulations imposed by the Minister of Labour, the amount will be determined, considering their period of service. Since, a provision to the effect that the compensation computed in terms of the aforesaid formula shall not exceed Rs.1,250,00 has also been incorporated into the Regulations, it has been found that, the compensation entitled to workmen receiving higher monthly salaries in the event of unfair dismissal from service or the closure of institutions remains at a lower level. Taking those issues into consideration, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour to increase the maximum limit of compensation from Rs.1,250,000 to Rs.2,500,00, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Marketing Pure Ceylon Tea through Online or Offline Platform in China",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10856",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal is made to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Sri Lanka Tea Board (SLTB) and Fujian Starchina International Trade Company Limited, Fujian Province, China, a subsidiary of Benny Tea Industry Company Ltd which is mainly engaged in tea imports, exports, e-business in clearing operations for marketing Pure Ceylon Tea through Online or Offline Platform in China. In terms of the said MoU, the said company has extended its willingness to set up a 5 G Online marketing platform which assists for warehousing and delivery network of China for online promotion and marketing of Ceylon Tea Brand name, in addition to the normal delivery of Ceylon Tea to China. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Sri Lanka Tea Board (SLTB) and Starchina International Trade Company Limited for marketing Pure Ceylon Tea through Online or Offline Platform in China, taking the advantage of potential opportunities for Ceylon Tea within the China tea market, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-01-11-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2021-01-11",
    "description": "Importation of frozen coconut kernel to use for coconut kernel based industries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10855",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-01-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2017\u201112\u201112 to import coconut kernel, subject to certain conditions, upon the insufficient supply of local coconut production for the coconut kernel based industries. Accordingly, 2,542 metric tons of coconut kernel have been imported during a period of 08 months. However, it has been estimated that there would be a shortage of 250 million nuts during this year. Therefore, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence for the proposals made by the Minister of Plantation for taking necessary action to import coconut kernel, subject to the same terms and conditions adopted previously, if the bi-monthly production of coconut remains less than 400 million continuously for 04 months."
  },
  {
