    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is been planned to expand the showroom of the Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation which is currently operating at the Narahenpita Dedicated Economic Center and establish a sales center called \u201cRajawasa\u201d in order to facilitate the customers to obtain the products manufactured and sold in the following Government Institutions under one roof at a reasonable price.\n*\t Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation\n*\tCeylon Fisheries Corporation\n*\tEducational Publications Department \n*\t Sri Lanka Tea Board\n*\t State Pharmaceuticals Corporation \n*\t B.B.C. Lanka Limited \n*\t Cooperative Development Department \n*\t Lanka Sathosa Limited\n*\t Ceylon Cashew Corporation\n*\t Mantai Salt Company\n*\t Litro Gas Limited\n*\t State Timber Corporation\n*\t Colombo Commercial Fertilizers Limited\n*\tCeylon Fertilizer Company Limited\n*\t Milco (Pvt.) Ltd\n*\t Coconut Development Authority\n*\t State Printing Corporation \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to modernize the premises where the showroom of the Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation presently located and to establish the proposed \u201cRajawasa\u201d Sales Center, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Providing relief for continuing inter-provincial bus operations in the face of the COVID-19 pandemic situation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10722",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been decided to waive off the following charges from the bus operators with effect from March 2020 for continuing inter-provincial bus operations amidst the COVID - 19 pandemic situation. \n\n*\tPermit renewal fees \n*\tLate fees \n*\tTender fees \n*\tLog fees \n*\tEntrance fees \n*\tExpressway temporary permit fees\n\nHowever, it has been identified that the bus operators need to be provided with relief enabling them to provide quality and efficient passenger transport service, since they have confronted with numerous constrains due to re-emergence of the pandemic situation. Accordingly, considering a proposal made by the Minister of Transport, the Cabinet granted approval for further providing the said concessions to the bus operators until the end of this year."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Establishment of a Dedicated Pharmaceutical Zone at Arabokka Estate, Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10721",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Presidential Task Force for Economic Revival and Poverty Alleviation has identified the pharmaceutical manufacturing industry as one of the potential industries that could attract foreign direct investments as well as earn foreign exchange. Therefore, it has been planned to establish a special pharmaceutical manufacturing zone with modern facilities within an area in extent of 400 acres of the Arabokka estate in Hambantota enabling to attract the world renowned pharmaceutical manufacturing companies. It is expected to declare the said project as a Strategic Development Project and grant concessions and incentives for the investors who invest in the said pharmaceutical manufacturing zone. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health for the establishment of 20 pharmaceutical manufacturing companies in 200 acres as phase I of this Project and another 20 pharmaceutical manufacturing companies in 200 more acres as its phase II and to furnish necessary infrastructure facilities by the Board of Investments of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Construction of a Paediatric Surgical Ward at the Teaching Hospital, Ratnapura",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10720",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Teaching Hospital, Ratnapura is the largest tertiary care hospital in the Sabaragamuwa province thus providing services to a large number of patients from other provinces as well. Adhering to the need of a surgical ward with proper facilities for the pediatric ward complex consisted of 116 beds, it has been planned to construct a paediatric surgical ward in the second storey of the relevant paediatric ward building. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Health for the construction of the proposed paediatric surgical ward with the funding of the donors and to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Health and the relevant donors for the said purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Reservation of Borrow Area for Offshore Sand Mining",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10719",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The requirement of long-term reserving of a borrow area for offshore sand mining has been arisen for mining sand for the construction industry and as well as for the projects implemented by Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation. The institution has satisfied its sand requirement since the year 1994 by mining sand within an offshore area of 61 square kilometers, having obtained exploration license periodically. Considering the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing, the Cabinet decided to grant approval to permit the the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation for offshore sand mining from the said borrow area of 61 square kilo meters for a period of 10 years, subject to carrying out an Environmental Impact Assessment."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Model Memorandum of Understanding on Police Cooperation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10718",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that entering into bilateral memoranda of understanding with the foreign police organizations who perform their duties in a highly efficient manner with the help of modern technology, will enable our police officers to share their experience, knowledge, skills and internationally recognized practices and standards on modern police duties. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of Internal Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management to enter into Memoranda of Understanding between the Ministry under which the subject of police falls and the foreign police organizations under the guidance of the Foreign Ministry to establish police cooperation under 17 fields such as terrorist activities, terrorist financing, drug related crimes, human trafficking and smuggling, money laundering, cybercrime etc, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Supply of security services to hospitals and other institutions under the Ministry of Health for the year 2020/2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10717",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contract has to be awarded for the supply of security services to hospitals and other institutions under the Ministry of Health for the year 2020/2021. Accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Health to award the supply of security services for 35 hospitals and institutions in the Western Province to Rakna Arakshaka Lanka Limited and to award the supply of security services for 26 hospitals and institutions located outside the Western Province to LRDC Services (Pvt) Ltd, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Providing locally manufactured sarees as uniforms for Dhamma School teachers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10716",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Granting of uniforms to the Dhamma School teachers serving in the Buddhist Dhamma Schools throughout the island is being implemented since the year 2004 and accordingly, 76,000 sarees are required for the year 2020 to be awarded as uniforms to Buddhist Dhamma School teachers .  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to purchase 76000 sarees made by local textile manufacturers at Rs. 2,400/- per each, to a sum of Rs. 182.4 million from Lanka Salusala Limited, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Re-establishment of the Spices and Allied Products Marketing Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10715",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Spices and Allied Products Marketing Board has been established under the provisions of section 2 of the State Agricultural Corporations Act No 11 of 1972. At its meeting held on 2008\u201107\u201116, the Cabinet decided that the functions of the said Board be vested with the Department of Export Agriculture and the institution be closed with effect from 2008\u201107\u201127. However, the Spices and Allied Products Marketing Board currently falls under the purview of the State Ministry of Development of Minor Crops including Sugarcane, Maize, Cashew, Pepper, Cinnamon, Cloves, Betel Related Industries and Export Promotion. Since the necessity of having a formal mechanism to implement the programmes and projects identified by the said State Ministry, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to reactivate the Spices and allied products Marketing Board and continue its activities, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Establishment of a New Refinery of 100,000 barrels per day (bblspd) at Sapugaskanda for the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10714",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- As the existing capacity of the refinery located at Sapugaskanda belonging to the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation is only 40,000 (bblspd), the Corporation refinery meets only 25 % of the local demand for refined petroleum products. The remaining 75% has to be imported, relying much on the foreign exchange. Although a feasibility study had been conducted in 2010 for the renovation and expansion of the refinery to increase that capacity up to 100,000 (bblspd), the subsequent technological changes that have taken place in that field have made it impossible to proceed on the results of the feasibility study.\n\nAccordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to take necessary action to initiate a new feasibility study by the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation to determine the scope, technical, operational and financial feasibility of the project which is to be implemented with a focus on several alternative proposals to enhance the existing refinery capacity of petroleum products, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Streamlining the Fertilizer Production and Distribution System in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10713",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Production, supply and application of fertilizer should be scientifically handled in order to ensure a sustainable soil quality to produce quality crops for a healthy food production process. Therefore, a proper Fertilizer Supply Chain Management System with appropriate technological procedures that do not lead to fertilizer wastage, scarcity and deviation from standards, should be followed. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture, to take necessary action to provide infrastructure facilities with scientific standards and components based on an automated centralized methodology upon instructions of the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka, including the completion of National Fertilizer Secretariat with modern technologies, upgrading existing laboratories and strengthening the district level operating and evaluation system including a field inspection mechanism to be established in collaboration with the Sri Lanka Institute of Nanotechnology, to its scope, was approved by the Cabinet ."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Obtaining used empty bullet Casings and disposed Armor Plates as raw materials for the industries of traditional artisans",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10712",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Attention has been drawn to solve the issues confronted by the traditional craft industries and rural industries in order to empower the industrialists who involved in those sectors, since such industries can have a huge impact on the economy of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, it has been planned to supply the manufactures the raw materials at a concessionary basis, enabling them to price such goods in order to compete with the imported goods in the market. For the purpose, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to obtain the empty bullet casings (Brass) and disposed armour plates used by the Sri Lanka Army, the Sri Lanka Air Force and the Sri Lanka Navy to the National Crafts Council, deviating from procurement procedure and subject to the pricing formula  approved by the Cabinet in the year 2017 and also to purchase copper, brass and aluminum etc disposed by the Sri Lanka Telecom, the Department of Sri Lanka Railways, the Ceylon Electricity Board and the National Water Supply and Drainage Board at a concessionary price to the National Crafts Council, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Obtaining discarded rails of the Department of Sri Lanka Railways for the construction of electric fences and protective fences to minimize the elephant-human conflict",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10711",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, Elephant - human conflicts are reported in 133 Divisional Secretariat Divisions in 19 Districts in Sri Lanka. Construction of protective fences and electric fences are the key measures from among the measures taken by the Department of Wild Life Conservation to control this situation. Approximately 4,500 km of electric fences have already been erected by now in the aforementioned 133 Divisional Secretariat Divisions while approximately 1,500 km of electric fences, and elephant retention centres with protective fences have been planned to be constructed. Although, timber posts are being used to construct these fences at present those are frequently subject to fall down by elephants. Using of concrete posts too is beyond practical approach due to difficulties found in renovating them.\n\nTherefore, it has been proposed to utilize discarded rails as an alternative solution for the purpose. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Conservation and the Minister of Transport to obtain the discarded rails by the Department of Sri Lanka Railways to the Department of Wild Life Conservation, on free of charge, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "National Programme for the Establishment of Export Production Villages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10710",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been designed to implement an Export Production Villages Programme enabling to develop rural products within a formal business model and connect them with the export supply chain as well as to upgrading local manufacturing industries to produce import substitutions. This programme aims to mobilize homogeneous producers scattered in a particular area as an Export Production Village Company and provide with them opportunity to produce their productions to the export market and also to address the issues having minimized the challenges to be faced by them. Further, it is expected to establish Export Production Villages covering the sectors of Agriculture, Fisheries, Industry and Services and to enter into future trade agreements with leading export companies thereby ensuring the sustainability of the said Export Production Villages. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade, to implement the said proposed programme by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board utilizing the necessary provisions, under the guidance of the Ministry of Trade, was approved in principle, by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-02-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-11-02",
    "description": "Performing teaching activities by means of television and radio services under the Distance education system",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10709",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the difficulties erupted for the continuation of teaching activities in the schools due to the COVID - 19 pandemic situation, approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to use both \u201cEye Channel\u201d and \u201cNethra Channel\u201d to perform teaching activities by means of television and radio services under the distance education system. With the re-emergence of COVID - 19 pandemic in the country, it has been perceived that optimal alternative distance educational methodologies are essential to be applied for the continuation of educational activities, since re-opening of schools as scheduled seems to be not practical at present. Therefore, it has been planned to prepare and telecast television educational programmes from grades 3 to 13 in all the three languages; Sinhala, Tamil and English. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education, to implement a series of Educational prorammes with the assistance of the State and private television and radio channels in collaboration with the National Institute of Education and the State Ministry of Education Reforms, Open Universities & Distance Learning Promotion, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Extending the grace period agreed on the payment of the salaries to the private sector employees in the wake of the crisis caused by the Covid-19 pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10708",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Task Force has been appointed representing Employers, Trade Unions, the National Labour Advisory Council, the Ministry of Labour and the Department of Labour has been appointed to look into the payment of salaries to the private sector employees in the wake of the crisis caused by the Covid-19 pandemic. The said Task Force has agreed to take action as follows from May to September, 2020.\n    \u2022 Retaining the jobs of employees of institutions which suspended operations due to the Covid 19 pandemic. \n    \u2022 to make arrangements to deploy employees on a roster basis or any other suitable method enabling them to serve proportionately where the institution that can't deploy all their workers in the duty due to the requirement of maintaining social distancing.\n\n    \u2022 to pay either 50% of the basic salary of the relevant month in which employee last received his full salary or Rs.14,500, whichever is more remunerative to the employee, in respect of employees of the institutions which had a requirement to retain their workers at home due to the absence of work. \n    \u2022 to pay contributions to the Employees\u2019 Provident Fund and the Employees Trust Fund by the employer for the salaries so paid.\n\nThe Cabinet noted that the matters submitted by the Minister of Labour to the effect that the said Task Force is in agreement to take action as mentioned above up to December of this year as the spread of Covid-19 pandemic further continuing in the country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Procurement for the supply of 2,000,000 Vials of Biphasic Isophane Insulin Injection BP, 30/70, 1000 IU/10 ml",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10707",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- International competitive bids were invited for the procurement of Biphasic Isophane Insulin Injection which is used to treat for the diabetic patients. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to award the procurement for the supply of 2,000,000 vials of Biphasic Isophane Insulin Injection BP, 30/70, 1000 IU/10 ml to M/s Wokhardt Limited at a total C&F price of US$ 3 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Awarding the Contract for construction of the Faculty Building Complex (Phase I) for the Faculty of Agricultural Sciences of the Sabaragamuwa University, Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10706",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- National competitive bidding procedure has been followed for the construction of the Faculty Building Complex (Phase 1) for the Faculty of Agricultural Sciences of the Sabaragamuwa University, Sri Lanka. Accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Education, to award the said contract to Sathuta Builders Pvt. Ltd, Kurunegala to a sum of Rs.797.81 million (without VAT) as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Construction of houses for 14 selected devotees affected by the Easter Sunday attack at St. Sebastian's Church, Katuwapitiya, Negombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10705",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approval was granted on 2019\u201109\u201117 to implement a housing project for the families affected by the bomb explosion that took place at St. Sebastian's Church, Katuwapitiya, Negombo on 2020\u201109\u201121. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to award the contract for the construction houses for 14 selected families at a cost of Rs. 3.24 million per each under the above programme to the State Engineering Corporation of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Revision of the \u201cSwashakthi Loan Scheme\u201d to provide loan facilities towards developing Small and Medium Scale Business Sector and generating employments",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10704",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the year 2017, the \u201cSwasakthi Loan Scheme\u201d has been launched jointly by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and the Small Business Development Division of the Ministry vested with the subject of Youth Affairs with an investment of Rs. 3500 million. Said loan scheme has been implemented through commercial banks and it provides loans to start a business based on a successful project plan. At present, under the said loan scheme, 13890 entrepreneurs have been provided with Rs. 3064 million. Accordingly, taking into consideration the nature of the project and the compliance with the current needs, the proposal made by the Minister of Youth and Sports, to provide loans to young entrepreneurs within the age of 18 and 40, subject to a maximum of one million rupees, for the implementation of new small and medium scale projects in the following business sectors, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tIT and computer related projects. \n*\tAgricultural, dairy and animal husbandry projects. \n*\tProjects related to tourism promotion. \n*\t Projects related to innovations and innovative machinery and plants. \n*\t Food processing products and related projects."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Handing over Raigam Korale Tea Shakthi Tea Factory to Raigam Tea Small \tHoldings Development Society",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10703",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the cease of the tea production activities of the Raigam Korale  Shakthi Tea Factory from April 2019 by the the Dikhena Tea Small Holder Development Society which had taken over the said tea factory on lease basis, tea smallholders who supplied their production to the said factory are faced with severe difficulties. Approximately Rs. 42 million had to be paid to the tea smallholders who supplied tea to the said factory, broker companies and other external parties by the the Dikhena Tea Small Holder Development Society. Taking into account the request made by the tea smallholders to restart the activities of the said factory, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to hand over the said factory on lease basis to Raigam Tea Small Holdings Development Society, which has the financial strength and 1,800 members to carry out production activities of the Factory, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Proposed dedicated zone for textile manufacturing and related industries at Punnaikudah of Eravur-Pattu Divisional Secretariat Division in Batticaloa District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10702",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The establishment of an apparel industrial Zone in Eravur by the Board of Investment in collaboration with the Land Reforms Commission has been identified as a significant priority project of the Ministry of Industries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to declare the apparel industrial zone proposed to be established at Punnaikudah of Eravur-Pattu Divisional Secretariat Division in Batticaloa District as a strategic Development Project as a 'Dedicated Zone for Textile Manufacturing and Related Industries', to vest 275 acres of land identified for the purpose and belonging to the Land Reforms Commission with the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka, to secure provisions required for the said project and to provide investment incentives for the investors those who are investing in that industrial zone, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Signing a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Government of the Republic of India for obtaining Indian Grant Assistance to implement the High Impact Community Development Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10698",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India has extended their grant financing assistance to Sri Lanka since 2005 to implement small scale development projects in view of strengthening the bilateral relationship and development partnership between two countries. Under this grant financing programme, a large number of projects pertaining to the development of infrastructure in the fields such as education, health and community development have been implemented through the Government institutions, Local Authorities and Non Government Organizations. Under the same, the Government of India is in an agreement to provide financial assistance to Sri Lanka in order to implement high impact community development projects for a period of five years from 2020 to 2025. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to enter into a new MoU for the purpose with the Government of India, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Development of Wind Farm Projects in Mannar Island",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10697",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Construction work of 100 MW Wind Power Plant in Mannar Island is now underway with an investment of US$ 200 million of the Asian Development Bank (ADB). The physical progress of the project is 73% and the construction is expected to be completed by early 2021. Of the US$ 200 million obtained for the project, a balance of US$ 47 million remains and it has been found that another 06 wind turbines could be installed using the said balance thereby increasing the power generation capacity of the said Plant by 20 MW. The Asian Development Bank has granted approval in principle for the capacity enhancing proposal and accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Power to take action accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Introduction of a mechanism to utilize non-forest lands among the residual lands except conservation and reserved forests which are vested with the Conservator General of Forests for productive economic purposes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10696",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- A decision had been taken in 2006, to transfer the powers vested with the Divisional Secretaries to authorize the use of the remaining non-forest lands of residual lands for activities such as chena cultivation, other farming and temporary economic activities to an Inter-Ministerial Committee. At its meeting held on 2020\u201107\u201101, Cabinet decided that it would be appropriate to introduce a simplified mechanism of granting permission to engage in such economic activities to minimize the hardships faced by those temporarily engaged in chena farming and other economic activities in such lands. Accordingly, having studied the issues, the officers of the Ministry of Wildlife and Forest Conservation, Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Lands have formulated a new mechanism. As such, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Conservation, the Minister of Environment and the Minister of Lands to implement the said mechanism, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Establishment of Sri Lankan Embassies in Romania and Spain",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10695",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Diplomatic relations between Romania and Sri Lanka commenced in the year 1957 and so far, very good bilateral relations have been established between the two countries. Further, Diplomatic relations between Spain and Sri Lanka commenced in 1955. Accordingly the proposal made by the Foreign Minister to establish Sri Lankan Embassies in the said two countries with a view to further developing the existing relations with those countries with Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Modernizing the process of conducting Examinations in the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10694",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka conducts mainly 4 National Examinations related to school education and about 325 Institutional Examinations annually. The departmental staff carries out most of the work related to conducting those examinations following the usual office procedures and the necessity of digitalizing the examination process has been identified to maintain the accuracy and reliability of the examinations. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to purchase new technical equipment including internet facilities required to modernize the examination management process of the Department of Examinations, to train the respective staff to utilize the said devices and to establish Examination Evaluation Centres at provincial level to facilitate the exam evaluation process, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Re-allocating the Regidale Watte land at Kahapola, Piliyandala to the National Zoological Department",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10693",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval in the year 2016 to acquire the Regidale Watte land at Kahapola, Piliyandala which was under the National Zoological Department to the then Ministry in charge of the subject of Buddhashasana and vest the same with the institution called \u201cLight of Asia Foundation\u201d under a Memorandum of Understanding for its project for the Erection of the Theme Park of Sakya Kingdom of Kapilawasthu in India. The said project had been scheduled to commence in the year 2017 and complete in March 2020, however its progress is still less than 5%. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhashasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to cancel the Agreement entered into with the \u201cLight of Asia Foundation\u201d and acquire the said land back to the Ministry of Buddhashasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to re-transfer the said land to the National Zoological Department, retaining 5 acres of the land under the Ministry for its future development activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Obtaining Additional Financial assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) for the Small and Medium Sized Enterprises Line of Credit Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10692",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Development Bank has given its consent to grant a loan amounting to US$ 165 million including an Emergency Response Component of US$ 100 miilion for the measures to be taken to provide solutions to mitigate the circumstances erupted and the negative impact confronted by the Small and Medium Scale Entrepreneurs due to the COVID -19 pandemic. In addition to the above loan, it has also been agreed to award a grant of US$ 1.25 million under the Japan Fund for Poverty Reduction. \nFurther, it has been agreed to grant a concessionary loan amount of US$ 400 million for the Secondary Education Sector Improvement Project under the Results Based Lending financial modality of the Asian Development Bank.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to enter into the respective agreements with the Asian Development Bank to obtain the said loan amounts and the grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Capacity Expansion Project of the Colombo International Container Terminal",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10691",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Project for the development of the South Container Terminal of Colombo Port was implemented under an investment of US$ 500 million and its construction was completed on 2016\u201112\u201101 and is in commercial operation at present. An Agreement has been entered into by the Colombo International Container Terminal Limited with the Sri Lanka Board of Investment to implement the aforesaid Project. Taking into account the present demand for the activities of the said Terminal and the prospective business opportunities, it has been decided to expand the said project enhancing the capacity of the Terminal without commencing new constructions. \n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to introduce new equipment to upgrade and moderate the existing equipment investing US$ 90 million, and thereby implement the productivity enhancing project of the Terminal and to publish the relevant tax relief in accordance with the provisions of the Strategic Development Projects Act in the Government Gazette, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
