    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation to introduce a new Act, in place of the existing Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka Act No.36 of 1987, incorporating the provisions required to regulate the stock market of Sri Lanka in keeping with current international best practices, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-26-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-10-26",
    "description": "Appointment of a Delimitation Committee to establish new Divisional Secretariat Divisions, to gazette the already established Divisional Secretariat Divisions and to establish and reconstitute of Grama Niladhari Divisions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10688",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Based on the administration and development requirements of the Government as well as the requirements of the public, many requests have been made by people's representatives as well as people's organizations for the establishment of new divisional secretariat divisions in certain areas of the country, reconstitution of some divisional secretariat divisions, delimitation and then gazette the already established divisions yet to be gazetted, establishment of new Grama Niladhari divisions and reconstitute of the existing Grama Niladhari divisions. Although, a Delimitation Committee has to be appointed for the purpose, every 05 years, the report of the last committee appointed in the year 2012, has not been published in the Government Gazette and accepted officially due to the technical deficiencies in the Report. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of Internal Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management, to appoint a new Delimitation Committee for the purpose of carrying out the relevant functions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-19-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-10-19",
    "description": "Amendments to the Twentieth Amendment to the Constitution to be \tmoved at the Committee Stage in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10687",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-19",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020\u201109\u2011 02 has granted approval to publish the draft Bill on the Twentieth Amendment to the Constitution in the Government Gazette and to submit the same thereafter in Parliament for approval. Accordingly, taking into consideration the determination of the Supreme Court on the said draft Bill, the amendments to be moved at the Committee Stage of the said Bill in Parliament were submitted to the Cabinet by the Minister of Justice and the Cabinet granted approval for the same proposals. \n\nFurther, it was decided at this Cabinet meeting that the provisions relating to following matters too should be moved at the Committee Stage of the Bill of the Twentieth Amendment to the Constitution.\n\n    \u2022 Provisions to increase of number of the Supreme Court Judges and the Court of Appeal Judges , taking into account the large number of cases pending in such courts.\n\n    \u2022 Provisions to submit only the Bills relating to matters arising in connection with the national security and disaster situations in Parliament, treating those as Urgent Bills.\n      \n    \u2022 Provisions for authorizing the Auditor General to audit the accounts of a Public Corporation or a Company in which the Government or a Public Corporation holds 50% or more of the shares.\n\n    \u2022 Incorporate provisions relating to the number of Ministers of the Cabinet of Ministers, Ministers who are not members of the Cabinet of Ministers and Deputy Ministers as provided in the Nineteenth Amendment to the Constitution in the Twentieth Amendment to the Constitution without change."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-19-013-en",
