    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Obtaining Financial Assistance from the Asian Development Bank for Improving the Quality of Secondary Education in Government Schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10647",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2020\u201104\u201101 to obtain a loan amounting to US $ 400 million from the Asian Development Bank in order to implement Result Based programmes for the Education Sector.\n\n\tAccordingly, plans have been drawn to invest the said amount of money under the following sectors:\n\t\n* \tExtensive reform in the secondary education curriculum and in assessment   methodologies.\n  \n* \tDeveloping a secondary school network fully equipped with facilities at  Divisional Secretariat Division level and thereby ensuring the access to high quality secondary education opportunities for all children.\n\n* \tIncreasing the number of National Schools up to 1000.\n\n* \tUpgrading the National Colleges of Education to the degree awarding status.\n\n* \tEnsuring the teacher balancing and teacher employment and thereby increasing the student achievement level.\n\n\tTherefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to  implement the above mentioned investment programme of US $ 400 million during the  period from 2020 - 2025 through the relevant  institutions connected to the Education Sector for the purpose of implementing of the Educational reforms adhering to the National Policy Statement 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Amendments to the Workmen's Compensation Ordinance No.19 of 1934 \t(Chapter 139)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10646",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-In the policy statement of \u201cVistas of Prosperity and Splendour\u201d under the heading of \u201ca Culture of Working for the Country\u201d, it has been stated that action would be taken to amend the Workmen's Compensation Ordinance No.19 of 1934 and  increase the compensation payment entitled to the employees in the event of a sudden accident. \n\n\tAccordingly, a draft Bill has been prepared by the Legal Draftsman to amend \tthe relevant provisions of the Workmen's Compensation Ordinance in order \tto increase the compensation to be paid to the employees injured due to a \tsudden  accident and it has been observed that the said draft has to be to further \tamended in view of the following reasons. \n\n    \u2022 to increase the fine of Rs 1000 that could be imposed in terms of the existing provisions in a situation where employers fail to submit the statement of compensation to the Commissioner for Worksmen's Compensation in respect of an accident caused to an employee under section 42 of the  the Workmen's Compensation Ordinance.\n      \n    \u2022 to amend the  Schedule IV of the  the Workmen's Compensation Ordinance which indicates the amount of compensations as follows to suit the current situation:\n      \n          i \tto increase the minimum monthly wage applicable for the \tpayment of compensation from Rs. 0 to Rs 10,000/- which \tprevails from Rs. 0 to 2,500/- at present.\n\n          ii\tto revise the maximum monthly wage applicable for the \tpayment of compensation from Rs. 100, 000/- upwards which \tprevails from Rs. 20,001/- upwards at present. \n          \n          iii\tto increase the amount of compensation paid in the event \tof death (on the basis of the wage) from Rs. 1,140,000/- \tto 2,000,000/- which prevails from Rs. 181,665/- to 550,000/- \tat present.\n          \n          iv\tto increase the amount of compensation paid in a permanent \ttotal \tdisablement (on the basis of the wage) from \tRs.1,200,000 to Rs. 2,000,000/- which \tprevails from \tRs.196,083.80 to Rs. 550,000/- at present.\n          \n          v\tto increase the amount of compensation paid in a temporary \tdisablement \t(on the basis of half-monthly wage) from Rs. \t5,000 to  Rs. 47,500/- which prevails from Rs. 1,320 to Rs. \t5,500/- at present.\n          \n    \u2022 to fulfill the task of  recovering the compensation to confiscate the property through the Fiscal/Registrar attached to the Office of the Commissioner for Workmen's Compensation, in order to expedite the process of recovery of compensation.\n      \n    \u2022 to introduce a new insurance scheme for workmen's compensation. \n\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour to further amend the \tdraft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman so as to incorporate the above \tamendments as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Promulgation of Regulations on maintaining 'Special Deposit Accounts' under the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10645",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2020\u201104\u201108 to make Regulations under the  Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017 to open and maintain current deposits in the name of 'Special Deposit Accounts' to deposit the foreign currency remitted to the country through  the banking system for a period of 06 months with the view to encouraging the influx of foreign exchange  into the country. Accordingly, the validity period of the Regulations due to expire on 2020\u201110\u201107 and as such, the Monetary Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka has made following recommendations so as to further retain the foreign exchange remitted to the Sri Lanka -\n\n* \tPayment of interest  rates on normal term deposits for the 'Special Deposit Accounts'  renewed and maintained after maturity.\n\t\n* \tGranting permission to transfer the income on maturity of the 'Special Deposit Accounts' to the other accounts in Sri Lanka.\n\n* \tto credit the income of 'Special Deposit Accounts' of resident individuals but who are not eligible to open Foreign Currency Account (Non Government Organizations, Guarantee Companies etc.) on maturity, to a LKR account, subject to the condition that such income shall not be remitted outside Sri Lanka in the future.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by  the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to promulgate  new Regulations in terms of section 7 of the Foreign Exchange Act to be read  with the section 29 therein, in addition to the Regulations published in the Gazette (Extraordinary) Notification No. 2170/4 dated 2020\u201104\u201108 and No. 2182/32 dated 2020\u201107\u201101 with regard to the Special Deposit Accounts and to present the said Regulations in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Ban on Cattle Slaughter in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10644",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-As a country with an economy based on agriculture, the contribution of the cattle to develop the livelihood of the rural people of Sri Lanka is immense. Various parties have pointed out that the cattle required for traditional farming purposes is insufficient due to the rise of cattle slaughter and that the lack of sufficient cattle for the improvement of the local dairy industry enabling to enhance the livelihood of the rural community while reducing the large amount of foreign exchange outflow on imported milk powder has become an obstacle for the development of that industry. Accordingly, taking into account this situation, the Cabinet granted approval to implement the following proposals submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister.\n\n\n\n\n*\tTo take necessary action, without delay, to amend the existing Animals Act No.29 of 1958, the Butchers Ordinance No.09 of 1893 and other relevant consequential laws and rules and regulations passed by the Local Authorities which are being implemented in the country at present pertaining to cattle slaughter. \n\t\n*\tTo take necessary action to import beef required for the people who consume beef and provide same at a concessionary price without delay. \n\n*\tTo implement a suitable programme regarding the aging cattle, which cannot be used for agricultural purposes effectively.\n\n*\tTo ban the cattle slaughter in the country with immediate effect, subject to taking aforesaid steps."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "The Light Rail Transit System Project (LRT) proposed to be implemented \tin the Western region of Sri Lanka under the financial assistance of the \tJapan International Cooperation Agency (JICA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10643",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Cabinet approval has been granted to implement the Light Rail Transit System Project within the Western region of Sri Lanka under the financial assistance of JICA. However, it has been observed that it would not be able to achieve the expected outcome of that project due to the following reasons. \n\n\n\n*\tAccording to the initial plan of the project, it had been proposed to introduce a Light Rail Service with facilities to travel along the overland railway tracks as an alternative mode of transport for persons who come to the city of Colombo for employment and other requirements by using their private motor vehicles. \n\n*\tHowever, the previous Government, changing the aforesaid plan, had taken the necessary basic measures to implement the proposed Light Rail Transit System on a railway track built on pillars that may cause huge environmental damage.\n\n*\tIt has been found that if the project is implemented, a large number of buildings including houses and business premises will have to be demolished and a very high cost will have to be incurred for constructing the railway track on pillars.\n\n*\tIt has been observed that it would not be possible to provide the required facilities through this train expected to be implemented under the proposed Light Rail Transit System as an alternative mode of transport to attract persons, coming to the city of Colombo for employment and other purposes by using their private motor vehicles.\n\n*\tFurther, it has also been found that if the proposed Light Rail Transit System Project is implemented, a heavy operational cost will have to be incurred for the same. \n\n\tAccordingly, taking into consideration the matters submitted by the Minister of Transport as the Minister in charge of the subject of implementing this Project at present, the Cabinet decided to cancel the Light Rail Transit System Project planned to be implemented in the Western region."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Awarding the long term contracts to import diesel for a period of 8 months",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10642",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-The proposal made by the Minister of Energy to award the following long term procurement to import diesel for a period of eight months from 2020\u201110\u201115 to 2021\u201106\u201114 as recommended by the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tTo award the procurement of 1,365,000 Bbls of Gas Oil with maximum sulphur percentage of 0.05 and 315,000 Bbls of Gas Oil with maximum sulphur percentage of 0.001 to M/s Emirates National Oil Company, Singapore (ENOC).\n\n*\tTo award the procurement of 1,120,000 Bbls of Gas Oil with maximum sulphur percentage of 0.05 to M/s Emirates National Oil Company, Singapore (ENOC)."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Procurement for constructing the North Central Main Canal and North \tWestern Main Canal under the Mahaweli Water Security Investment \tProgramme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10641",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "The Asian Development Bank has agreed to grant US$ 675 million for the Construction work of Phase 1 and the Feasibility Study of Phase 2 of the Mahaweli Water Security Investment Programme. 17 contract packages are due to be awarded under the Phase I of the project and out of which 10 contracts have already been awarded. As such, the following proposals made by the Minister of Irrigation pertaining to the procurement for constructing the North Central Main Canal and North Western Main Canal under this program, was approved by the Cabinet. \t\n\n*\tTo take action to award the contract for the construction of the Mahakithula Inlet Tunnel, Mahakithula and Mahakirula Reservoirs and feeder Canal from Mahakithula reservoir to Mahakirula reservoir to China CAMC Engineering Co. Ltd. which has already submitted bids for the same, on the prices agreed upon through negotiations.\n\n*\tTo take action to award the Contract for the construction of 28km long tunnel section through the Minneriya, Giritale, Hurulu Conservation Forests and Sanctuaries of 95.66 km long North Central Maha Ela Construction Project to be constructed to supply drinking water to the North Central Province and the Vavuniya District in the Nothern Province to China State Construction Engineering Corporation Ltd. which has submitted bids for the same, on the prices agreed upon through negotiations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Provision of School Uniform Material Programme - 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10640",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020\u201106\u201110 granted approval to provide school uniform materials through domestic textile manufacturers in place of giving vouchers for school uniforms. Accordingly, relevant procurement process has been initiated and only four domestic textile manufacturers have submitted bids. During the field visits, it has been observed that they have already manufactured approximately 40% of the total textile requirement and it has been confirmed that these manufactures have the capacity to meet the \ttotal school uniform material requirement by the end of January, 2021. Taking into account the matters submitted by the Minister of Education on providing school uniform materials, the Cabinet granted approval to take necessary action to purchase the total requirement of school uniform material from domestic manufactures and accordingly to provide the school children with uniform materials instead of vouchers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Establishment of a Special Unit under the Ministry of Justice to strengthen \tthe process of Administration of Justice",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10639",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-It is manifestly clear that delays in the legal system in Sri Lanka creates a major \timpact on the people involved in litigation and the country's economy. In the \tyear 2016, the National Law Conference Committee complied a report on the \tvarious issues causing delays in litigation, the adverse consequences of these \tissues, and the proposed solutions for the same. By the end of 2019, there were 766,784 pending court cases in all courts of the country and expeditious solutions need to be considered to address the situation.\n\n\tIt has been identified that necessary action should be taken in the areas such as development of infrastructure, reform of the law, digitization of courts and capacity building. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, the Cabinet granted approval to establish a Special Unit under the Ministry of Justice to implement a Law Reforms Programme within a period of 3 years with the contribution of the Legal Experts in the field of Law."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Amendment to the Code of Criminal Procedure Act No. 15 of 1979",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10638",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-An Amendment to the Code of Criminal Procedure Act No.15 of 1979 had been presented to Parliament to authorize the Magistrate to dispense with the requirement of producing suspects or accused persons in person before the Magistrate for extending orders relating to committal to remand custody, in view of avoiding the repetition of unfortunate and violent incidents that occurred recently while transporting prisoners to the courts, However, approval could not be granted to the same due to the Prorogation of Parliament.\n\n \tAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to further amend the Code of Criminal Procedure Act No. 15 of 1979 and to instruct the legal draftsman to prepare amending legislation accordingly, enabling to facilitate the accused and suspected persons to appear before courts by using contemporaneous audio visual links and to provide such facilities for the accused and suspected persons being rehabilitated under a judicial order in a different case, taking also into account the new trends that have arisen under the Covid-19 pandemic, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Draft legislation for the prohibition of Anti-Personnel Mines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10637",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-On 2017\u201112\u201113, Sri Lanka acceded to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use, Stockpiling, Production and Transfer of Anti-Personnel Mines and on their Destruction. In terms of the provisions of the Article 9 of the said Convention, Sri Lanka should draft legislation to implement the provisions of the said convention incorporating appropriate legal, administrative and other measures including the imposition of penal sanctions to prevent and suppress of any such act. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to finalize the drafting process incorporating the observations by the Attorney General with regard to the draft that has been already prepared by the Legal Draftsman, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Pilot project for distributing eco-friendly fertilizer as subsidized fertilizer for the Maha season 2020/2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10636",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2020\u201102\u201120 to allocate Rs 250 million for the implementation of a pilot project for providing organic fertilizer subsidy from the Yala season 2020, under the Chemical Fertilizer Subsidy Programme. Accordingly, paddy has been cultivated around 25,000 hectares in 14 Districts using compost manure, organic liquid fertilizer and bio fertilizer. This has reduced the use of chemical fertilizers by 30% - 50%. Taking into consideration the success achieved by implementation of the pilot project, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to cultivate 48,000 hectares of paddy using eco-friendly fertilizer during the Maha season 2020/2021 was, approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Printing activities of Government and Semi-Government Establishments to be undertaken by the Department of Government Printing",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10635",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-As the Official Printer of the Government, the Department of Government Printing has the potential of carrying out a significant portion of the printing requirements of Government and Semi-Government institutions. However, it has been found, that these institutions pay a large sum of money annually to local and foreign private companies for their printing works. Taking into consideration the above, according to the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media the Cabinet decided that all Government and Semi-Government Institutions which do not have printing institutions under their Ministries should take steps to get their printing work which is not exceeding 25% of the value of printing requirements, done through the Department of Government Printing."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Working Capital requirement for the maintenance of the Buffer Stock of rice for the period from October 2020 to January 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10634",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-Since rice production takes place in the country from October to January every year, the rice requirement during the said period is accomplished through the buffer stock of rice maintained from the rice produced during the other months. Accordingly, it has been estimated that a sum of Rs 2,241 million will be required to maintain the buffer stock of rice which is approximately 3% of the rice requirement for the period of four (04) months from October 2020 to January 2021, i.e. 25,000 metric tons including the cost of storage. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade for the issuance of a Letter of Comfort by the General Treasury enabling to obtain a working capital loan for a period of four (04) months from the People\u2019s Bank to Lanka Sathosa so that the said activity can be carried out by the Lanka Sathosa, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding between the University of Peradeniya and the Department of Animal Production and Health (Joint Venture) with the Royal Veterinary College, UK for the implementation of the One Health Poultry Hub Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10633",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-The University of Peradeniya and the Department of Animal Production and Health (Joint Venture) with the Royal Veterinary College of the United Kingdom have planned to implement a research project known as One Health Poultry Hub with the financial contribution of the Global Challenges Research Fund of the United Kingdom. \n\n\n\nThis research project is expected to improve the production of poultry and eggs, to identify the issues that emerge when expanding the local poultry industry to the export sector and direct the production process to the correct pathway through technological and human resource development. The Global Challenges Research Fund of the United Kingdom has agreed to provide 700,000 Sterling Pounds for this project for a period of 05 years. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education for entering into the Memorandum of Understanding relating to the said research project between the said parties,was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Completion work of the project for urgent improvements in the water treatment plant of the Kirindi Oya Water Supply Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10632",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Project for urgent improvement in the old water treatment plant of the Kirindi Oya Water Supply Scheme had been entrusted in the year 2019 with the State Engineering Corporation by the then subject Ministry of Housing. However, this project has not yet been completed to date and its present overall progress is 40%. For the construction work, the present capacity of the old treatment plant has been reduced by 50% and consequently the community in the area is confronted with extreme difficulties due to the inability to obtain sufficient water. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing, to entrust the responsibility of implementing the Project to the National Water Supply and Drainage Board with the intention of completing the project expeditiously and to provide the allocation for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Renovation and conservation of the Deegawapi Stupa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10631",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "-H.E the President has established a Presidential Task Force for the Management of Archaeological Heritages in the Eastern Province and the said Task Force has planned to establish a fund for the immediate renovation and conservation of the Deegawapi Stupa which is considered as the main Stupa in the Province. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President to establish a Trust Fund to raise funds to fulfill the requirements relating to the renovation and conservation activities of the Deegawapi Stupa and to carry out these renovation and conservation activities through a Sub\u2011Committee appointed representing both the State and the Private Sector under the Chairmanship of the Secretary, Ministry of Defence, Major General (Rtd) Kamal Gunaratne and Supportive Committees under the supervision of the Presidential Task Force, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-28-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-09-28",
    "description": "Taking further measures regarding the families in the houses reported to be prone to high risk due to a geographical instability in the district of Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10630",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Walls of 223 houses in 06 Grama Niladhari divisions of the Hingurakgoda Divisional Secretariat Division in the Polonnaruwa district have been unusually cracked due to a geographical instability in the interior of the earth causing the danger of the collapse of those houses. Out of the said houses 67 houses identified to have been severely damaged and uninhabitable, should be evacuated with immediate effect, and resettled in a suitable place. \n\n\nApproval of the Cabinet has been granted previously at its meeting held on 2017\u201106\u201127 for a methodology for the construction of permanent houses for families residing within high risk zones of earth slips and, accordingly taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of Internal Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management regarding the necessary measures to be taken on the said affected families, the Cabinet approved to take the following measures -\n\n\n* \tEvacuation of families from the houses identified as high risk and settle them temporarily in another secure place.\n\n\n* \tProvision of a rental allowance subject to a maximum of Rs.10,000.00 per month for a period of 06 months for each family so settled.\n\n\n* \tImplementation of an accelerated housing scheme with required infrastructure facilities by the Ministry of Urban Development and Housing and provide houses from the said Housing Scheme to the families to be evacuated.\n\n\n*\tIf the proposed housing scheme cannot be implemented within a short period of time, provide the following relief granted under the resettlement programme for the families who were evacuated due to high risk of landslides in terms of the Cabinet decision dated 2017\u201106\u201127 to the families to be evacuated from their places of living due to disaster situation in the Hingurakgoda Divisional Secretariat Division. \n\n\ni \tGranting Rs.1.6 million to purchase a land with a house.\n\n\nii\tGranting Rs.0.4 million to purchase a land and Rs.1.2 million to build a house .\n\n\niii\tIf a land has been granted by the State, granting Rs.1.2 million to build a house on such land."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "Proposal for the Central Bank of Sri Lanka to offer USD/LKR Buy-Sell \tCurrency Swaps for tenors between one to two years",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10629",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Central Bank of Sri Lanka has identified the need to facilitate the non\u2011resident \tinvestors to invest in Governments Securities and in other sectors with a view to encouraging foreign exchange inflows to the Country. Accordingly, the Monetary Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka has permitted to introduce the facility to offer USD/LKR Buy-Sell Currency Swaps for tenors between one to two years. As such, the arrangements submitted by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to pursue action as follows with the objective of hedging the foreign exchange risk that may occur to the Licensed Commercial Banks accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tTo carry out the near and the far legs of the swap under the same exchange rate. \n\n*\tTo permit premature unwinding of swaps at the prevalent exchange rate with a penalty.\n\n*\tThis facility is applicable only if there is foreign exchange inflows into the country and subject to a minimum of US$ 25 million and a maximum of US$ 1000 million.\n\n*\tIn the event the US$/ LKR exchange rate depreciates during the implementation of this programme, the loss that may cause to the Central Bank of Sri Lanka will be set off in future when transferring its dividends to the General Treasury enabling to treat the loss to the Central Bank as a cost to the General Treasury."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "Design, Construction and Financing the balance work of the Housing Project at Elliot Place, Borella",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10628",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The housing project consisting of 400 housing units at Elliot Place, Borella is being implemented by the Urban Development Authority for the middle income earners in the Government and private sector. However, since the said project did not proceed as planned due to financial problems in the company that was awarded the contract for the design, construction and financing of the project, the contract was terminated. This project has been identified as a priority project and, National competitive bids have been called to complete the balance work of the said project. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to award the said housing construction contract to M/s Access Engineering PLC, for a sum of Rs 9.37 billion (without tax), as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "Amending the Sri Lanka Disaster Management Act No.13 of 2005",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10627",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Based on the recommendations and proposals of the disaster management professionals and also the experiences gained from the disasters that took place in the past, the Legal Draftsman is currently working on the preparation of a draft Bill to amend the Sri Lanka Disaster Management Act No.13 of 2005 as per the Cabinet approval given on 2016\u201109\u201113 so as to suit to the present day requirement. In the meantime, since, it has been observed that people evicted from their places of residence due to the damages caused to houses and high risk of landslides, resettle in the same locations again, the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2019\u201102\u201126 had decided that action has to be also taken to prevent this situation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of Internal Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management to instruct the Legal Draftsman to amend the Sri Lanka Disaster Management Act, No. 13 of 2005 incorporating the said provisions in the draft amendment Bill currently being prepared, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "Prohibition of Obscene Publications Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10626",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Publication of obscene publications produced through information technology and other means using children has increased rapidly during the recent past. Although provisions are contained in the Penal Code and the Obscene Publications Ordinance to take action relating to the said matters, it has been found that those provisions are inadequate to deal with the current circumstances. Therefore, as a remedial measure, a document has been prepared by the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka (ICTA) and the Sri Lanka Computer Emergency Readiness Team (CERT), on the advice of the Attorney General incorporating the information required to draft a new Bill, and accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a new bill based on the said document, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "The Large Scale Water Supply and Sewerage Projects implemented by \tthe National Water Supply and Drainage Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10625",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply to treat the following large \tscale projects implemented by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board\tas special projects so as to exempt such projects from being charged taxes\tunder \tthe relevant tax laws and accordingly to provide facilities for such\tprojects, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tHemmathagama Water Supply Project\n\n*\tRuwanwella Water Supply Project\n\n*\tJaffna and Kilinochchi Water Supply Project\n\n*\tRathmalana/ Moratuwa Wastewater Disposal Project\n\n*\tKalu Gang Water Supply Expansion Project"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "Establishment of the Land Data Infrastructure and Land Information \tService System",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10624",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish the administration networks in the Sri Lanka Survey Department using new technology thereby expediting the survey process and increasing productivity with a view to rendering the services of the Department more efficiently. Accordingly, it has been found necessary to install the Land Information Service System with developed infrastructure facilities enabling the parties using land information to use the said information for their services. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Lands to implement the project for establishing the 'Land Data Infrastructure and Land Information Service System' according to the recommendations submitted by the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka (ICTA), with an investment\tof US$ 60.33 million under the Government Programme of Sri Lanka Korean EDCF Loan Funds, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "Meeting of the Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10623",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The first meeting of the Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living appointed by the Cabinet to provide policy and practical solutions to maintain the Cost of Living stable in the country was held under the Chairmanship of H.E the President on 2020-08-31. Accordingly, the decisions taken at the said Sub-Committee meeting pertaining to the following matters to ensure that essential goods including food items are available in the market without any scarcity and to monitor the stable maintenance of the Cost of Living were submitted to the Cabinet by the Minister of Trade and the Cabinet granted its concurrence for the same. \n\n* \tTo focus more attention on the most affected categories, when taking measures pertaining to the reduction of the Cost of Living.\n\n*\tTo maintain a stable local policy towards motivating the farmers to engage in cultivation and accordingly restrict the imports only to essential goods. \n\n*\tTo formulate a system to purchase the goods by the consumers at a reasonable price, providing suitable prices for the products of the farmers since the prices of goods would rise due to the pressure of the intermediaries.\n\n*\tTo establish a seed bank as a solution to the dearth of various high quality seeds that can be grown locally and for the preservation of local seeds which are progressively getting extinguished.\n\n*\tTo implement a mechanism for the distribution of products such as vegetables and fruits effectively to the consumers at an affordable price regulating the prices of the same. \n\n* \tTo design and implementation of a programme under the guidance of the Ministry of Plantation, Ministry of Agriculture and the Ministry of Trade to directly purchase the produced from the farmers and sell them in towns in populated areas accordingly.\n\n*\tTo suspend the import of additional crops which can be cultivated locally since there is a huge tendency of cultivating such crops by farmers, and give priority to promote the increase of production of local vegetables and to promote substitute crops for the crops to be imported.\n\n*\tTo ensure the availability of sufficient stocks of rice in the market at the guaranteed price by the Government, while maintaining safe stocks of rice without leaving space to escalate rice prices until the paddy harvest of the \tMaha season reaches the market.\n\n*\tDue to the complete suspension of the importation of the required materials specially maize required for producing chicken feed, the price of maize has gone up resulting in the increase of the prices of chicken and eggs. Therefore, it has been permitted temporarily to import wheat to be used as a substitute for maize on import permits for the purpose of controlling the escalation of the prices of chicken and eggs. As such, a suitable programme will have to be expeditiously implemented by the responsible Institutions for providing the required lands, seeds, fertilizer and required technology to expand the maize cultivation in the country.\n\n*\tThe Ceylon Fisheries Corporation to take measures to increase the market stalls and to expeditiously open the 40 stalls designed to be opened enabling the consumers to purchase fish at a reasonable price.\n\n*\tExpeditious action to be taken to increase the milk production and for such purpose, implement an arrangement to provide the milk farmers with required facilities and technical knowledge.\n\n*\tSince there is a tendency of a price increase of coconuts in the market, to implement a programme to sell coconuts in the populated towns by the Ministry of Plantation, enabling the consumers to\tpurchase them at a reasonable price."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-21-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-09-21",
    "description": "Census of Population and Housing - 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10622",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Census of Population and Housing of Sri Lanka is conducted once in every 10 years and the Department of Census and Statistics, as authorized by the Census Ordinance, has planned to conduct the next Census in the year 2021. This Census will provide qualitative and timely data and information at Grama Niladhari Division level on population, its geographical distribution, various demographic and social characteristics of the population and housing condition required for national policy formulation and planning. Since the planned activities of the Census of Population and Housing - 2021 have been affected due to the COVID - 19 pandemic which prevailed globally as well as locally, the proposal made by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to conduct the same as follows, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tto conduct the activities of listing stage of the Census from January to May, 2021 which had been scheduled to be commenced in July, 2020 \n\n*\tto conduct the enumeration stage from June to November, 2021\n\n*\tto carry out the data dissemination stage from November, 2021 to May, 2022\n\n*\tto conduct the post enumeration survey to establish the accuracy of census data collected at the enumeration stage, in the year 2022."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-16-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2020-09-16",
    "description": "Action taken during the 45th Session of the United Nations Human Rights Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10621",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Foreign Minister informed the Cabinet that the 45th Session of the United Nations Human Rights Council commenced on 2020\u201109\u201114 in Geneva, Switzerland and during the session the statements made  by the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights under the topic of \u201cGlobal Human Rights Update\u201d and by the United Kingdom on behalf of the Core Group of the Resolution 30/1 with reference to Sri Lanka and the response statement made clarifying the position of Sri Lanka on the allegations raised by the above  statements and the Cabinet took note the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-16-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-09-16",
    "description": "Preparation of Budget 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10620",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, presented the policy frame work to be followed in the  preparation of the Budget for the year 2021, giving priority to the following:\n\n* \tAllocation of resources to ensure the outcomes of the Government Policy document 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour' is achieved.\n\n*\tAllocation of resources to achieve the objectives stated in the Gazette Notification issued pertaining to the assignment of subjects and functions of the Cabinet Ministries and State Ministries.\n\n* \tProvision of safe drinking water to all, implementation of the programme for the rehabilitation and development of 100,000km roads covering the entire country, giving priority to aquatic resources and irrigation sectors.\n\n* \tAllocation of resources required for the Public Investment Programme creating an enabling environment for successful operation of business activities following the expenditure management methodologies under the prevailing circumstances since the State revenue for the 2021 is estimated to be approximately 10.2% of the Gross Domestic Production.\n\n* \tProviding  assistance for the digitalization of the Government processes.\n\n* \tFocus attention on the possibilities of adopting simple methodologies by \treviewing the existing methodologies enabling to yield better effective results utilizing fewer resources.\n\n\n\nAccordingly, the draft Appropriation Bill for the year 2021 is scheduled to be tabled in  Parliament during the second week of October 2020.\n\nThe proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to take necessary action to draft the Appropriation Bill of the year 2021 based on the policies mentioned above, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
